2026-07-25 11:09:31,600 1254555 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'docs/modules/browser-playwright-audit.md route inventory is missing /control entirely', 'description': 'Found 2026-07-25 while rehashing this spec after Control-page work (task custom-app-extension-point, unrelated task).\n\nThe spec\'s route inventory table (§Invariants > Route inventory) lists: /, /overview, /radar, /nodes, /messages, /config, /devices, /range, /performance, /node/!<hex>. It does NOT list /control at all, even though /control has been a real, shipped route since task pac-host-command-surface (earlier this same session). Worse, §Navigation state explicitly says: "An unknown or removed persisted activeTab, including control, falls back to overview" — the spec author treated \'control\' as a REMOVED/deprecated value, not a live route. This predates today\'s work; not something I introduced.\n\nIMPACT: the acceptance suite this spec describes (tests/test_playwright.py) would not know to navigate /control, assert its data surface, or check its now-existing sub-tabs (Summary/Command/Config/Stats/Yagi Align/Chat, task control-section-ia). If the suite is ever run against current code, Control is silently unaudited — not because it\'s excluded on purpose, but because the spec\'s inventory is stale.\n\nFIX: add a /control row to the route table, add a "Required data surfaces" entry for Control (pacHostStatus/pacHostQueues presence, sub-tab bar rendering, at minimum the Command sub-tab\'s unit picker), and correct the Navigation-state line so \'control\' is treated as a real persisted value, not a stale-state fallback case. Should be its own small /idiot task against this spec file — did not fix in-flight, out of scope of the task that found it.'}
