2026-07-25 13:12:08,575 1254555 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'Redesign toast notifications — bottom-right, multi-line wrap, proportional width, polished', 'description': 'Peter, 2026-07-25: "the toast that is used everwre is awful, it is 1 line appears at the top, overflows the viewport and is amateur. should popup bottom right and it needs to be polished and professional." Followed by: "needs to wrap to multi lines while still being a proportional size for the viewport."\n\nInvestigation: the "used everywhere" toast is app-ui.js\'s showToast() (this.toasts array) + drawer-sidebar.html\'s `<div class="toast toast-top toast-end ...">` DaisyUI container — 8 call sites (app-control.js, app-devices.js, app-messages.js, app-nodes.js, app-ws.js). Real defects found:\n1. `toast-top toast-end` + inline `top-16` — top-right, not bottom-right as requested.\n2. No `min-w-0` on the flex-1 text span inside a flex row — the same flex-shrink-refuses-below-content-width bug seen elsewhere in this codebase (drawer-sidebar.html favourites nav comment) — long messages can overflow rather than wrap.\n3. Fixed `max-w-xs` (20rem) regardless of viewport — not proportional on narrow/mobile widths.\n4. Class binding only distinguishes error vs everything-else-as-success: `t.type === \'error\' ? \'alert-error\' : \'alert-success\'` — a \'warning\' or \'info\' toast (both real, used in app-ws.js) currently renders GREEN (alert-success), which is wrong per STYLE_GUIDE §4\'s fixed status-color vocabulary.\n\nNote: there is a SECOND, separate toast implementation, op-toast.js (vanilla DOM, used only by op-flow.js device-write operations) — already bottom-right, already wraps correctly. Not touched by this task; the duplication is filed separately in the bugs backlog, out of scope here (this task fixes the one Peter is looking at, "used everywhere").\n\nFix (public/partials/drawer-sidebar.html, public/app.js if needed — expect no JS logic change, showToast() already passes `type` through untouched):\n- Container: `toast-bottom toast-end`, drop `top-16`; width `max-w-[min(24rem,calc(100vw-2rem))]` so it\'s proportional at any viewport, capped at 24rem on desktop.\n- Text span: add `min-w-0 break-words` so long/multi-line messages wrap inside the flex row instead of overflowing.\n- Class map: `{success:\'alert-success\', error:\'alert-error\', warning:\'alert-warning\', info:\'alert-info\'}[t.type] || \'alert-info\'` — fixes the warning/info-render-as-green bug per STYLE_GUIDE §4.\n- Icon glyph per type (✓/✕/⚠/ℹ), matching the existing op-toast.js precedent\'s icon-per-state pattern for a bit of visual polish and quick scannability without reading the color.\n- Entrance/exit motion: slide-up + fade (200ms in / 150ms out) reinforcing the new bottom anchor — restrained, not gimmicky, follows frontend-design skill guidance against decoration that doesn\'t serve the brief.\n- No inline `style=` — all Tailwind utility classes, per STYLE_GUIDE §7.\n\nVerify via Playwright, both themes, at a realistic desktop width AND a narrow mobile width (proportional-sizing claim needs proof at both), trigger a long multi-line message and confirm it wraps rather than overflowing, trigger all four types and confirm correct colors.'}
