2026-07-25 15:10:37,189 1254555 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "Yagi Align sub-tab — rebuild against mt-transport's live align backend", 'description': 'mt-transport shipped the align backend (commit b63c6de, xsession [align-backend]/[align-live-ish]) — Peter confirmed go-ahead ("so have you built the aligne frontend as I dont see it?"). Rebuilds the archived reference/alarm-integration/{src/align-api.js,public/app-align.js,align.html,align.css} feature into the Control > Yagi Align sub-tab (skeleton built earlier this session, task control-section-ia).\n\nArchitecture change from the archive: the old page was a standalone, framework-free /align route (deliberately no Alpine, to survive a CDN outage on a phone at the mast). That constraint no longer applies — Alpine is vendored locally in this dashboard already (public/vendor/alpinejs-3.15.12.min.js), not CDN-loaded, so building this as a normal Alpine mixin/sub-tab (consistent with the rest of Control) carries none of the original risk. Standalone /align route is retired, not preserved alongside.\n\nNew API (API.md "Antenna alignment" section, confirmed live):\n  POST /v1/mesh/align/ping   {target, n?}   opens/retargets session, fires one burst, 409 if a burst is already active\n  POST /v1/mesh/align/stop\n  GET  /v1/mesh/align                        complete view-model (polling fallback — used here, SSE not yet built, same deferral as the ledger)\n  POST /v1/mesh/align/config {replyWindowSec} 5-120, server-persisted\nModel pushed complete on `mesh.align` SSE, byte-identical field names to the OLD WebSocket model — mt-transport ported our own signalQuality() verbatim with unit tests matching our numbers.\n\nNo /align/targets endpoint anymore — the old backend built that from listFavourites(); reuse the ALREADY-pushed `this.favourites` root state directly (same {num,label} shape), no new backend route needed.\n\nTwo things flagged as ours alone (mt-transport cannot do them):\n1. PASV interlock — gate Yagi auto-rotation on the model\'s `running` field (we no longer force dashMode; the operator/existing rotator logic must respect running:true so it doesn\'t swing mid-burst).\n2. yagi_q/omni_q render as a gap when null, never 0 (no data from that antenna != terrible signal) — same class of trap as the ledger\'s sent-vs-done.\n\nScope:\n- src/pac-host.js: alignPing({target,n}), alignStop(), alignConfig({replyWindowSec}) — thin POST passthroughs, same pattern as queueCommand(). New _pollAlign() on its own cadence (2s — faster than the 5s queue poll since burst progress should feel live during a ~30s burst), pushing a new pac_host_align WS message type on change (mirrors queuesMessage()\'s change-detection pattern).\n- src/pac-align-api.js (new file): thin Express router, POST /align/ping, /align/stop, /align/config — mirrors pac-command-api.js exactly, zero mesh knowledge.\n- src/index.js: mount the new router.\n- src/ws-relay.js: replay pac_host_align on connect, rebroadcast on pacHost\'s new \'alignChanged\' event.\n- public/app-align.js (new file): Alpine mixin — alignModel state (root, pushed), alignNBurst/alignReplyWinSec (raw browser-originated inputs per the archive\'s own stated invariant — N and reply-window are the only browser-originated values), alignTarget, ping()/stop()/setReplyWindow() actions. Zero derived state — renders exactly what\'s pushed (quality/label/cls/trendDir/trendDelta/best/gapToBest/bestAgo/barPct all computed by mt-transport now).\n- public/app.js: merge alignMixin, declare align* root state.\n- public/app-ws.js: pac_host_align handler, pure assignment.\n- public/partials/tab-control.html: Yagi Align section becomes the real UI (target picker from `favourites`, N/reply-window controls, PING/End buttons, current-reading card, reading bars) — ported from align.html\'s structure, STYLE_GUIDE-compliant (no raw hex, no inline style beyond genuinely-computed bar heights).\n\nPASV interlock (responsibility 1 above) is a SEPARATE concern from rendering — likely lives in whatever currently drives auto-rotation (rotator/dash-mode logic), not this sub-tab\'s rendering code. Investigate during implementation whether it\'s in scope here or a distinct task; do not silently skip it.\n\nVerify: live against the real pac-host service, real PING against BNCH (awake unit) if a burst actually lands a reading (mt-transport warned no reading has been observed on air yet — a burst returning `warning:"No replies — try again."` on a sleeping/marginal target is expected, not a bug), both themes, target picker populates from favourites, N-burst and reply-window controls send correctly, null yagi_q/omni_q render as a dash not 0.'}
