2026-07-25 18:43:33,588 1032 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'RAISED 2026-07-25 18:45. The config schema pull has NEVER SUCCEEDED — not once, on any unit,\nall day. The persistent schema cache is empty: `cache` table holds ONE row (a migration\nmarker), and there are no legacy <store>/<node>/schema.json files either.\n\nEVIDENCE IT IS NOT "the unit was asleep" (which is what the 504 claims):\n- `GET /v1/mesh/schema/b80f?refresh=1` returned 504 "unit did not answer" at 17:42, roughly\n  15 SECONDS after a `status` command to the SAME unit round-tripped successfully in ~5 s.\n  The unit was on USB, awake, in dev mode, freshly flashed to 2-260725-21.\n- The pac-host log shows the status commands (queued/immediate try/done) but NOTHING for the\n  schema attempt — no send, no sch page, no timeout line. So the request appears not to have\n  put anything on air at all.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND THE FEATURE: I told node-dash on xsession that the schema is served\nfrom a persistent cache and to "expect a fast answer, not a device round-trip". I later\ncorrected that to "the cache is empty", but the deeper truth is worse — the mechanism that\nwould fill it has never worked. Their config-form work is planned against it.\n\nWHERE TO LOOK (do not re-derive):\n- lib/config.js `schema()` — resolution is hot cache -> disk -> device. The DEVICE leg sends\n  `sch <page>` via the fire-and-forget path (`send` = mesh._sendRaw) and waits for port-260\n  frames routed by `onSchemaFrame`.\n- `sch` is in index.js NO_REPLY, so it deliberately resolves on send and does NOT await a\n  text reply — the data is supposed to arrive as 260 frames. If those never arrive, or are\n  not matched to the in-flight pull, the wait times out and surfaces as 504 via\n  deviceUnreachable() in host-module.js.\n- `_onEvent` routes `ev.kind === \'app\' && ev.portnum === PORT_ALARM` with `obj.t === \'sch\'`\n  into `this.config.onSchemaFrame(ev.from, obj)`. Check the device actually EMITS those.\n\nIDEAL CONDITIONS EXIST RIGHT NOW: bench unit !987ab80f is on USB, awake, dev mode, fw\n2-260725-21, AND Peter has the CH343 debug tap connected (/dev/rak-debug -> ttyACM0). So the\ndevice side can be observed directly while a pull is attempted — do NOT drive control lines\n(configure before open); see memory rak-serial-needs-dtr.\n\nFIRST STEP IS LOGGING, NOT A FIX. There is currently no log line anywhere in the sch path,\nwhich is why this went unnoticed for a whole day of use. Add it before theorising.'}
