2026-07-25 20:05:20,300 1032 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'schema-pull-never-works', 'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'ROOT CAUSE FOUND 2026-07-25 19:10 — AND IT IS FAR WIDER THAN THE SCHEMA.\n\nNEITHER ALARM UNIT HAS EMITTED A SINGLE PORT-260 (PRIVATE_APP) FRAME ALL DAY.\nRecorder counts for 2026-07-25:\n  OMNI !2687afb1 (our gateway, OUTBOUND) : 10117\n  bench  !987ab80f                       : 0\n  deployed !8cee336b                     : 0\n\nSo the device -> host port-260 return path is DEAD in that direction. This is not a schema\nbug, not caching, not sleep.\n\nEVIDENCE CHAIN (all today, all reproducible):\n1. `GET /v1/mesh/schema/b80f?refresh=1` -> 504, twice, against a unit that was awake on USB.\n2. `config` verb to the SAME unit round-tripped in 7 s (18:37) — so commands REACH the device\n   and TEXT replies come back fine.\n3. Sent `sch 0` directly and watched mesh-gw /events for 30 s: ZERO private_app frames.\n4. Firmware IS correct on its side: main.cpp:2807 `sch` builds the page and calls\n   mesh.send(PAC_ALARM_APP=260, ...) with reply[0]=0 (no text reply, the frame IS the reply).\n\nWHAT THIS BREAKS — everything in index.js NO_REPLY, i.e. every verb that answers by a 260\nframe rather than text:\n  debug · sch · cam grab · chunk pull · push pull\nThat is the config schema, the debug frame, AND THE ENTIRE CHUNK/IMAGE TRANSFER PATH.\nText-reply verbs (status, config, ping, name, txp, sleepmode) are unaffected, which is why\nthis went unnoticed all day.\n\nMAY ALSO EXPLAIN the camera finding: cam=0 on battery was attributed to cam-deep-sleep-hold,\nbut image transfer rides this same 260 path — do not close that task on the sleep-hold\ntheory until this is fixed and retested.\n\nWHERE TO LOOK NEXT (not yet investigated):\n- Does the device actually TRANSMIT the 260 frame? Check on the CH343 debug tap\n  (/dev/rak-debug -> ttyACM0) while sending `sch 0` — the firmware logs its own TX. That\n  splits "device never sent" from "sent but we never received".\n- If the device IS transmitting: does mesh-gw decode/emit it? Our gateway must be on a\n  channel whose PSK matches. NOTE the alarm carries the private channel at ITS index 0,\n  while the gateways use index 1/2 — a mismatch here would drop exactly these frames while\n  leaving text (which rides a different channel/path) working.\n- Was this EVER working? Check earlier recorder CSVs (mesh-20260723/24) for PRIVATE_APP from\n  987ab80f / 8cee336b. If it worked before, find what changed.\n\nDO NOT tell node-dash the schema is coming until this is understood — I have already had to\ncorrect that claim twice.'}
