2026-07-25 20:24:56,197 7900 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Fix a real, confirmed data-regression bug found during /investigate (2026-07-25), reported to Peter, approved for a dedicated /idiot fix.\n\nRoot cause: `upsertNode` (src/db.js) and `node-list.js`\'s `handleNodeUpdate` both apply BLE-nodedb-replay data (`node_info`/`node_update` events — explicitly NOT reception evidence, per this repo\'s own comments) unconditionally, with no check that the incoming `last_heard` is actually newer than what\'s already stored. A radio\'s BLE resync replays its ENTIRE local nodedb cache, which for any node the radio hasn\'t personally re-heard recently is itself stale — and every replay re-writes that old snapshot over whatever fresher data direct reception had already produced, silently rolling short_name/long_name/hw_model/position/last_heard backward together.\n\nConfirmed live with 5 real nodes where `nodes.last_heard`/`updated_at` sat at a value strictly OLDER than the most recent DIRECT-reception `signal_history` entry (signal_history is written only from hops===0 packets, i.e. unambiguous real reception) for that same node — up to 4.4 days stale (F4HB), 2.5 days (TA2m), 17.75h (trac).\n\nPeter\'s direction: "for those which belong here /idiot it" — this bug belongs in node-dash (both broken call sites are in this repo); the OTHER symptom investigated alongside it (BLE device uptime_s freezing for ~3 days) was assessed as a mesh-gw-side issue and raised separately via xsession (~/.claude/xsession-meshgw.md, item [uptime-stall]), not fixed here.'}
