2026-07-25 20:48:11,757 1032 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER\'S DECISION 2026-07-25 21:00: "rip out schema. we will create a schema.yaml or .json\nfile. unbelievable 7 pages, that is the equivalent of a small image."\n\nTHE SCHEMA MUST NEVER CROSS THE RADIO AGAIN.\n\nWHY — this was already the documented design and was implemented the wrong way anyway.\n`pac-garage-alarm/docs/config-schema.json` (dated 2026-07-18) says in its own first line:\n  "Machine-readable config metadata for auto-generating a config UI. STATIC per firmware\n   version (NEVER SENT OVER THE AIR). ... Symlink into consumers (node-dash)."\nSo a file was always the intent. The over-air `sch` pull is redundant with it.\n\nWHAT THE OVER-AIR PULL ACTUALLY COSTS (measured 2026-07-25, do not re-derive):\n- 20 fields at SCHEMA_PER_PAGE=3 => 7 PAGES, each a separate request/response round trip.\n- Device answers 30-90 s per page when busy => a full pull is MINUTES.\n- A real page decoded: 178 bytes of the 237 cap (59 wasted), and the 35-byte column header\n  ["id","ty","lb","df","w","mn","mx"] is REPEATED ON EVERY PAGE = 245 bytes of pure\n  redundancy across the 7.\n- The task `config-schema` step 4 specified SIX fields per page; the code shipped THREE.\n  Steps 2, 5, 7 of that task were never completed.\n- Net: ~1.2 kB of static data moved with more coordination than a small image transfer.\n- It has NEVER once succeeded: the persistent cache is empty on every unit, every day.\n\nTHE REPLACEMENT:\n1. GENERATE the file from CONFIG_FIELDS at BUILD time. Not hand-maintained — the existing\n   docs/config-schema.json is dated 18 July and the firmware has changed since, so it is\n   probably already stale. This is the spirit of config-schema step 2 ("emit from the SAME\n   table applySet() validates against, one source of truth"). Generating it makes drift\n   impossible rather than merely discouraged.\n2. SERVE it from GET /v1/mesh/schema/:target, selected by the unit\'s FIRMWARE VERSION\n   (already known from `status` / the long name). Instant, no radio, works while the unit\n   sleeps, no cache needed, no 504.\n3. REMOVE from firmware: the `sch` verb, buildSchema(), SCHEMA_PER_PAGE, the schema TX\n   path. KEEP CONFIG_FIELDS ITSELF — applySet() validates against it and that is unrelated.\n4. REMOVE from clients/mesh/lib/config.js: _pullPage, onSchemaFrame, the _pending map and\n   the schema* timeouts. The `sch` entry in index.js NO_REPLY goes too.\n\nCONSEQUENCES TO HANDLE:\n- timing.schemaAnswerMs / schemaRetryMs become dead once the pull is gone — remove them\n  from settings.js and both config files, and from test/timeouts.js REQUIRED list.\n- node-dash has been told THREE times about schema availability, each version wrong. They\n  must be told the final shape: it is a file, served instantly, keyed by fw version. Do not\n  announce until it actually works.\n- The firmware half needs a FLASH, so it is bench-only; the deployed unit keeps the dead\n  `sch` verb until its next swap. Harmless — nothing will call it.\n\nDO THIS FIRST (step 1+2, no firmware): generating the file and serving it makes the feature\nwork TODAY without touching the deployed unit. The firmware removal (step 3) is cleanup and\ncan wait for the next flash window.'}
