2026-07-25 20:48:26,694 7900 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Add a monotonicity gate so BLE-nodedb-replay data can never roll last_heard/identity backward over fresher direct-reception data:\n\n1. src/db.js — stmts.upsertNode: add `WHERE excluded.last_heard IS NULL OR nodes.last_heard IS NULL OR excluded.last_heard >= nodes.last_heard` to the ON CONFLICT(num) DO UPDATE clause. SQL-level gate, protects every caller uniformly.\n2. src/persist.js — _upsertCache(num, nodeId, u, pos, lastHeard): new 5th param; reads stmts.getNodeByNum before writing nodeinfo, skips the write if lastHeard is older than the stored nodes.last_heard (nodeinfo has no last_heard column of its own, borrows nodes' via the now-authoritative upsertNode gate). All three call sites (user event, raw packet NODEINFO_APP, handleNodeInfo replay path) updated to pass last_heard through.\n3. src/node-list.js — NodeList.handleNodeUpdate: shared isStaleReplay(existing) closure, guards all 3 replay-merge branches (scan-active cache-hit, scan-active pending-buffer, PASV/ACTV enrich-existing) — returns early instead of merging when node.last_heard is older than the existing in-memory entry's last_heard.\n\nVerified live: SQL-level reject/accept test against a real stale node (trac, num 1241821236), plus incidental confirmation via the BNCH/GARG short-name-swap propagating correctly (fresh data still accepted). Specs updated: docs/modules/db.md, docs/modules/persist.md, docs/modules/node-list.md."}
