2026-07-25 21:15:44,517 17830 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "New file mcpp-chat/hook.py: reads the hook JSON on stdin, resolves the party from the payload's cwd (fall back to CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR then getcwd), queries chat.db READ-ONLY via the existing chat.py helpers, emits the JSON shape each event wants — additionalContext for SessionStart/UserPromptSubmit, decision:block + reason for Stop. Silent and exit 0 when there is nothing pending, and on ANY error: a hook that breaks must never break the session. Stop guards on stop_hook_active so it can block at most once per stop cycle; it self-clears because chat_read advances the cursor. Then merge three hook entries into ~/.claude/settings.json (currently has no hooks), pipe-test each with synthetic stdin, validate with jq -e. Files in scope: mcpp-chat/{hook.py, docs/hooks.md, tests/test_hook.py, README.md} and ~/.claude/settings.json."}
