2026-07-25 21:25:29,459 22510 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Reported from node-dash and confirmed: [uptime-stall] is answered but deliberately unresolved (waiting on mesh-gw to ship the fix), and the Stop hook re-blocks every turn because "author + status=ack" counts as actionable forever. The only escapes are resolving early — which would falsify the board — or prune-ok, which needs done. Fix the blocking rule rather than adding a park state: Stop must block only when ANOTHER party is waiting on this session\'s response. Housekeeping the session itself controls the timing of (your resolve, your prune-ok) stays visible in passive context but must never hold a turn open.'}
