2026-07-25 21:30:29,191 23302 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'SPEC: specs/schema-file-not-over-air.md (attached). Two commits, one per repo.\n\nDONE 2026-07-25:\n- pac-garage-alarm 174a14b — tools/gen_schema.py parses the CONFIG_FIELDS table in main.cpp\n  and emits docs/config-schema.json stamped with FW_VERSION. Runs as a pre-build step beside\n  bump_fw.py, so drift is impossible rather than discouraged. Resolves constant defaults\n  (txp = TX_DBM) and emits "" for text fields to match fmtField(). A parse mismatch FAILS THE\n  BUILD rather than writing a partial file — that guard caught the txp gap on the first run,\n  which is exactly how the predecessor rotted to 10 of 20 fields unnoticed.\n- mt-transport 71b1af5 — the client half. _pullPage / onSchemaFrame / `sch` in NO_REPLY /\n  schemaAnswerMs / schemaRetryMs are all gone. GET /v1/mesh/schema/:target serves the file:\n  20 fields in ~14 ms, ZERO airtime, and it works for a SLEEPING unit — the case that was\n  impossible before. Response carries the file\'s fw AND the unit\'s, so `stale` is\n  true / false / null instead of silently rendering a form for the wrong build.\n  Committed together with all-timeouts-configurable: the two changes share settings.js,\n  config.js, both config files and test/timeouts.js, and are the same defect seen twice.\n\nFIXED ON THE WAY: Config._field() degrades to built-in bounds when the schema is\nunavailable but caught only the old code ESCHEMA. The file path raises ESCHEMAFILE/ECONFIG,\nwhich propagated — turning "schema file missing" into a hard failure of EVERY config write.\n\nSuite 19 files green (config 31, timeouts 34, align 49, butler 49, db 37).\n\nSTILL OPEN:\n- Step 3 (firmware removal of `sch` / buildSchema / SCHEMA_PER_PAGE) needs a FLASH, so it is\n  bench-only and waits for the next flash window. It is dead code meanwhile — nothing calls it.\n- Step 4\'s second half: node-dash has been told three times about schema availability, each\n  version wrong. They get told once more now that it is verified working.'}
