2026-07-25 22:11:39,588 23106 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'Node signal (dBm) freezes at last direct reading, never updates once a node goes relay-only (from mt-transport chat)', 'description': 'mt-transport report (mcpp-chat `mt-transport--node-dash` #13/#17, [hops-and-lasthop-rssi]): GARG\'s node page showed "~-40 dBm" while their per-packet data showed the node relaying at 1-2 hops with a true direct RSSI of -128 (noise floor). Confirmed root cause, real bug not by design:\n\n- src/node-status.js:413 reads `nodes.rssi`/`nodes.snr` for the Signal stat card.\n- Write path (src/persist.js): `rssi`/`snr` are only set when `isDirect(hops===0)` is true; a relayed packet passes `null` for both.\n- src/db.js:399-400 upserts with `COALESCE(excluded.rssi, rssi)` — a relayed packet\'s `null` never overwrites the stored value, so once a node goes relay-only its `nodes.rssi`/`nodes.snr` freeze at the last genuinely-direct reading forever (possibly a bench/USB-proximity value) and never indicate staleness.\n\nThis is the RSSI-equivalent of the nodeinfo-replay-regression pattern (task `nodeinfo-replay-regression`, already fixed) but for a different field pair and a different cause (COALESCE hiding a stale value rather than an unconditional overwrite). Fix should make the Signal card reflect that the value is stale/direct-only once the node has been relay-only for some period, or track last-hop RSSI as a separate labeled field alongside the direct-only one. Reply to mt-transport in the chat channel once addressed.'}
2026-07-25 22:11:47,622 23106 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'Traceroute "verified" hop count goes stale silently — no re-run prompt when a node relocates (from mt-transport chat)', 'description': 'mt-transport report (mcpp-chat `mt-transport--node-dash` #13/#16/#17, [hops-and-lasthop-rssi]): GARG\'s node page showed 0 hops "verified" while the node was actually relaying at 1-2 hops per mt-transport\'s live packet data. Not a bug — working as designed: src/node-status.js:43-71 (`hopsField`) explicitly prefers a cached traceroute ("VERIFIED... Authoritative... Verified wins when present") over live reported hop_start/hop_limit data, and the desc field does show "verified {timestamp}" so the staleness is technically on screen. Root cause of the confusion: the cached traceroute almost certainly predates GARG\'s field deployment (17:06 BST) — captured while it was on the bench, direct via USB — and nothing prompts a re-run once the node moves/redeploys, so a bench-time "0 hops" reading is displayed as current indefinitely.\n\nConsider: re-run traceroute automatically on redeploy/relocation signal, or visually flag the verified route as "may be stale" past some age threshold, so a timestamp buried in stat-card desc text isn\'t the only signal. Not urgent — correctly attributed as a UX/staleness gap, not a data-correctness bug like step 34. Reply to mt-transport in the chat channel if/when addressed.'}
