2026-07-25 22:28:34,025 23302 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'AUDIT 2026-07-25 22:20 BST. Peter: "how many other bugs are you expecting me to uncover for you, seems\nthat I work for you not the other way around" — then "you can fix them all while I sleep".\nFound by auditing the live API, not by him. All four are the same failure: THE API STATES SOMETHING\nIT HAS NOT MEASURED.\n\n1. fw REGEX ONLY MATCHES THE BROKEN NAME (index.js:236)\n   /^[0-9a-f]{4}\\s+(\\S+)$/i demands 4 hex chars, which is the FALLBACK long name a unit carries when\n   its role name has NOT been applied. Every correctly-named unit fails:\n     "b80f 2-260725-21"   -> 2-260725-21   (works only because THAT unit\'s name is broken)\n     "Garage 2-260725-20" -> NULL          (the DEPLOYED unit)\n     "Bench 2-260725-9"   -> NULL\n     "GARG 2-260725-20"   -> NULL\n   CONSEQUENCE, MEASURED LIVE: the `stale` version check shipped TODAY is inert on the deployed unit.\n     /schema/b80f  unitFw=\'2-260725-21\' stale=True\n     /schema/336b  unitFw=None          stale=None\n   It was verified this evening against the one unit whose name happens to match. That is the whole\n   point of `stale` — stopping a dashboard rendering a form for the wrong build — and it is off on\n   the only unit that cannot be reflashed.\n\n2. `awake` IS NOT LIVENESS (index.js:248 and :427)\n   `awake: this.unitMode(id) === \'dev\'`, and unitMode() reads cfg.units[id].mode — an operator\n   setting typed into a config file. GARG reports awake:false because someone wrote "mode":"live",\n   NOT because it is asleep. It would report the same sitting awake on the desk. `slp` is null on\n   both units, so nothing real backs it either.\n\n3. DEVICE LABELS INVERTED (config.yaml, host.config.json)\n   !8cee336b is AT THE GARAGE labelled "Bench alarm"; !987ab80f is ON THE BENCH labelled\n   "Garage alarm". Short names and modes were toggled at the swap; labels were not.\n\n4. LEDGER: pruneRequests() IS DEAD, AND `queued` HIDES AN ACTIVE RETRY\n   store.js:266 defines pruneRequests(); the only caller is test/db.js:119. 150 rows for one unit\n   and growing without bound.\n   And Peter, looking at /control: "ping / 29m ago / queued" — with tries=3/5 and a delivery attempt\n   9 minutes earlier invisible. Our contract makes `state` the headline and buries `tries`, so\n   `queued` means both "never attempted" and "3 of 5 attempts made". Nobody rendered it wrong; the\n   contract invited it. Also no `nextTry`: even seeing tries you cannot tell if the next attempt is\n   in 30 s or 15 min, because it is gated on the unit\'s wake window that only we know.\n\nCORRECTION ALREADY ISSUED: I told Peter GET /v1/mesh/align was not reading its config. WRONG —\nindex.js:91 wires cfg.align.radios in; the nulls are an idle state machine. Do not "fix" that.\n\nRULE FOR THIS TASK: if a value has not been measured, the API says null and says why. Never infer a\nphysical fact (awake, fw) from a config file.'}
