2026-07-25 22:41:28,977 23302 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'SPEC: specs/audit-260725a-truth.md (attached). Run under /idiot, all 5 phases.\n\nDONE 2026-07-25 22:40 — VERIFIED LIVE on the running pac-host:\n\n1. fw regex — index.js now anchors on the VERSION SHAPE /(?:^|\\s)(\\d+-\\d{6}-\\d+)\\s*$/, not the\n   4-hex prefix. BOTH units parse now:\n     !8cee336b \'Garage 2-260725-20\' -> fw 2-260725-20   (was NULL)\n     !987ab80f \'b80f 2-260725-21\'   -> fw 2-260725-21\n   THE POINT: /schema/336b went stale=None -> stale=True with unitFw=\'2-260725-20\'. The staleness\n   check shipped that morning was INERT on the deployed unit and now works.\n\n2. awake — new Mesh._awake(id): heard within mode.silentMs => true, beyond => false, NEVER heard\n   => null (UNKNOWN). No longer derived from unitMode(). Both /devices and unitInfo use it.\n   `slp` stays separate (device SETTING, not state).\n\n3. labels — swapped in config.yaml + host.config.json, with a comment recording that labels\n   encode LOCATION and must be toggled on every swap. Verified against reported positions:\n   2.501 km apart on bearing 301.2 deg.\n\n4. ledger — pruneRequests() now called on connect with store.keepPerUnit (declared in settings,\n   default 500); it only ever removed terminal rows so live ones were never at risk.\n   `trying` is now STICKY: a row stays `trying` between attempts, so `queued` means exactly\n   "not yet attempted". This is what Peter hit — /control showed "ping 29m ago queued" while the\n   record held tries 3/5. Five sites touched; the two dangerous ones (cancel, _sweep expiry)\n   gained an inflight guard so a retrying row stays cancellable AND expirable instead of becoming\n   immortal. Added nextTryAt + db.js migration 3 (next_try_at) so it survives a restart.\n\nTESTS: 19 files green. butler 49->56 (cancel-while-retrying, expire-while-retrying, restart\nresumes), devices 31->40 (fw shapes incl. role-named units, awake three-valued despite a\nmode override). Three stale assertions encoded the OLD state machine and were corrected; the\nrestart one was REWRITTEN to assert the real invariant (it still gets delivered) rather than a\nstate string.\n\nAPI.md updated: the state table, sticky `trying`, `nextTryAt`, and `awake` as a three-valued\nMEASUREMENT. node-dash needs NO code change — `trying` was already in the documented enum, so\ntheir existing display starts telling the truth by itself. They still need TELLING.\n\nFOUND, NOT FIXED (pre-existing, logged in the spec): a restart grants ONE extra delivery attempt\n— a row interrupted at tries==maxTries is reloaded, selected, incremented past maxTries, tried,\nthen failed. Old code did the same via queued. Terminates correctly, costs one transmission.\nThe guard belongs in _deliverNext and is a separate change.\n\nDEFERRED: awake returning true/false from real traffic — pac-host restarted so lastHeardMs is\nempty and every unit correctly reads null. Needs one ~15-min heartbeat; watcher running.\n\nCORRECTION STANDING: /v1/mesh/align is NOT broken. index.js:91 wires cfg.align.radios; the nulls\nare an idle state machine. I told Peter otherwise and was wrong.'}
