2026-07-26 08:30:48,823 37757 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'wake-schedule-known', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'DESIGN CORRECTION FROM PETER, 2026-07-26: "next_wake should be a variable for each device!"\n\nRight, and it is not a detail — it decides the shape. nextWake is a PER-DEVICE FIELD carried on\nthe model\'s node record and surfaced on GET /v1/mesh/devices, alongside the fields it belongs\nwith (lastHeard, awake, slp, mode). It is NOT a helper each call site computes for itself.\n\nSame rule as every-timeout-configurable: ONE declaration, derived nowhere else. If nextWake is\nrecomputed at each site we get three subtly different answers and no way to tell which is wrong —\nthat is precisely how `awake` came to be inferred from a config file.\n\nEverything else in this task then DERIVES from that one field rather than re-deriving the beat:\n  nextTryAt              = device.nextWake (the butler stops claiming it is unknowable)\n  immediate-try gating   = now < device.nextWake - windowMs  =>  do not transmit, schedule\n  ttl / maxTries sizing  = a multiple of device.beat\n  API `awake`            gains its forward half: "asleep, next window at HH:MM:SS"\n\nSo the model gains TWO fields per node, not one: `beat` (measured interval, or the device\'s own\nreported `beat` from the config reply) and `nextWake` (lastHeardMs + beat). Both null until\nmeasured — never guessed, same rule as audit-260725a-truth.\n\nOrdering unchanged: after reply-correlation. But this makes step 2 (nextTryAt) a CONSEQUENCE of\nstep 1 rather than a separate change, so the two collapse into one.'}
