2026-07-26 08:39:52,276 41109 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'SPEC: specs/reply-correlation.md — to be written under /idiot, all 5 phases.\n\nPHASE 1 COMPLETE 2026-07-26. Full trace + caller census:\n  gw event ──► index.js:177  timing.onReply(reply, ev.replyId)      1 production caller\n  butler   ──► index.js:114  deliver(unit,verb,args,entry) ──► command()   ENTRY DROPPED HERE\n  command  ──► index.js:357  timing.enqueue(thunk, opts)            1 production caller\n  _pump    ──► timing.js:130 e.sentId = res.id   (memory only, transient object)\n  timeout  ──► timing.js:142 inFlight = null     (sentId dies)\n  align.js consumes ev.replyId INDEPENDENTLY (onPong/onEnvelope) — NOT in scope, do not touch.\n  Tests: test/transport.js blocks A-F are the only ones exercising timing.\n\nWORSE THAN FIRST STATED: _idem() (index.js:341) sets retries:2, so timing.js:145 re-unshifts\nTHE SAME ENTRY and _pump overwrites e.sentId. One butler try = up to 3 transmissions, 3 packet\nids, ONE retained. A 5-try request can put 15 packets on air and keep the last id only. The map\nmust capture EVERY sentId including the internal retry path.\n\nDECIDED 2026-07-26 — SCOPE BOUNDARY. Peter asked me to stop putting decisions like this to him.\nThe sleep-gate (do not transmit to a unit whose _awake() is false) does NOT go in this spec,\neven though butler.js is already open and it is three lines.\nREASON: this task\'s acceptance is "re-run the SAME 6-ping probe, 3/6 -> >=5/6". The gate moves\nthat same number. Shipping both at once makes the result unattributable — the exact failure mode\nthis whole morning has been about. ONE CHANGE PER MEASUREMENT.\nIt becomes its own task, sequenced immediately AFTER this one, measured on transmissions per\nsettled request (5 -> 4). It needs nothing from wake-schedule-known: _awake() already answers it.\n\nDESIGN, settled in Phase 1:\n  - sent ids live ON the request row (JSON column), not a side table: pruning takes them with\n    the row, restart-safety is free, and the lookup scans only open rows (maxPending 10/unit).\n  - onReply must also receive ev.from and require it to match the unit — a matched reply_id is\n    currently never checked against the node we sent to. Signature change, one caller.\n  - saveQueue is DELETE-then-INSERT: a new column must land in THREE places (db migration,\n    rowToEntry, saveQueue rows) or it silently drops on every persist. That is exactly how\n    toNum/channel were lost before (butler.js:103-106).\n  - a late reply for a PRUNED row finds nothing. Acceptable, but must be LOGGED, never silent.\n  - terminal stays terminal (goal note): a late reply attaches as evidence, never flips state.'}
