2026-07-26 11:26:50,496 62529 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: docs/modules/messages_want_ack_id_passthrough.md. 6 files:\n(1) core/message_manager.py send_text_message: add want_ack: Optional[bool]=None param; line 93 becomes inner.want_ack = (to != 0xFFFFFFFF) if want_ack is None else bool(want_ack). Nothing else in that method changes — the if inner.want_ack ack-timeout branch stays, so emission is byte-identical for every existing (no want_ack) caller.\n(2) core/ble_device.py send_text_message wrapper (919-927): add want_ack: Optional[bool]=None, forward to self._msg.\n(3) core/methods.py send_text (490-508): parse want_ack = params.get("want_ack") (coerce bool if not None); pkt_id = params.get("id") or params.get("pkt_id") (id canonical, pkt_id back-compat alias); pass want_ack through.\n(4) docs/API_REST.md: add want_ack and id rows to the POST /{node_id}/messages request table; note id is canonical, pkt_id a deprecated alias.\n(5) docs/API_SSE.md §message_status: add one sentence stating packet_id is always the id returned from POST /{gwId}/messages (caller-supplied or auto-assigned) and is never rewritten in flight — safe to key correlation off. THIS is mt-alarm\'s blocker.\n(6) module/help.py:54: body hint {text, to?, channel?, reply_id?, want_ack?, id?}.\nDecisions: want_ack default None preserves to!=broadcast; broadcast+want_ack honored literally (option a); id==0 -> auto (existing pkt_id or random covers it). Not changing: response model {id,to}, the ack-timeout logic, the HTTP route (forwards body verbatim), event emission for existing paths. Observe: static grep, functional (unit-drive send with want_ack override both ways + id echo), regression (existing broadcast/DM emission unchanged). Track: sha256 -> spec, check_specs, commit, then post on mesh-gw--services that the API_SSE.md line landed.'}
