2026-07-26 11:40:47,945 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'discover-services', 'title': 'Discovery: verify what this component actually is, against a structure that was rebuilt on 2026-07-26 and is UNPROVEN', 'steps': ['Read ROLE.md, README.md, ../docs/device-behaviour.md. Confirm they match the code.', 'Run all 19 suites. Confirm pac-host serves and a live command round-trips to the bench.', 'Adjudicate the 8 DRIFTED specs in docs/history — for each, was the change intended?', "THE ACK GAP: mesh-gw message_status → gw.js {kind:'status'} → index.js:_onEvent has no branch. Confirm.", 'Rewrite ../docs/api/http.md as a CONTRACT — guarantees, not implementation.', 'GARG stopped answering on 2026-07-26 — 15 transmissions over 45 min, zero replies, telemetry still arriving. Device, link, or us?']}
2026-07-26 11:48:10,411 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'DISCOVERY RESULTS 2026-07-26, all measured, none taken on trust.\n\nVERIFIED WORKING\n- pac-host online :8787, mesh-gw :8001, both radios READY. /v1/mesh/devices serves.\n- 18/19 suites pass.\n- device-behaviour.md §6 knobs match settings.js:98 exactly (windowMs 10000,\n  minBeatMs 20000, beatTolerance 0.25). §8 already records the ACK gap. Doc is honest.\n\nFINDING 1 — flaky test, NOT a code fault. mesh/test/devices.js fails ~40% of runs\n(5 runs: PASS PASS FAIL PASS FAIL). Fixture sets lastHeard = now-B with beat B, so\nnextWake lands exactly on `now`; any elapsed ms trips `while (t < now) t += n.beat`\nat mesh/index.js:446 and rolls a full 900s. Production logic is correct.\n\nFINDING 2 — ACK GAP CONFIRMED at the line. mesh/lib/gw.js:140 normalises\nmessage_status -> {kind:\'status\', packetId, status}. mesh/index.js:_onEvent (177-236)\nbranches on heard / text / app+PORT_ALARM / app+PORT_CHUNK. No status branch.\nContract with mesh-gw is ALREADY SETTLED — enum, sent->queued->relayed->terminal\nordering, and packet_id identity guarantee are cited in ../docs/api/gateway.md.\nS1 needs nothing from anyone.\n\nFINDING 3 — BEAT LOCK, new, not in the roadmap, probable cause of GARG.\nRecorder: GARG beat is 900s +/-3s all day, 58 distinct transmissions, metronome.\nAPI reports beat 1830694 (30.5 min). mesh/lib/model.js:41 seeds beat from the FIRST\ngap with no plausibility guard. If that gap was a missed beat (two today: 07:37,\n08:52) it locks at 2x, and line 42 then rejects every correct 900s gap forever\nbecause |900000-1830694| > beat*0.25. No re-seed path exists. nextWake is therefore\nup to 15 min wrong and the butler transmits into a window where the unit is deaf.\nBNCH (hops 0, beat 220907, correct) answers on try 1.\nNOT described in device-behaviour.md §6 or §7 — doc gap to raise with mt-alarm.\n\nFINDING 4 — GARG never stopped answering. 11 pings since 07-25 19:50: 5 done,\n6 no_reply. The "15 transmissions / 45 min / zero replies" is two ordinary no_reply\nruns (08:55, 09:41). The next request (10:54) settled done at 11:37 on try 2.\nCross-window retry works. Device healthy, link carrying telemetry fine.\n\nFINDING 5 — trial-logger IS NOT RUNNING. Not in pm2, no process, last CSV write\n10:42 (minutes after the restructure). Writes to the OLD tree\npio/projects/pac-garage-alarm/data/mesh-*.csv from code now at services/trial-logger.\nThe instrument every acceptance number depends on is down. Blocked on mt-transport\nanswering where it should run from — will not restart into the wrong path.\n\nDRIFT ADJUDICATION — 1 spec / 8 files, not 8 specs. all-timeouts-configurable.md:\nsettings.js, butler.js, index.js, config.yaml, host.config.json, store.js,\ntest/devices.js, test/mode.js. Plus 5 specs never hashed (source_hash ~) and 4 with\nuntracked scope entries. Put to mt-transport for verdict; if they cannot say, treat\nall 8 as unadjudicated and reconstruct from git rather than re-hash on assumption.\n\nCROSS-SESSION\n- mesh-gw--services: [message-status-semantics] DONE. NOTE: opened by the outgoing\n  mt-transport session under our identity — content is sound but is not our testimony.\n- mt-transport--services: [handover-to-services] acked. Inherited three node-dash\n  items: [standing-rules], [receipt-labels] (shape agreed {id,label,unit,type}, NOT\n  BUILT), [mesh-verbs] (NOT BUILT, blocked — cmds help string omits cam/chunk/push/camu,\n  needs a flash; do not ship a partial list as complete).\n- [services-discovery-handover] OPEN, waiting on mt-transport: http.md ownership,\n  drift verdict, trial-logger home.\n\nNOTHING EDITED. No spec exists for any fix yet.'}
2026-07-26 11:59:22,299 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'recorder-sqlite-backend', 'title': 'PARKED — move the recorder off per-day CSV onto SQLite, with a retention policy. NOT before or during the deployment.', 'steps': ["Read the parked reasoning in docs/history/mesh-devices-route.md §Storage backend (task name 'cache-sqlite-backend' — it is PROSE ONLY, there is no such spec file and no mcpp task; this task supersedes that pointer)", 'Decide the store. better-sqlite3 12.x is already proven on Node 20.19.2; node:sqlite needs >=22.5 and this box is 20.19.2. @pac/mesh has NO local node_modules — ws/yaml resolve from /usr/share/nodejs — so dependency plumbing is the real cost, not the native build.', "Preserve 'readable without an agent'. CSV is append-only, greppable, crash-safe mid-write, and Peter can open it in anything. Whatever replaces it must not lose that — export, view, or keep a CSV tail.", 'RETENTION IS PART OF THIS DECISION, not a follow-up. 32 MB in 10 days, ~1 GB/year, no policy at all. The ledger has keepPerUnit; the recorder has nothing.', "Acceptance: reply-correlation B3 ('zero pongs in the recorder without a matching settled request in the ledger') becomes ONE query instead of Python-loading CSV while curling the HTTP API. Same shape as ack-consumption's reconciliation. That join is the reason to do this.", 'Cross-midnight questions must stop needing manual globbing — the overnight probe analysis had to load two day-files and merge them by hand.']}
2026-07-26 12:01:09,270 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'spec-drift-adjudication', 'title': 'BLOCKED on spec-hash.py — adjudicate 132 drifted files across 31 specs. Do NOT re-hash until the reader is fixed.', 'steps': ['BLOCKER: ../scripts/spec-hash.py:113 cannot read 32 of 43 specs. Raised as [spec-hash-blind] on mt-transport--services. It is in the coordination repo, NOT ours — report, do not fix. Wait for it to land.', 'When fixed: re-run --check-all and confirm it now reports ~132 drifted files in ~31 specs, not 8 in 1. If it still says 8, the fix did not work and nothing below is safe.', 'Adjudicate the 7 REAL drifts in all-timeouts-configurable.md, verdict supplied by mt-transport from git: settings.js/butler.js/index.js/devices.js/mode.js = wake-schedule-known; store.js = reply-correlation; config.yaml = audit-260725a-truth. Re-hash and put the REASON in the status line, not a bare tick.', 'host.config.json in all-timeouts-configurable.md is a RESTRUCTURE ARTEFACT, not a change of meaning — its hash was invalidated by the firmware/->device/ path rewrite. Record that plainly. A bare re-hash would launder it into a clean tick.', "Adjudicate the other 30 specs' drift once visible. Most is genuine evolution (many later specs landed on index.js, settings.js, config.yaml, butler.js). Each needs a verdict, not a bulk re-hash.", 'Fix the 5 MISSING scope entries: host/API.md is hashed in 4 specs (mesh-devices-route, request-ledger-sqlite, schema-file-not-over-air, wake-schedule-known) and no longer exists — it is the pre-restructure name for ../docs/api/http.md. Also ../pac-garage-alarm/docs/config-schema.json in schema-file-not-over-air.', "Repair 3 specs still scoped into the OLD tree, missed by the c8d0695 docs sweep: camera-fetch-stall, chunk-resume, custom-meshtastic-role (projects/mt-transport/clients/node/*, mylibs/, projects/pac-garage-alarm/). All three are DEVICE work sitting in services' history — decide whether they belong here at all before repairing paths.", 'command-butler.md and trial-logger.md have NO scope: block — nothing declares what they cover, so nothing can ever check them.', "mesh-module.md scopes 'mesh/lib/*.js' and single-service-host.md scopes 'host/**'. The resolver does not glob, so these are permanently unhashable. Enumerate or drop."]}
2026-07-26 12:05:47,388 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'bugs', 'title': 'STANDING BUG LEDGER — every defect found, verified or unverified. Append, never delete. Nothing is closed until it is fixed or disproved with evidence.', 'steps': ["B1 CONFIRMED/OPEN — recorder timers are undefined. host.config.json modules.recorder declares only require/wsUrl/dataDir. recorder.js:70-71 read cfg.silenceCheckMs and cfg.reconnectMs = undefined. setInterval(undefined) measured firing 184x/200ms (~920/s), so _checkSilences busy-runs continuously in the LIVE process; recorder.js:151 setTimeout(undefined) hot-loops reconnect (~40 attempts/100ms in the 11:49 log). all-timeouts-configurable.md NAMES trial-logger/recorder.js in scope with comment '# silenceCheckMs / reconnectMs', but test/timeouts.js scans only lib/ + index.js + host-module.js — the enforcing test does not cover the file. FIX NEEDS: declare both in config AND extend the scan.", 'B2 CONFIRMED/OPEN — beat lock. model.js:41 seeds beat from the FIRST gap with no plausibility guard. A missed beat seeds ~1830694; line 42 then rejects every correct 900s gap forever (|900000-1830694| > beat*0.25). No re-seed path. nextWake up to 15 min wrong → butler transmits into a deaf window. Independently confirmed by mt-transport at the same lines. Design constraints agreed: seed from N consistent gaps or confirm provisionally; a run of mutually-agreeing REJECTED gaps is the re-seed signal; prefer device-reported beatReported; a value that cannot be corrected by new evidence is worse than a null one.', "B3 CONFIRMED/OPEN — ACK gap (this is S1 ack-consumption). gw.js:140 normalises message_status to {kind:'status',packetId,status}; index.js:_onEvent (177-236) branches on heard/text/app+PORT_ALARM/app+PORT_CHUNK and has no status branch, so it falls off the end. 'never arrived' and 'arrived, answer lost' are indistinguishable. mesh-gw contract SETTLED and cited in ../docs/api/gateway.md: delivered=arrival (only this one); no_ack=UNCONFIRMED not lost; failed=+error_name; queue_failed=never left the radio; no_ack_needed=broadcast. Ordering sent->queued->(relayed)*->terminal. packet_id never rewritten.", "B4 CONFIRMED/OPEN — silent addressing downgrade. resolve.js:29 returns num:null when a 4-hex suffix or short name is not in the roster; index.js:365 then sets directed=false and sends a private broadcast instead of a PKC DM, with NO error and no null. Per mesh-gw's contract a broadcast gets want_ack off and no_ack_needed, so the request becomes unackable. Ledger consistent: unit '336b' 1 row 0 done, unit '*' 13 rows 0 done, vs '!987ab80f' 94 rows 90 done. NOT deployment-blocking — resolve.js:16-17 resolves numeric/8-hex WITHOUT the roster and both units are config-declared by full id; live bench ping answered ~4s. Severity was overstated by me before that test was run.", "B5 CONFIRMED/OPEN — the ledger cannot say whether a request went out addressed or broadcast. requests.to_num is null on 215/217 rows. store.js:219 persists it and store.js:236 carries a scar comment that toNum/channel were lost once, but only the TEXT path sets it (index.js:550-568); the command path stores a unit key and re-resolves per attempt. Per-attempt resolution is CORRECT and must be kept — mt-transport confirmed setting toNum at enqueue would re-introduce the staleness text-addressing-lost was fixed to avoid. What is missing is the resolution OUTCOME per attempt, alongside each sentIds entry ({id,to} or a parallel array). Blocks B3: without it a no_ack_needed cannot be told from 'unackable because we broadcast it'. CAUTION: must not break the sentIds lookup settleByReplyId depends on.", "B6 CONFIRMED/OPEN — devices.js block 2d is flaky (~40%: measured PASS PASS FAIL PASS FAIL). Fixture sets lastHeard=now-B with beat B so nextWake lands exactly on now; any elapsed ms trips 'while (t < now) t += n.beat' at index.js:446 and rolls a full 900s. PRODUCTION LOGIC IS CORRECT — the test encodes an instant where it should encode a window. Fix: assert nextWake > now && <= now + beat.", "B7 CONFIRMED / NOT OURS — spec-hash.py:113 cannot read 32 of 43 specs and reports them as clean. regex ^\\s{2}(\\S+)\\s+([0-9a-f]{16}): (\\S+) swallows the trailing colon in 'path: hash' (20 specs → keyed 'path:' → falls into the UNTRACKED branch); ^\\s{2} misses the single-line 'source_hash: a b; c d' form (12 specs → reported 'unset (~) never tracked'). Only 3 specs are actually checked. Reported drift 8 files/1 spec; ACTUAL 132 files/31 specs. Fails toward REASSURANCE. Lives in ../scripts/ (coordination repo) and its docstring claims use by firmware, transport, services and lib — every repo's baseline is suspect. Raised as [spec-hash-blind]. REPORT, DO NOT FIX.", 'B8 OPEN QUESTION / THEIRS — mesh-gw /{gwId}/nodes returns 1 node (the gateway); /devices shows node_count 1 and sync_mode config_only on both radios. Our roster is sourced only from there and is NOT persisted (cache table holds one unrelated row), so every pac-host restart loses it. Drives B4. Raised as [roster-and-echo]. Do not guess the cause — it is their service.', "B9 OPEN QUESTION / DECIDES S1 ACCEPTANCE — does mesh-gw echo suppression hide our own transmissions from the recorder? Today's CSV has 6965 packets from our gateway node and ZERO TEXT_MESSAGE_APP, nothing addressed to either unit. If the recorder is blind to our own sends by design, S1's acceptance number must come from the ledger + message_status, NOT the CSV. Must be answered BEFORE the S1 spec states its acceptance criterion. Raised as [roster-and-echo].", "B10 CONFIRMED/OPEN — spec corpus integrity, blocked behind B7. host/API.md is hashed in 4 specs (mesh-devices-route, request-ledger-sqlite, schema-file-not-over-air, wake-schedule-known) and does not exist — pre-restructure name for ../docs/api/http.md. ../pac-garage-alarm/docs/config-schema.json also missing. 3 specs still scoped into the OLD tree (camera-fetch-stall, chunk-resume, custom-meshtastic-role), missed by the c8d0695 sweep, and all 3 are DEVICE work sitting in services' history. command-butler.md and trial-logger.md have NO scope: block. mesh-module.md ('mesh/lib/*.js') and single-service-host.md ('host/**') use globs the resolver cannot expand — permanently unhashable. Tracked in task spec-drift-adjudication.", 'B11 CONFIRMED / NOT OURS — dev/CLAUDE.md lists trial-logger as a separate running service. It is a MODULE inside pac-host (host.config.json modules.recorder); it is not in pm2 and never will be. This wrong assumption cost me time during discovery. Neither this session nor mt-transport owns that file.', "B12 CONFIRMED / DOC — ../docs/roadmap/README.md records GARG as 'stopped answering, unexplained' and treats it as a reason to hesitate before deploying. It is ~50% intermittent and has been for 20h (11 pings since 07-25 19:50: 5 done, 6 no_reply; the 10:54 request settled done at 11:37 on try 2). mt-transport retracted it and asked this repo to correct the file. Also: device-behaviour.md §6/§7 describe beat measurement but do NOT record the B2 lock failure mode — §7 'Assumed, not measured' should carry it.", "B13 CONFIRMED / MINOR — 'cache-sqlite-backend' is cited as a parked task but exists only as prose inside docs/history/mesh-devices-route.md §Storage backend. No spec file, no mcpp task. Superseded by task recorder-sqlite-backend, which carries the reasoning forward."]}
2026-07-26 12:09:12,605 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'B1 SEVERITY RAISED after measurement — the reconnect path, not the silence check, is the serious half.\n\nMEASURED, not estimated:\n  - setInterval(undefined) fires 184x per 200ms  => ~920/s\n  - pac-host CPU sampled from /proc/<pid>/stat over 10s: 39 ticks = 3.9% of one core,\n    continuously, steady-state, for nothing.\n  - n.gaps is capped at 20 (recorder.js:183 `.slice(-20)`), so median() sorts <=20\n    elements. The per-tick work is BOUNDED. That is why it is only ~4% and not worse.\n\nSo the silence check is a real, permanent 4%-of-a-core waste. Wasteful, measurable,\nNOT major on its own. I record that plainly rather than inflating it.\n\nTHE MAJOR HALF IS THE RECONNECT, AND IT IS LATENT\n\nrecorder.js:151  this._reconnect = setTimeout(() => this._connect(), undefined)\n\nundefined delay => fires next tick. On a websocket failure this becomes an unbounded\nreconnect storm against mesh-gw: observed ~40 attempts in ~105ms in the 11:49 log\n(10:50:12.956 -> 10:50:13.061 UTC), i.e. several hundred connection attempts per second,\nlimited only by WS setup cost.\n\nWhy that is the serious one:\n  - it fires EXACTLY when mesh-gw is unavailable — the moment the system is already\n    degraded is the moment pac-host starts hammering it.\n  - mesh-gw owns every radio. A connection flood against it during an outage risks\n    turning a transient WS drop into a longer one.\n  - it is LATENT: invisible while mesh-gw is healthy, so it will not be noticed in\n    testing and will first appear during the multi-day deployment.\n  - there is no backoff of any kind, capped or otherwise.\n\nROOT CAUSE IS A SPEC THAT CREATED THE DEFECT IT WAS WRITTEN TO PREVENT\n\nall-timeouts-configurable removed inline `|| 8000` fallbacks on principle ("an undeclared\nvalue is one nobody knows they can change"). recorder.js:70-71 duly lost its fallbacks.\nThe matching values were never added to host/host.config.json modules.recorder, which\ndeclares only require/wsUrl/dataDir. Note wsUrl and dataDir KEPT their `||` defaults\n(recorder.js:67-68) and are fine; only the two timing values were stripped.\n\nAnd test/timeouts.js — the test written to enforce that spec — scans lib/ + index.js +\nhost-module.js only. trial-logger/recorder.js is IN the spec\'s scope list, with the\ncomment \'# silenceCheckMs / reconnectMs\', and is not scanned. The enforcing test does\nnot cover the file the spec named.\n\nFIX MUST INCLUDE ALL THREE OR IT WILL RECUR:\n  1. declare silenceCheckMs and reconnectMs in host/host.config.json modules.recorder\n  2. extend test/timeouts.js to scan trial-logger/ so this cannot regress silently\n  3. reconnect needs a floor and ideally backoff — an undefined delay should never be\n     able to become a hot loop. Consider failing loudly on an undeclared timing value\n     rather than silently accepting undefined, which is the same fail-toward-reassurance\n     shape as B7.\n\nMY ERROR, RECORDED: I read \'reconnect in undefinedms\' in the pac-host log during\ndiscovery and moved on without investigating. It was visible at 11:49 and I did not\nraise it until Peter pushed back at ~12:10.'}
