2026-07-26 12:09:59,489 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'B1 SEVERITY RAISED after measurement — the reconnect path, not the silence check, is the serious half.\n\nMEASURED, not estimated:\n  - setInterval(undefined) fires 184x per 200ms => ~920/s\n  - pac-host CPU from /proc/<pid>/stat over 10s: 39 ticks = 3.9% of ONE CORE,\n    continuously, steady state, for nothing.\n  - n.gaps is capped at 20 (recorder.js:183 `.slice(-20)`), so median() sorts <=20\n    elements. Per-tick work is BOUNDED. That is why it is ~4% and not worse.\n\nSo the silence check is a real, permanent ~4%-of-a-core waste. Wasteful and measurable,\nbut NOT major on its own. Recorded plainly rather than inflated.\n\nTHE MAJOR HALF IS THE RECONNECT, AND IT IS LATENT\n\n  recorder.js:151   this._reconnect = setTimeout(() => this._connect(), undefined)\n\nundefined delay fires on the next tick. On a websocket failure this becomes an unbounded\nreconnect storm against mesh-gw: observed ~40 attempts in ~105ms in the 11:49 log\n(10:50:12.956 -> 10:50:13.061 UTC) — several hundred connection attempts per second,\nlimited only by WS setup cost. There is no backoff of any kind.\n\nWhy this one is serious:\n  - it fires EXACTLY when mesh-gw is unavailable. The moment the system is already\n    degraded is the moment pac-host starts hammering it.\n  - mesh-gw owns every radio. A connection flood during an outage risks turning a\n    transient WS drop into a longer one.\n  - it is LATENT — invisible while mesh-gw is healthy, so it will not show up in\n    testing and would first appear during the multi-day deployment.\n\nROOT CAUSE: A SPEC THAT CREATED THE DEFECT IT WAS WRITTEN TO PREVENT\n\nall-timeouts-configurable removed inline `|| 8000` fallbacks on principle ("an undeclared\nvalue is one nobody knows they can change"). recorder.js:70-71 duly lost its fallbacks.\nThe matching values were never added to host/host.config.json modules.recorder, which\ndeclares only require/wsUrl/dataDir. Note that wsUrl and dataDir KEPT their `||` defaults\nat recorder.js:67-68 and are fine — only the two timing values were stripped.\n\nAnd test/timeouts.js, the test written to enforce that spec, scans lib/ + index.js +\nhost-module.js only. trial-logger/recorder.js IS in the spec\'s scope list, with the\ncomment \'# silenceCheckMs / reconnectMs\', and is not scanned. The enforcing test does not\ncover the file the spec named.\n\nFIX MUST INCLUDE ALL THREE OR IT RECURS:\n  1. declare silenceCheckMs and reconnectMs in host/host.config.json modules.recorder\n  2. extend test/timeouts.js to scan trial-logger/ so it cannot regress silently\n  3. give reconnect a floor and ideally backoff. An undefined delay must never be able to\n     become a hot loop — prefer failing loudly on an undeclared timing value over\n     silently accepting undefined, which is the same fail-toward-reassurance shape as B7.\n\nMY ERROR, RECORDED: \'reconnect in undefinedms\' was in the pac-host log I read during\ndiscovery at 11:49 and I moved past it. I did not raise it until Peter pushed back.'}
