2026-07-26 12:10:20,203 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "B14 CONFIRMED / TOOLING — mcpp resolves the task name 'bugs' to DIFFERENT tasks depending on the call. plan_task_notes_set(name:'bugs') wrote into the node-dash/mt-radar bugs task (note 1562) while plan_task_show(name:'bugs') returned THIS task (context 735, services) with notes:[]. Same name, same session, two tasks. Impact: a note believed filed is silently filed in another project's ledger — the exact 'recorded in a place nothing reads' failure. Workaround: plan_task_switch first, then call notes_set with NO name param, so it targets the active task. Stray note 1562 has been deleted from the other project and re-added here as note 1563; verified that task now holds only its own three pre-existing notes. NOT OURS to fix."}
2026-07-26 12:11:36,608 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'B2 EVIDENCE CORRECTED 2026-07-26 — my first beat analysis read the WRONG FILE.\n\nI computed GARG\'s cadence from /usr/share/pac/dev/pio/projects/pac-garage-alarm/data/\nmesh-20260726.csv — the ABANDONED old-tree recorder output, frozen at 10:42 by the\ncutover. The live file is\n/usr/share/pac/dev/projects/mt-alarm/device/data/mesh-20260726.csv.\nCaught only when Peter asked whether I was working in the old repo.\n\nRE-RUN AGAINST THE LIVE FILE. The finding stands and is better evidenced:\n\n  distinct GARG transmissions today : 62  (was 58 from the stale file)\n  inter-beat gaps > 60s             : 35\n  900s   : 29     <- the beat, unambiguous\n  1800s  :  5     <- exactly one missed beat each\n  4505s  :  1     <- see caveat below\n\nSo GARG\'s interval is 900s and we hear ~83% of its beats. The model reported\nbeat = 1830694 ms. Beat lock confirmed on live data, not on the stale copy.\n\nCAVEAT, STATED RATHER THAN BURIED: the single 4505s gap (09:52:14 -> 11:07:19) falls in\nthe window where OUR recorder was itself unreliable — stale dataDir after the\nfirmware/->device/ rename, writing erratically and then not at all until the 11:49\nrestart. That gap is an instrument artefact and must NOT be counted as missed beats. It\nis excluded from the 83% above being described as a device or link property.\n\nLESSON: two CSV trees now exist with the same filenames, one live and one abandoned.\nReading the wrong one produces plausible, wrong numbers silently. Until the old tree is\ndeleted, every recorder query must state which path it read. See B10 / mt-transport\'s\n"do not split them" note on the CSVs.'}
2026-07-26 12:19:10,731 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'B8/B9 ANSWERED 2026-07-26 by mesh-gw, [roster-and-echo] CLOSED. B8 is NOT A BUG: sync_mode config_only sends want_config with SPECIAL_NONCE_ONLY_CONFIG (ble_device.py:64,1992) so the nodedb is deliberately never synced; /{gwId}/nodes is a SNAPSHOT of the sync-time dump (ble_device.py:2272-2276), not a running tally — live NODEINFO never accretes into it. It will NEVER carry our units. Fix is OURS: persist our own device->num map (option i). We declined sync_mode full — config_only is their deliberate choice and 2 units do not justify roster churn on an 82-node mesh. B9 ANSWERED, AND IT CHANGES S1: our own TEXT sends are suppressed by id at ble_device.py:2361 BEFORE becoming an event, so the recorder can NEVER see them — by design. S1 acceptance MUST measure from message_status (live) and/or GET /{gwId}/messages (server-side ledger), NOT the /events packet stream. ROUTING_APP acks ARE emitted as separate packets referencing ours via request_id — that is what we saw and misread. S1 IS NOW UNBLOCKED.'}
