2026-07-26 12:50:59,936 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': "B15 CONFIRMED/OPEN — image push has NO give-up path. B1's exact twin, and worse. settings.js:47-48 declares pushMaxStale:8 and pushMaxUnanswered:30; host.config.json:44-45 carries both; timeouts.js:27 asserts both 'declared and positive'. push-receiver.js:46 takes {idleMs,maxStale,maxUnanswered,actMs,quietMs} and images.js:63 constructs it with ONLY {idleMs, actMs, quietMs} — maxStale and maxUnanswered are never passed. So this.maxStale/this.maxUnanswered are undefined, and push-receiver.js:203 'if (this.staleRounds >= this.maxStale)' and :223 'if (this.unanswered >= this.maxUnanswered)' are ALWAYS FALSE (verified in node: 99 >= undefined -> false). Both give-up guards are dead: a stuck push never declares 'stuck: N consecutive repair rounds' and an unresponsive device never declares 'device unresponsive'. Against a unit deaf ~99% of the time this means an image transfer can retry indefinitely with no terminal state. Found while implementing B1; NOT fixed (out of scope). Needs its own task+spec."}
2026-07-26 12:51:03,446 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'B16 CONFIRMED/OPEN — timing.chunkAnswerMs is declared and consumed by nobody. settings.js:36 chunkAnswerMs:8000, mesh/config.yaml:20, host.config.json:34, and timeouts.js:24 asserts it declared+positive. No consumer anywhere in mesh/, host/ or trial-logger/. Dead config. Note settings.js:30 and timeouts.js:8 both reference it in comments about the schemaAnswerMs misdiagnosis, so it may be a leftover from that fix. Either something should read it or it should be deleted — a declared knob nobody reads is a lie about what is configurable. Found while implementing B1; NOT fixed.'}
