2026-07-26 13:20:33,604 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "Stop the recorder's timing values being undefined in the live service, and close the hole that let it happen.\n\nThe values were declared under modules.mesh.timing while the recorder is a separate host module that only ever receives modules.recorder (host/index.js:63). setInterval/setTimeout accept undefined and fire on the next tick, so there was no error — just a ~920/s silence check and a reconnect path with no delay.\n\nThe CPU waste (3.9% of a core, continuous) was the visible half. The reconnect was the serious half and it was latent: no backoff, several hundred connection attempts per second, and it only runs when mesh-gw is already unavailable — the one service that can reach the radios, during a multi-day deployment.\n\nFix the wiring, not the values. Then make recurrence impossible: timeouts.js must scan trial-logger/ and must assert that every declared timing value REACHES a consumer, not merely that it is declared."}
2026-07-26 13:20:45,434 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Spec: docs/history/recorder-timers-undeclared.md (attached). Commit e9148c3.\n\n1. recorder.js — req(cfg, k) throws on missing/non-positive instead of accepting undefined. Also declares alertsDefaultLimit/alertsMaxLimit (the /alerts `|| 100, 1000` the new scan caught).\n2. host.config.json — both values under modules.recorder, deliberately duplicated rather than read across from modules.mesh.timing.\n3. trial-logger.js — explicit DEFAULTS block; a declaration site for the standalone path, ALLOW-listed in the scan.\n4. timeouts.js — scan trial-logger/ (14 -> 16 files); new coupling assertion with a named KNOWN_UNCOUPLED set.\n5. offline_recorder.js — 5 throw cases + 2 verbatim-value cases.\n\nRESULT, measured: pac-host idle CPU 39 -> 3 ticks/10s; silence check ~9200 -> 0 fires/10s; reconnect log 'undefinedms' -> '5000'. timeouts 36 assertions, offline_recorder 31 checks. Live: bench ping answered, recorder connected, CSV growing.\n\nmesh suite 18/19 — devices.js is B6-flaky (FAIL PASS FAIL PASS FAIL over 5 runs), pre-existing, untouched.\n\nFOUND AND NOT FIXED (in the bugs ledger, reported to mt-transport as [recorder-cpu-fixed]):\n- B15 image push give-up guards are DEAD. images.js:63 never passes maxStale/maxUnanswered, so push-receiver.js:203/:223 compare `>= undefined` — always false. A stuck push has no terminal state. Needs its own task+spec. Worse than the bug this task fixed.\n- B16 chunkAnswerMs declared in three places, read by nothing.\n- trial-logger/test/offline_recorder.js is NOT in the documented suite run (`for f in mesh/test/*.js`), so its six Recorder constructions would have broken silently."}
