2026-07-26 13:38:05,123 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'B7 RECLASSIFIED 2026-07-26: NOT OURS -> OURS TO FIX. mt-transport confirmed they wrote spec-hash.py this morning, verified my diagnosis independently (plain/colon/inline reproduced), and are now read-only — the fix falls to us. THEIR CAUSE ANALYSIS: the tool was written AFTER the corpus, to read the format they were writing that same morning, then "verified" against ONE spec (reply-correlation) they had just written in that format. A reader validated against one input it was designed for is not validated. THE FIX IS NOT THE REGEX — it is the failure DIRECTION: \'source_hash absent\' and \'source_hash present but unparseable\' both print \'spec never tracked\' and both exit 0. Required behaviour: (1) a source_hash key that yields zero parsed entries is an ERROR with non-zero exit and the words \'present but unparseable\', never \'untracked\'; (2) \'UNTRACKED <path>\' may ONLY mean \'in scope: and absent from a block we successfully read\'; (3) --check-all must report specs PARSED vs specs SEEN so a run skipping 32 of 44 cannot be mistaken for clean. Normalising the three formats on write comes AFTER the reader is strict, never before — otherwise you normalise from data you cannot read. Blocks task spec-drift-adjudication.'}
