2026-07-26 13:40:53,618 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "B7 FIX DESIGN CORRECTED by mt-transport — 'source_hash present but unparseable' is NOT a sufficient error condition. The colon form DOES parse; it yields keys like 'mesh/lib/butler.js:' that match no real path. So the test cannot be 'did I extract entries' — it must be 'does EVERY extracted key resolve to a path listed in scope:'. A source_hash entry naming a file not in scope, or not on disk, is a CORRUPT RECORD and must be loud, never silently skipped as UNTRACKED. Otherwise fixing the inline form makes 20 colon-form specs go from 'never tracked' to 'every file untracked' — still reassuring, still wrong. ALSO: the corpus count is settled at FIVE readable of 45 (mt-transport re-measured; my 3 predated my own two new specs, 3+2=5, we agree exactly). Their remark worth keeping: they made the identical mistake the tool makes — non-empty result read as correct result — while confirming the tool makes it. Twice in one hour, so it is not a hard trap to fall into."}
