2026-07-26 13:58:22,217 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "Stop the service guessing a device's heartbeat when the device has already told us, and stop a wrong guess being permanent.\n\nBoth units reported beat:900 in their own status replies. The API reported 894526 (GARG) and 335061 (BNCH), both measured, both wrong, with slp null on both.\n\nTwo faults:\n1. beat/slp were extracted ONLY on the fast path — the synchronous return of timing.enqueue. A unit deaf ~99% of the time answers late, settling via _onEvent -> settleByReplyId, which touched neither. The authoritative value was reachable only by the route the deployed unit almost never takes.\n2. The seed took the FIRST gap unguarded, so a missed beat locked the estimate at 2x and the tolerance band then rejected every correct gap forever. No escape hatch.\n\nConsequence: nextWake up to 15 minutes wrong, so the butler fires commands into a window where the unit is deaf."}
2026-07-26 13:58:32,662 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Spec: docs/history/beat-seed-unguarded.md (attached). Commit e2596ee.\n\n1. index.js — _learnFromReply(id, reply) extracts slp/beat; called from command() (fast) AND _onEvent (slow).\n2. model.js — seed requires TWO AGREEING GAPS (beat stays null until then). RESEED_AFTER=3 consecutive rejected gaps that agree with each other but not with the held beat overturn it. One outlier changes nothing. beatSource 'device' still untouchable by measurement.\n3. devices.js — blocks 2e (replay GARG's real cadence), 2f (re-seed from a deliberately wrong seed), 2g (_learnFromReply), 2h (the _onEvent WIRING).\n\nMEASURED: replay of GARG's real recorded cadence — old code 1800000, new code 900000. Live bench 335061/measured/null -> 900000/device/0. devices.js 52 -> 68 assertions. Suite 19/19.\n\n2h EXISTS BECAUSE PETER PUSHED. 2g calls _learnFromReply directly, so it would have passed with _onEvent never wired to it — a thing that exists and is never reached, the same defect one level up. Verified by deleting the _onEvent call and confirming the test fails.\n\nNOT FIXED, recorded: heard() is still fed every transmission, not just heartbeats, so a unit that never answers still has only a conflated measurement to go on. Device-reported now wins, which mitigates it; it does not solve it.\n\nDEFERRED: A1/A2 live GARG. Requests ms1skuet.2 (status) and ms1saegu.1 (ping) queued; a background watcher will report when beatSource flips to 'device'. Confirmatory only."}
