2026-07-26 14:23:02,283 70497 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "The GARG panel rendered one coherent-looking row — 2.5 km / RSSI -36 dBm / SNR +6.0 / HOPS 0 — whose halves came from different radios and different packets. Peter was using it to judge a YAGI cable repair, and it said direct-and-excellent when the real direct measurement was -128 dBm at the noise floor. Opposite conclusions.\n\nRaised by mt-transport (xsession [garg-panel-mixed-source]) with an independent physics check: -36 dBm direct over 2.501 km is impossible — 868 MHz FSPL is ~99 dB, so 22 dBm TX with ~9 dBi both ends gives about -59 dBm as the best conceivable direct reading.\n\nGoal: make a node's displayed signal provably describe ONE reception by ONE radio, so the row can no longer be internally contradictory."}
2026-07-26 14:23:17,043 70497 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Three defects, fixed in order of what unblocks what.\n\nSTORAGE (this commit) — signal_history gains rx_device; dedup key becomes\n(num, packet_id, rx_device). Previously (num, packet_id) + INSERT OR IGNORE, so when\nOMNI and YAGI both heard one broadcast the second radio\'s reading was silently dropped\nand the survivor was arbitrary. Verified live: packet 848265232 now stored twice,\nOMNI -20.0 dBm / YAGI -28.0 dBm — an 8 dB antenna A/B that the old key destroyed.\n\nGATE (next task) — persist.js isDirect() tests hop arithmetic only, which mesh-gw has\nnow confirmed (xsession [inbound-relay-attribution], DONE) is unsafe: a relayed packet\nCAN present hop_start - hop_limit == 0. Evidence: 1014 of GARG\'s 8269 hops==0 rows\naverage -39.7 dBm on a link whose physical floor is ~-59; the strong/weak populations\nsplit exactly at -59/-60. The discriminator is relay_node (MeshPacket field 19,\ntop-level, low byte of the relaying node\'s num), observed live at 2/176/176.\nTRAP: mesh-gw serialises with proto3 default-omission, so relay_node is ABSENT when 0 —\nabsent means "not relayed", NOT "unknown". Same omission applies to hop_limit.\nAgreed test: direct iff relay_node absent-or-0 AND (hop_start - hop_limit) == 0, with\nabsent hop_limit treated as 0. Accepts a 1-in-256 low-byte collision that wrongly\nrejects a real direct packet — right side to err on, since the current gate wrongly\nACCEPTS relay traffic and corrupts stored link quality.\n\nDISPLAY (later, splits by domain) — nodes.rssi/snr/device is still one scalar per node,\nlast-writer-wins between the two radios, so the stored pair can describe a different\nradio than the rest of the panel. De-scalarising it changes the read path (Domain 1)\nand then the rendering (Domain 2), which CLAUDE.md forbids combining. Also open:\nhopsField() treats a traceroute of unbounded age as authoritative (GARG\'s is 14 days\nold and outvotes the live value) — ledger #35/#38.\n\nNOT DONE, deliberately: existing signal_history rows are neither backfilled nor purged.\nThey mix true direct and mis-gated relay traffic and nothing distinguishes them;\nbackfilling rx_device would fabricate attribution we do not have.'}
