2026-07-26 14:24:17,282 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Stop a command meant for one unit being shouted at nobody, and stop the resolver depending on a roster that will never carry our units.\n\nA target we could not resolve produced num:null, which _addressed() treated as "broadcast". Three consequences: the packet went out unackable (mesh-gw derives want_ack from having a real destination), the ledger row was filed under the raw string so the butler could never cue it into a wake window, and the caller got an id for a command that would never arrive. Live ledger: one such row, 336b, 0 done.\n\nsendText() and alignPing() already raised ETARGET on exactly this. Only the command path fell through.\n\nNOT a licence to delete the fallback: dm.default:false is an operator choice meaning "always broadcast", with its own declared channel, and it predates PKC DMs. Raise only when DM is the intended mode.'}
2026-07-26 14:24:29,236 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: docs/history/resolve-miss-silent-broadcast.md (attached). Commits cf2784a (services) + 580a213 (mt-alarm docs).\n\n1. resolve.js — resolveTarget(target, roster, extraIds). Roster still wins; extras are a fallback. Short NAMES deliberately unresolvable from ids (config carries `label`, not short_name).\n2. index.js — _knownIds() = cfg.devices ∪ cfg.units ∪ _ours. _resolveOrThrow raises ETARGET only when dm.default !== false. Used by command(), _sendRaw(), _unitKey().\n3. test/resolve.js 8 -> 15, test/dm.js blocks 3/3b/3c, test/cli-live.js fixture + ping assertion.\n4. ../docs/api/http.md — new "Targets" section.\n\nMEASURED: live bench by 4-hex suffix b80f -> pong (was a silent broadcast); unresolvable -> 502 ETARGET, nothing transmitted; \'*\' and dm.default:false still broadcast; suite 19/19.\n\nPETER\'S CALL, and it was the right one: my first version deleted the fallback outright. dm.js block 3 documents it as designed behaviour with a declared knob. Narrowed to "raise only when DM is the intended mode".\n\nTWO FIXTURES WERE PROPPED UP BY THE BUG: cli-live.js declared no devices and only passed because unresolved targets broadcast; its ping asserted a ch2 broadcast where the real service sends an addressed DM.\n\nOUTSTANDING: [command-etarget] raised on the NEW node-dash--services channel (there was none). http.md is NOT BINDING until they ack. Two questions put to them: do they ever send short names as targets (those now fail, and we declined mesh-gw\'s sync_mode:full on their behalf without asking), and do they surface 502 distinctly from 504 (504 = asleep, normal; 502 = never sent, never will be).'}
