2026-07-26 14:53:57,450 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Stop "never arrived" and "arrived, answer lost" being the same observation.\n\nmesh-gw has reported the delivery outcome of every packet this service ever sent. gw.js normalised message_status to {kind:\'status\'} and index.js:_onEvent had no branch for it, so every verdict fell off the end of the function. A failure therefore looked identical whether the command reached the device or not — and on a link where the round trip is ~15 min against a 20 s reply window, those need opposite responses.\n\nRoadmap S1, the highest-value open item, and it needed nothing from anyone: the enum, ordering and packet_id identity guarantee were already settled with mesh-gw on [message-status-semantics].\n\nThe rule that makes it safe: an ack is EVIDENCE, not a state change. queued/trying/done/failed is about the ANSWER; delivery is a separate fact about the same row.'}
2026-07-26 14:54:13,125 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: docs/history/ack-consumption.md (attached). Commits d94d3d1 (services) + 9a5c703 (mt-alarm docs).\n\n1. gw.js — lift error_name/error_reason/res out of raw onto the status event.\n2. db.js — migration 5: ack_state, acked_at, acks, sent_to. Live db v4 -> v5, 224 rows intact.\n3. store.js — persisted in rowToEntry AND the insert, same change (store.js:236\'s warning).\n4. butler.js — TERMINAL_ACK map + ACK_RANK; noteAck() scans by packet id (the status event carries no unit); noteSent() gains toNum.\n5. index.js — the _onEvent \'status\' branch that never existed; onSent passes opts.to (the address ACTUALLY used, null when broadcast).\n\nMEASURED live: ms1usena.0 state=done ackState=delivered acks=["delivered"] sentIds=[1318022095] sentTo=[2558179343]. The row 20 min earlier reads null — no backfill. butler 91 -> 116 assertions, db 45, devices 72, suite 19/19.\n\nVERIFIED THE WIRING BY DISABLING IT: the _onEvent branch test fails when the branch is removed. Lesson carried from beat-seed-unguarded, where the same trap sat one level up. Testing noteAck alone would have passed with the branch still missing.\n\nhost-module.js was in scope and needed NO change — the queue route passes store entries through, so all four fields surfaced for free. Recorded rather than edited to match the spec.\n\nNOT DONE, deliberately: acting on the signal (retry policy, alerting) is a separate change — one change per measurement. And no backfill of the 217 old rows.\n\nOUTSTANDING: node-dash has not acked either http.md change ([command-etarget] the ETARGET break, and the ackState addition). Neither is binding until they do.\n\nNEXT: S2 wake-timed-send. Confirmed with Peter that delivery is currently REACTIVE — index.js:146 \'heard\' -> butler.onHeard -> deliver. There is NO timer at nextWake and no pre-emptive lead time anywhere; nextWake is only reported as nextTryAt and used to gate sending at a radio measured asleep. Note mode.windowMs is 10000 and windowSource is \'assumed\' — S2 must not design a lead time against a window nobody has measured.'}
