2026-07-26 14:58:55,579 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': "B18 CONFIRMED/OPEN — the live model is IN-MEMORY ONLY, so every restart discards beat, beatSource, lastHeardMs and slp. Model (mesh/lib/model.js) holds a plain Map and nothing persists it; _ours is persisted via store.saveDevices but the model is not. Observed today: after each pac-host restart both units read beat=null src=null nextWake=null until re-learned. B2 made this MORE visible, deliberately — seeding now needs TWO agreeing gaps rather than one, so re-learning a 900s beat by measurement takes up to ~30 min instead of ~15. Mitigated but not solved by B2's other half: a single status/config reply carrying beat sets it instantly via beatReported, and that now works on the slow path too. IMPACT ON S2: a pre-emptive wake-timed send cannot engage until the beat is known again, so after a restart delivery silently degrades to the old reactive behaviour for a window or two. NOT FIXED — persisting the model is its own task and its own decision (a persisted beat is a MEASUREMENT that may be stale on reload, which cuts against 'say only what you measured'). Logged so the next session does not mistake a post-restart null for a fault."}
