2026-07-26 15:04:23,006 70497 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'Control page renders a 504 (unit asleep, normal) identically to a 502 ETARGET (never sent, never will be)', 'description': '**Status:** CONFIRMED · **Domain 2 (presentation)** · **Found:** 2026-07-26, raised by `services` (xsession [command-etarget])\n\n`public/app-control.js:52-53` catches any command failure and shows `e.message` in an error\ntoast with `duration 0`. `src/pac-host.js` builds that message as `pac-host <status>: <error>`,\nso the two cases differ in *text* — but get identical styling, identical permanence and\nidentical placement.\n\nThey mean opposite things to a person:\n\n- **504** — the unit did not answer: asleep or out of range. **Normal operation** on this link.\n- **502 ETARGET** — the request was never transmitted and never will be. Nothing is queued,\n  nothing will arrive, and no amount of waiting changes it.\n\nPresenting a routine sleep exactly as alarmingly as a permanent refusal trains the operator to\nignore both.\n\n**Not affected:** the ETARGET change cannot currently fire for node-dash — we only ever send a\nfull `!hex` id via `numToNodeId()` (`src/utils.js:35-37`), never a short name. This is about how\nwe *render* the failure if it ever does, and about 504 being over-alarming today regardless.\n\n**Out of scope for the task that found it** (`direct-gate-relay-node`, backend/Domain 1) —\nCLAUDE.md forbids a fix spanning domains. Needs its own Domain 2 task.'}
