2026-07-26 15:06:59,910 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "Make nextWake a TRIGGER rather than a label.\n\nA command held at a sleeping unit waited for onHeard — the unit's own transmission — so we only began sending after watching the window open, and the watching consumed part of it. nextWake was computed, reported as nextTryAt, and never acted on.\n\nPeter's framing: there is no point sending when we know it is asleep, UNLESS it wakes in the next 10-15 s — that gives it a chance to hear the message on wake, and leaves room to send another while it is up.\n\nThe first half (do not send when asleep) already existed at butler.js:197-203. This adds the second."}
2026-07-26 15:07:16,156 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Spec: docs/history/wake-timed-send.md (attached). Commit 9c9bac9.\n\n1. settings.js / config.yaml / host.config.json — butler.wakeLeadMs 10000, butler.wakeTickMs 2000, declared in all three.\n2. butler.js — _startWakeTick(), _onWakeTick(), _windowImminent(), stop(); the enqueue gate now sends early instead of holding when the window is imminent.\n3. index.js — inject wakeTrusted(unit) (beatSource === 'device'); Mesh.close() calls butler.stop().\n4. test/butler.js — A1, A1b, A2..A7.\n\nMEASURED: butler 116 -> 129 assertions, suite 19/19, live tick 4 CPU ticks/10s across three samples.\n\nFOUR DECISIONS LOGGED IN decisions-for-peter (D2-D5), each with how to reverse it. D3 is the one he is most likely to push back on: pre-firing requires a DEVICE-REPORTED beat, so it is dormant on a measured one.\n\nA1b: added after finding A1 was fake — it passed with the tick's delivery deleted because the enqueue path satisfied it. A1b can only be satisfied by the tick and fails without it. Third instance today of a test that did not test its own claim.\n\nCURRENT STATE: dormant on both units, no device-reported beat since the last restart (B18). Engages when either answers a status. NO reliability improvement claimed — this makes delivery earlier in the window; whether that raises the success rate needs field data.\n\nNEXT after this: B15 (image push give-up guards dead), B16 (chunkAnswerMs dead config), B12 (roadmap/device-behaviour doc corrections), B7 (spec-hash reader — now ours, blocks spec-drift-adjudication)."}
