2026-07-26 15:09:00,252 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'B15 SEVERITY CORRECTED DOWN — I OVERSTATED IT. My original entry said a stuck image push "can retry indefinitely with no terminal state". THAT IS WRONG. images.js:109 sets deadline = now + timing.pushDeadlineMs (900000 = 15 min), images.js:145 loops `while (Date.now() < deadline)`, and images.js:175 throws EDEADLINE on expiry. So a stuck push DOES terminate — after 15 minutes. WHAT IS STILL TRUE AND STILL WORTH FIXING: maxStale and maxUnanswered are genuinely undefined (images.js:63 passes only {idleMs, actMs, quietMs}), so push-receiver.js:203 and :223 compare against undefined and NEVER fire. Their purpose is to give up EARLY and with a SPECIFIC reason — \'stuck: N consecutive repair rounds delivered nothing\' (:204) and \'device unresponsive: N progress queries unanswered\' (:224), both surfaced as EXFER via images.js:157-162. Instead every failure waits the full 15 minutes and reports a generic \'deadline at 47/120\'. COST: up to ~14 minutes of futile REPAIR/PROGRESS_Q airtime on a shared mesh already at ~30% channel utilisation, and a diagnostic that says \'timed out\' where it could say \'the device stopped sending\' or \'the device is not answering\'. So: a real defect about EARLINESS and DIAGNOSIS, not about unboundedness. I told mt-transport it was \'worse than the CPU bug\' — that was based on the same wrong reading and has been corrected to them.'}
