2026-07-26 15:14:23,177 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "D6 — DELETED the config knob timing.chunkAnswerMs rather than finding it a use. It was declared in settings.js, config.yaml and host.config.json, asserted by test/timeouts.js as 'declared and positive', and read by nothing. Its only consumer died in 7c2b5aa when the schema stopped being pulled over the air (`this.schemaTimeoutMs = deps.schemaTimeoutMs || 8000` removed). The chunk path it nominally described has its own declared values, all consumed. Deleting felt right because a knob nobody reads is a lie about what is configurable, and wiring it in would have meant inventing a use to justify keeping it. BUT: it is a removal from a declared surface, and Peter set the rule that every timeout must be configurable — he may prefer it kept and wired, or kept and marked obsolete. Reversing is trivial: re-add the three declarations and the REQUIRED_TIMING entry (commit 8df4f54). NOTE: I did NOT touch pushMaxStale/pushMaxUnanswered, which are also declared-and-unconsumed, because unlike this one they have a live consumer waiting and a real job (B15)."}
