2026-07-26 15:15:54,702 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "B20 CONFIRMED/OPEN — MY OWN BUG, shipped in S1 (d94d3d1) and found within the hour. sentTo is NOT padded, so it misaligns with sentIds on any row that existed before migration 5. Evidence, live row ms1saegu.1: sentIds has 15 entries, acks has 15, sentTo has 3. noteAck pads (butler.js:355 'while (e.acks.length < e.sentIds.length) e.acks.push(null)') but noteSent only pushes one sentTo per NEW transmission (butler.js:324) and never pads for transmissions recorded before the column existed. CONSEQUENCE: sentTo[i] does not correspond to sentIds[i] on any request that spans the change, so the per-attempt address — the whole point of B5, and what makes no_ack_needed interpretable — is unreadable for those rows. NEW rows created after the change are correct. This is exactly the class of defect this session has been fixing all day (an index-aligned pair where only one side is maintained), committed by me. FIX: pad sentTo to sentIds.length in noteSent, and defensively in noteAck, the same way acks is padded. Nothing can be recovered for the 15-entry historical rows — the addresses were never recorded — so they must read null, not a guess."}
2026-07-26 15:16:07,122 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "*** FINDING F1 — S1 ANSWERED THE PROJECT'S BIGGEST OPEN QUESTION WITHIN 90 MINUTES OF SHIPPING. Live row ms1saegu.1, ping to GARG created 13:38, settled 14:53: state=failed, error=no_reply, tries=5/5 — AND ackState=delivered, ackedAt=14:52:40, acks[9]='delivered'. `delivered` means the RECIPIENT ITSELF acked (from_num == to_num), which per mesh-gw's contract is the ONLY proof of arrival. So GARG RECEIVED our ping and did not answer it. Three of the later transmissions (acks[12..14]) came back 'failed' — mesh routing errors — so the link is also genuinely marginal. WHAT THIS RULES OUT: the roadmap says GARG's silence 'could be the device, the downlink, or PKC' and calls it possibly the most important open item. The downlink is now ruled out for at least one attempt: the packet demonstrably reached the device. Attention moves to the device's reply path (the 204-byte status reply has previously been shown undemodulable at snr -17.8 against an SF11 floor of ~-17.5) or the device itself. BEFORE S1 THIS WAS UNOBSERVABLE — a no_reply failure looked identical whether the command arrived or not. This is the first measured reliability insight of the session and it came from the roadmap's own top-priority item."}
2026-07-26 15:16:15,408 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'senttto-not-padded', 'title': 'B20: sentTo is not padded to sentIds, so the per-attempt address misaligns on any row that predates migration 5 — my own bug, shipped in d94d3d1', 'steps': ['Investigate: confirm the asymmetry between acks (padded) and sentTo (not), and what it does to a pre-migration row', 'Document: spec + attach', 'Implement', 'Observe: a pre-migration row must read sentTo aligned and null-filled, never short', 'Track: hash, validate, commit']}
