2026-07-26 15:20:33,724 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "Keep sentTo index-aligned with sentIds. My own defect, shipped in d94d3d1 and found ninety minutes later by reading the live ledger rather than the tests.\n\nnoteAck padded acks; noteSent only appended sentTo. A request carrying sentIds from before migration 5 put its next address at index 0, so the arrays diverged permanently: ms1saegu.1 read sentIds 15 / acks 15 / sentTo 3.\n\nThat is the row that produced finding F1. acks[9]='delivered' and sentTo[9] did not exist, while sentTo[0..2] looked plausible and described different transmissions. A misaligned companion array does not fail loudly — it answers confidently and wrongly."}
2026-07-26 15:20:45,900 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Spec: docs/history/sentto-not-padded.md (attached). Commit 72d685f.\n\nbutler.js — pad BOTH sentTo and acks to sentIds.length in noteSent, and both in noteAck.\nstore.js — rowToEntry pads on every READ, via a padTo() helper that grows but never truncates.\ntest/butler.js — a reloaded row with pre-existing sentIds must come out aligned, with the new address at the NEW index and the unrecorded slots null.\n\nMEASURED: live rows via the API 3-of-3 misaligned -> 0; ms1saegu.1 15/3/15 -> 15/15/15 with acks[9]='delivered' and sentTo[9]=null; butler 129 -> 135 assertions; suite 19/19. Verified by removing the pad and watching the test fail.\n\nTWO THINGS THE WORK FOUND, beyond the spec as written:\n1. acks was ALSO unpadded in noteSent — only noteAck padded it. My own new test caught it.\n2. Padding in the butler CANNOT reach settled rows: mesh.requests() reads store.listRequests directly, bypassing the butler, and a settled row never gets another transmission. rowToEntry is the only place covering every read path. store.js added to scope.\n\nnull is the honest fill — those addresses were never recorded, and back-filling the unit's current num would invent a measurement."}
