2026-07-26 15:36:21,528 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'push-receiver.js takes five values and documents them as "All five come from config. No defaults here". images.js passed three. maxStale and maxUnanswered were undefined, and both give-up guards compare against them, so `99 >= undefined` is false and neither had ever fired.\n\nSEVERITY CORRECTED TWICE, downward. I first recorded this as "no terminal state, retries forever" and told mt-transport so. images.js:109,145,175 bounds the loop with pushDeadlineMs (15 min) and throws EDEADLINE — a stuck push always did terminate.\n\nThe real defect is lateness and diagnosis: every failure waited the full fifteen minutes and reported a generic "deadline at 47/120" instead of naming which side stopped.'}
2026-07-26 15:36:31,647 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: docs/history/push-giveup-guards-dead.md (attached). Commit 30c57de.\n\nimages.js:_startTransfer now passes all five. push-receiver.js UNTOUCHED — both guards were correctly written and correctly placed, they were simply never given thresholds. The bug was at the construction site.\n\nValues 8 and 30 unchanged. push-receiver.js:38-42 argues 30 explicitly: on a lossy link replies are lost too, so a live device looks dead, and aborting a WORKING transfer is far worse than taking ~4 min to notice a genuinely dead one. Hence A5 — one round short of each threshold must NOT abort — which is the assertion that matters most.\n\nMEASURED: maxStale undefined -> 8, maxUnanswered undefined -> 30, both fire at threshold, neither fires early, KNOWN_UNCOUPLED 2 -> 0, images.js 31 -> 36 assertions, suite 19/19.\n\nTHE TEST WAS WRONG FIRST TIME. A1/A2 constructed a PushReceiver directly with explicit values, proving nothing about images.js — verified by deleting the fix and watching them still pass. Rewritten through _startTransfer and confirmed to fail without it. THIRD instance of that trap today (ack-consumption, wake-timed-send, this). The habit of deleting the fix and re-running is now the only thing that has caught it each time.\n\nKNOWN_UNCOUPLED is now EMPTY and the comment says it exists to be driven to zero, never to absorb entries.'}
