2026-07-26 15:38:56,198 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'WORK COMPLETED WHILE AWAY — 6 commits in services, 3 in mt-alarm.\n\n  9c9bac9  S2 wake-timed-send        nextWake becomes a trigger\n  8df4f54  config-values-that-lie    B16 + B19\n  72d685f  sentto-not-padded         B20 — MY OWN bug from S1, found in the live ledger\n  6ba87fa  roadmap-garg-correction   B12 spec\n  2370984  spec-hash-reader          B7 spec\n  30c57de  push-giveup-guards-dead   B15\n  mt-alarm: 4292272 (roadmap + device-behaviour), 6bbdd09 (spec-hash.py), 9a5c703 (http.md ackState)\n\nEVERY code defect in the ledger is now closed: B1 B2 B3 B4 B5 B6 B7 B12 B15 B16 B19 B20. Suite 19/19. Live bench command answers. Working tree clean in both repos.\n\nTHE HEADLINE: F1. S1 answered the roadmap\'s top open question 90 minutes after shipping — ms1saegu.1 failed with no_reply while ackState came back delivered, so GARG RECEIVED the ping and did not answer. The downlink is eliminated; the reply path is the remaining suspect, and mesh-cmd-retry already measured a 204-byte reply as undemodulable at snr -17.8. Device-side to confirm.\n\nSTILL OPEN AND NEEDING PETER OR ANOTHER SESSION:\n  - node-dash has acked NEITHER http.md change ([command-etarget] the ETARGET break, and ackState). Not binding until they do.\n  - spec-drift-adjudication: 167 drifted files across 40 specs now VISIBLE and needing adjudication. mt-transport\'s 7/1 attribution is verified WRONG and must not be used.\n  - B17: the device drift baseline is unmeasured, not zero. Device session\'s to re-measure.\n  - B11: dev/CLAUDE.md still lists trial-logger as a separate service. Nobody owns it.\n  - B18: the model is in-memory, so beat/slp are lost on every restart. Not fixed — persisting a measurement that may be stale on reload cuts against "say only what you measured", and that is Peter\'s call.\n  - GARG has not answered since 13:37. S2 is dormant for it (no device-reported beat); ENGAGED