2026-07-26 17:46:20,120 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "B22 CONFIRMED/OPEN — NOTHING IN THE SYSTEM SHOWS OUTBOUND TRAFFIC. Peter watched node-dash's message feed and stated flatly that no messages had been sent to GARG in six hours; I had ledger rows saying otherwise; NEITHER of us could settle it from any API. It took journalctl on mesh-gw. MEASURED: (a) node-dash /messages -> queryMessages (src/index.js:142) -> SELECT FROM messages (src/filters.js:22) <- INSERT only for portnum==='TEXT_MESSAGE_APP' on a RECEIVED packet via stmts.insertRxMessage (src/persist.js:313-319). No code path records an outbound send. (b) mesh-gw /events suppresses our own TX echo by packet id (their ble_device.py:2361, by design and correct). (c) mesh-gw GET /{gwId}/messages returned 7 messages, ALL with rx_time/rx_snr/rx_rssi, from_num all 2558179343, our gateway 646426545 appearing ZERO times; openapi shows only a since_id param, no direction filter. So the ONLY outbound record anywhere is pac-host's own ledger (sentIds/sentTo/acks), which has existed since 2026-07-26 afternoon. Any consumer of the mesh that is not us is blind to its own sends. Raised as [outbound-invisible] with node-dash and [outbound-not-retrievable] with mesh-gw; ownership not yet agreed. NOTE Peter's observation was CORRECT and my reading of it was wrong — 'the feed shows no sends' is not evidence that nothing was sent, because the feed has never shown sends at all."}
2026-07-26 17:46:34,786 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "B23 CONFIRMED/OPEN — OUR ledger records ack OUTCOMES but not evidence of TRANSMISSION, and that is my design decision from S1. In ack-consumption I classified sent/queued/relayed as 'progress, not outcome' and recorded NONE of them, on the reasoning that 'relayed' is an intermediate hop and not arrival. That reasoning is right about what relayed MEANS and wrong about whether it is worth keeping: it is the only evidence available to us that a packet reached the air. mesh-gw's log holds all three per packet — 'send_text_message ... sent' (BLE write), 'queued pkt_id=...' (the RADIO accepted it, res==0), 'routing_ack ... relayed' (it was transmitted) — and we throw all three away, keeping only the terminal verdict. CONSEQUENCE: when Peter asked 'was anything sent', our own ledger could show him no_ack/delivered but could NOT show that a transmission occurred, so I fell back on POST 200 OK (proves only that mesh-gw accepted a submission — he correctly rejected it) and on 'relayed from=!2687afb1', which I described as 'a node relayed it' when !2687afb1 is OUR OWN GATEWAY, i.e. a self-report, not corroboration. PROPOSED FIX: record sent/queued/relayed per packet alongside acks, so 'we transmitted it' becomes evidence rather than an assertion. Blocked pending the ownership answer on B22 — if mesh-gw exposes transmissions properly, this may be satisfied upstream instead."}
