2026-07-27 09:34:17,392 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'send-receive-timing', 'title': 'Analyse message send and receive timing end-to-end — every clock in the chain, and how far each one is actually trusted', 'steps': ['Investigate: name every clock in the chain and where each is measured — enqueue, butler lead time, gateway handoff, air time, device RX, device wake phase. State which are measured, which are inferred, and which are assumed.', 'B44: err_ms is the FIRST DIFFERENCE of the gap, not a prediction error against a stable beat. model.js:133 sets beat = gap, so one noisy sample predicts another and the errors add in quadrature. Quantify: collect >=10 consecutive gaps and compute the standard deviation of the gap itself vs the standard deviation of its first difference. Prediction should be tested against the CONVERGED beat.', 'Decide the estimator. agrees()/beatRejects already detect a genuine beat change, so an AGREEING gap can be averaged over a window without reintroducing the EMA lag that B38/B41 removed. Compare: single sample (today), damped EMA (pre-B41), windowed mean/median over agreeing gaps. Choose on measured variance, not preference.', 'Establish the anchor->wake offset. nextWake predicts the ANCHOR (first frame arriving at the gateway), not the wake instant; the ~2.1 s offset between them rests on ONE observation. BLOCKED: needs the CH34x tap (1a86:55d4) passed through to the VM.', 'Measure when a pre-wake-queued command actually lands on the device, in ms into the wake window. Method needs no flash: host-stamp the RX: line (main.cpp:4118) and the SLEEPNOW line, wake_start = sleepnow_stamp - awake_ms. Resolution is limited by USB buffering to tens of ms; a millis() added to the RX line would make it exact but needs a flash.', 'Spec and implement the chosen estimator. Acceptance: mean |err| over >=10 comparable wakes, measured from wake_log, against the 100 ms target. One change per measurement.']}
2026-07-27 09:35:48,282 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': "B44 CONFIRMED/OPEN — the wake predictor uses the single previous gap as the beat, so err_ms is the FIRST DIFFERENCE of the gap and our prediction error is ~2x the device's actual jitter", 'description': '**Where:** `mesh/lib/model.js:133` — `beat = gap;`\n\n**Evidence (measured, unit !987ab80f, 5-minute beat, fw 2-260727-90):**\n\n```\ngap:  300014  300017  299977  300059  299971\nerr:      —      +3     -40     +82     -88\n```\n\n`err_ms` equals `gap_n - gap_(n-1)` on every single row, exactly, three times over\n(-40, +82, -88). It is not a prediction error against a stable beat; it is the first\ndifference of a noisy series.\n\n```\nsd(gap deviation from 300000)   31.8 ms\nsd(first difference)            62.5 ms     ratio 1.97\nmean |err| as shipped           53 ms\nmean |err| vs a stable beat     28 ms\n```\n\n**Cause, and it is mine.** Fixing B38/B41 I replaced the damped EMA\n(`beat * 0.75 + gap * 0.25`) with `beat = gap`. The EMA was genuinely wrong — it lagged\na real beat change by ~1.5 s (measured: gap 901160, beat in use 899634). But a single\nsample predicting another single sample adds the two noises in quadrature. I fixed lag\nby importing variance and did not notice, because both estimators stay inside the 100 ms\ntarget and nothing was measuring the difference.\n\n**Why the fix is not a revert.** `agrees()` and the `beatRejects` machinery already\ndetect a genuine beat change and relearn through a separate path. So a gap that AGREES\ncan safely be averaged over a window without reintroducing the lag that B41 removed —\nthe two concerns were conflated in one assignment.\n\n**NOT yet known:** the magnitude of err has grown on every sample so far (3, 40, 82, 88)\nwith n=4. The gaps themselves show no trend, so this reads as noise, but it is recorded\nas unresolved rather than dismissed. Needs >=10 consecutive gaps.\n\n**Separately, not this bug:** `nextWake` predicts the ANCHOR (first frame arriving at the\ngateway), not the wake instant. The ~2.1 s offset between them rests on ONE observation\nand is currently unmeasurable — the CH34x tap (1a86:55d4) is not passed through to the VM.\n\n**Tracked by:** task `send-receive-timing` (764), steps 2, 3 and 6. Acceptance is\nmean |err| over >=10 comparable wakes from `wake_log`, against the 100 ms target.'}
