2026-07-27 09:43:02,388 64308 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'tap-rx-console', 'kind': 'note', 'text': '2026-07-27 — the Espressif adapter is NOT the RAK debug tap. Measured, not assumed.\n\nCaptured /dev/serial/by-id/usb-Espressif_USB_JTAG_serial_debug_unit_64:E8:33:86:1F:74-if00\nfrom 09:22:43 across THREE full wake windows (09:23:54, 09:28:54, 09:33:53).\nResult: 1 line — the logger\'s own "---- attached ----" marker. Zero bytes from the device.\n\nThe device WAS transmitting during that window: Serial2.begin(115200) at main.cpp:3226,\ng_sleepDbg on, and the mesh confirms all three wakes happened (wake_log gaps 299977,\n300059, 299971). So this is not a sleeping or silent device — the adapter is not wired to\nthe pin Serial2 transmits on.\n\nNote the earlier related error, so it is not repeated: Serial2 RX was pointed at WB_IO2,\nwhich is P0.34 = the 3V3_S rail enable (RAK-documented). That was reverted. TX remains on\ngpio 17.\n\nCURRENT BLOCKER for device-side timing work: the CH34x tap (1a86:55d4,\n/dev/serial/by-id/usb-1a86_USB_Single_Serial_5B1F007437-if00) is NOT passed through to this\nVM — only 239a:8029 (RAK app CDC, blocked as a DTR hazard) and 303a:1001 are present.\nWithout the CH34x there is no device-side serial visibility at all, which blocks\nsend-receive-timing (764) steps 4 and 5.'}
