2026-07-27 19:38:47,198 175346 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "Make the wake detector resolve every wake at any supported beat, and stop it attributing its own blind spot to the device.\n\nThe detector counts a frame as a NEW wake only after burstGapMs of silence. That was a fixed 120 s, chosen when the only unit ran a 900 s beat. Below ~120 s the reasoning inverts: consecutive real wakes fall inside the previous wake's burst window, never re-anchor, and the resulting ~2x gaps overwrite a correct stated beat. It is silent — no error, just fewer rows and a note blaming the device.\n\nSuccess is a RATIO measured against the recorder CSV, which has no schedule logic in its path and therefore cannot share the detector's blind spot: wake_log records >=90% of the bursts the recorder shows arriving, at a 60 s beat. Baseline 2 of 6 (33%)."}
2026-07-27 19:38:53,894 175346 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': '1. burstGapMs becomes a CEILING, not a fixed value: effective threshold = min(burstGapMs, beat * burstGapFraction), with burstGapFraction declared at 0.25. Burst span scales with what a wake DOES (the 59 s burst that motivated 120 s carried a command reply at a 900 s beat; the burst at a 60 s beat is ~1 s), so a fraction tracks it and a constant cannot.\n\n2. BOOTSTRAP: the above needs a beat, and there is none at model start — every restart. Add burstGapBootstrapMs, used only while the beat is unknown. Its value is DERIVED: it must sit below minBeatMs (20 s), the shortest beat accepted, so it can never merge two wakes of any supported schedule. 15000. The error is one-sided — too large silently doubles the beat; too small only splits a burst into sub-minBeatMs gaps, which the gap test already discards.\n\n3. The long-gap note states the observation and the threshold in force, and names no cause. Frames that were in fact received were being reported as "missed wakes or reboot?", which sent the investigation to the wrong component.\n\n4. Purge wake_log and node_state before measuring: the debug module seeds from storage at start, so old-estimator rows feed back into the new model. Back up first.\n\n5. Verify against the FAILURE as well as the fix — the same wakes with the bootstrap value absent must still alias, or the test proves nothing.'}
