2026-07-27 19:58:25,157 175346 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'wake-model-backfill', 'title': 'Seed the wake model from the RECORDER on start, so a restart does not blind the scheduler for 45 minutes on a 900 s unit', 'steps': ['Investigate: the recorder CSV schema and what the model needs. Establish exactly which columns map to model.heard() arguments (utc, from_id, port, hop_limit, hop_start), and confirm the recorder is ours (trial-logger/recorder.js, loaded by pac-host, dataDir device/data).', 'Decide the WINDOW and the FILTERS. Too long a window replays a stale schedule (GARG ran 300 s earlier today then 900 s); too short and a 900 s unit gets too few samples. Only direct arrivals, only anchor ports, only declared units (B47: wake_log holds 82 foreign nodes).', "Implement mesh/lib/backfill.js and call it at start, replaying in time order through model.heard(). beatSource must stay 'measured' — a replayed observation is evidence, never a device statement.", 'Acceptance, a number: TIME-TO-FIRST-BEAT after a restart for a 900 s unit. Today it is ~45 min (three 900 s gaps). Target: a beat within 1% of 900000 present within 60 s of start, measured from /v1/mesh/devices.', 'Verify the backfill cannot INVENT a schedule: replay a period containing the 300->900 s change and confirm the estimator does not adopt a blended value. A wrong beat delivered instantly is worse than a right one delivered late.', 'Track: relationship to wake-state-persistence (B31). node_state persistence restores CONCLUSIONS; this replays raw OBSERVATIONS through current code. Record which one wins and why, rather than leaving two mechanisms that disagree.']}
