2026-07-27 20:01:35,716 70497 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter, 2026-07-27: "this issue needs fixing, I have reported it several times but nothing seems to have been done."\n\nA remote node displays a strong RSSI — looking metres away — because the last hop was relayed by one of our own two radios (OMNI/YAGI, same house). The envelope\'s rx_rssi describes the link to the RELAY, not to the origin node, so a 2.5 km node inherits a room-distance reading.\n\nReported repeatedly. Bug ledger #16 opened 2026-07-18, marked complete at 14:45:42 and reverted six seconds later. persist.js:80-88 still carries the note from that attempt ("462 of 977 stored samples (47%)... the reported twitching between -1XX and -33"). The gate it added tested hop arithmetic only, which cannot detect a relay — so the record said fixed while the symptom continued. That is why it has kept coming back.'}
2026-07-27 20:01:51,702 70497 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'SHIPPED 4340f56 — isDirectPacket() gates on relay_node (MeshPacket field 19, inside data.packet, low byte of the relaying node). Proto3 default-omission: absent == 0 == not relayed, never "unknown". Typed events (position/user/telemetry) carry no relay_node so they no longer write signal at all; nothing lost, every reception with signal also arrives as a `packet` event (sampled: 12 packet-only, 2 paired, zero typed-only).\n\nWHAT IS PROVEN\n- The phenomenon is real and captured: GARG at 2.5 km heard at -45 dBm relayed by YAGI (relay_node 0xB4). Free-space best case on that path is about -59 dBm.\n- The mechanism is confirmed by mesh-gw: a relayed packet CAN present hop_start - hop_limit == 0.\n\nWHAT IS NOT PROVEN — do not let this be marked fixed on the strength of the commit\n- Over ~160 sampled live packets the dangerous variant (relayed AND arithmetic 0) did not occur once. Every relayed packet observed was already rejected by the old arithmetic gate.\n- So this commit closes a real hole but is NOT demonstrated to be what put strong readings on distant nodes.\n- My earlier claim that 12% of stored samples were mis-gated relay traffic was WRONG and is retracted: GARG\'s strong readings are episodic (62/62 on 17 Jul, none 19-22 Jul across 6933 rows, then a block 23-25 Jul), which fits the unit being physically near the gateway, not a continuous gate defect.\n\nLIKELIER REMAINING CAUSE — bug ledger #34, still open\nnodes.rssi/snr freeze at the last direct value with no staleness bound. A strong reading taken while a unit was nearby persists indefinitely once it goes relay-only. That survives this fix untouched and is the next thing to check against the live symptom.\n\nALSO UNRESOLVED, NO OWNER\nOMNI and YAGI rebroadcast for each other — two antennas in one house, so a relayed copy adds no coverage, costs airtime, and produces exactly the room-distance last-hop reading. Raised by mt-transport; Peter\'s view is they should reject relays from each other. node-dash has no lever on rebroadcast config. Needs logging and raising with mesh-gw.'}
