2026-07-27 21:05:46,575 70497 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter, 2026-07-27: "Traceroute is continuous no matter whether in PASV or ACTV mode. this is wrong. Traceroute needs to be enabled / disabled manually and persist its state. the button needs to be in the header."\n\nRoot cause is not one dispatcher ignoring the mode — each mode has its OWN automatic dispatcher, so switching mode swaps the trigger instead of stopping it:\n  PASV  passive-tracer.js  — every qualifying heard packet\n  ACTV  lifecycle.js       — rotator.on(\'point_target\')\n  SCAN  lifecycle.js       — scanner.on(\'contact\')\nThere was no mode in which traceroute was off, and no config key gated any of it (verified: only `pasv_config` timings existed). Measured rate while enabled: 8 dispatches in 10 minutes, 25 in 30.\n\nDOMAIN SPLIT (CLAUDE.md forbids one task spanning domains):\n  This task = Domain 1, the persisted gate.\n  The header button = Domain 2, separate task, opened once this lands.'}
2026-07-27 21:06:00,976 70497 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Config key `traceroute.enabled` (config-api DEFAULTS, default TRUE so deploying changes nothing until switched off). Gated inside `traceroute.dispatch()` — the single chokepoint every caller passes through — so a future caller cannot bypass it. Checked BEFORE the cooldown guard, or a gated dispatch would burn the cooldown slot and re-enabling would skip the next attempt. `manual: true` (traceroute-api) is never gated.\n\n`passive-tracer` also returns early on `!tracerouteEnabled()`. NOT redundant: its dispatch `.catch` calls `_failed.set()` and emits an empty `traced`, so a gated dispatch arriving as a rejection would mark every skipped node FAILED and push bogus empty routes to the browser. The two lifecycle sites use `.catch(() => {})` and need nothing.\n\nEVIDENCE (measured 2026-07-27, not recalled)\n- Gate is REACHED, not merely present. Same call, flag flipped:\n    enabled=false -> rejected "traceroute disabled"\n    enabled=true  -> rejected "timeout !987ab80f"  (transmitted)\n- Manual bypass live with the switch off: POST /!987ab80f/traceroute returned "timeout", not "traceroute disabled".\n- Disabled window 422s: exactly 3 traceroute_history rows, ALL attributed, none automatic —\n    19:59:23 to 2946046543  in-flight carryover (60s timeout => dispatched ~19:58:23, 13s BEFORE the 19:58:36 disable)\n    19:59:54 to 2558179343  my manual curl test\n    20:00:14 to 2558179343  my gate-test enabled=true probe\n  No new rows after 20:00:14.\n- Regression: GET /traceroute_history serves; GET /config returns 20 keys incl. traceroute.enabled.\n- check_specs: 70 checked / 70 spec files on disk, all four touched modules explicitly ok.\n\nNOT COVERED, recorded in the bug ledger\nThe [V1] LEGACY paths behind FF.SSOT_TRACEROUTE (passive-tracer.js, lifecycle.js) post to the bridge directly, bypassing dispatch() and therefore this gate. Dormant — FF.SSOT_TRACEROUTE is true. Separate task to remove.\n\nSIDE OBSERVATION, NOT CAUSED BY THIS CHANGE\nEvery traceroute in this period returns status `timeout`, including a manual one to a nearby node. Pre-existing; worth its own investigation.\n\nLEFT LIVE AS: traceroute.enabled = false. Automatic traceroute is currently OFF.'}
