2026-07-27 22:17:20,664 175346 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'config-map-completeness', 'title': 'The device advertises 21 config fields and services can write 6 — the other 15 fail ENOMAP after being offered to consumers', 'steps': ['Investigate: diff the generated schema against COMMAND_MAP in mesh/lib/config.js for every field. Establish for each unmapped field whether a text verb ALREADY exists (beat->interval, slp->sleepmode, rx.win->window are known), whether one exists but is unmapped, or whether the firmware has no verb at all. Those are three different problems and only the last one needs the device session.', 'Decide what the API does about a field it cannot write. Today the schema offers 21 and 15 throw ENOMAP on write — a promise populated by nothing, which is the failure class this project exists to prevent. Options: mark writability in the schema response, or refuse to advertise an unwritable field. node-dash renders its form from this, so the choice is a CONTRACT change and needs their ack.', 'Map every field that has a working verb. Each needs read (needsCurrent/readVerb) plus write plus a confirm predicate — the confirm is what makes a set verifiable rather than hopeful.', "Raise with the device session ONLY the fields that have no verb at all, as a firmware request. Do not guess which those are — step 1 establishes it from the firmware's own command table.", 'Acceptance, a number: writable fields go from 6 of 21 to N of 21, and a round-trip test sets and confirms each mapped field against the bench unit. State N before writing code.', 'Track: check docs/api/http.md tells the truth about which fields are writable, and announce the contract change to node-dash on the cross-session channel.']}
2026-07-27 22:40:22,986 175346 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'hop-zero-direct', 'title': 'FIRMWARE: hop override cannot express 0, so direct-only is unreachable — 0 is overloaded as the off sentinel', 'steps': ['Investigate: DONE. MeshtasticTransport.h:360 `_hopOverride = 0` means off; .cpp:211 `if (_hopOverride) hopLimit = _hopOverride;` so a forced 0 is indistinguishable from no override. packFlags(hopLimit, hopLimit) sets hop_start = hop_limit at origin, so an override of n yields n/n and every relay decrements from there.', 'Implement: separate the VALUE from the IS-SET flag. `hop` reports, `hop off` clears, `hop 0..7` forces — with 0 meaning genuine direct-only (no relay).', 'Verify on the BENCH over serial: `hop 0` then confirm outbound frames carry hop_start=0, and that the recorder shows no relayed copies of them.', 'Track: GARG is deployed and cannot be reflashed, so bench and remote firmware will be OUT OF SYNC until the next site visit. The version string makes that visible.']}
