2026-07-28 07:23:57,124 175346 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'B63 CONFIRMED — the pre-empt path fires DURING an open window, so a "pre-wake" send can actually be an in-window send', 'description': 'Found 2026-07-28 during nextwake-current-cycle Phase 1. Not fixed — outside that task\'s scope.\n\n`butler._windowImminent` (mesh/lib/butler.js:129-135) returns true when\n\n    at - now <= wakeLeadMs && at - now > -wakeLeadMs\n\nand `at` comes from `_nextWake`, which can return the wake ALREADY IN PROGRESS (a few ms in the\nfuture — that is the nextwake-current-cycle defect). So during an open window `at - now` is ~0,\nthe test passes, and `_onWakeTick` logs\n\n    butler: <unit> — window imminent in <n> ms, sending EARLY rather than waiting to hear it\n\nfor a window that is not imminent but already open. The unit\'s own `heard` event also fires\n`onHeard -> _deliverNext(unit,\'window\')` for that same window.\n\nPROBABLY BENIGN, WHICH IS NOT THE SAME AS HARMLESS: `_onWakeTick` skips a unit already in\n`this.inflight` (butler.js:111), so the two paths cannot transmit concurrently for one unit. No\nduplicate transmission has been observed.\n\nWHAT IS WRONG ANYWAY: the log line asserts a cause it has not established — the same class of\ndefect as B53. "sending EARLY" describes a pre-emption that did not happen, and it does so in\nexactly the logs used to judge whether pre-emption works, i.e. it corrupts the evidence for\nwake-preempt-value.\n\nNOT VERIFIED: whether any historical "pre-wake" fire was in fact an in-window send. That needs\nthe log line correlated against the wake anchor, and would change how the existing pre-empt\ncounts are read.'}
2026-07-28 07:24:07,168 175346 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'B64 CONFIRMED — wakesDirect is computed in the model but published nowhere, so the direct-fraction behind a phase estimate is invisible', 'description': 'Found 2026-07-28 during nextwake-current-cycle Phase 1. Not fixed — outside that task\'s scope.\n\n`model.heard` maintains `wakesDirect` (mesh/lib/model.js), the count of DIRECT arrivals in the\ncurrent phase window. It was added on 2026-07-27 with an explicit justification: relayed arrivals\nare now admitted into the phase estimate, so the estimate\'s quality depends on how many of its\nsamples were direct — a window of all-relayed samples is biased by relay delay, one containing a\ndirect sample is not.\n\nThe devices route publishes `phase` and `phaseSamples` (mesh/index.js:513-514) and NOT\n`wakesDirect`. Verified live 2026-07-28 06:5x: GET /v1/mesh/devices for !987ab80f returns\n`wakesDirect: None` — the key is absent, not null.\n\nSo the field exists, is maintained, and cannot be read by any consumer. That is the same defect\nclass the code comment itself warns about two lines above — "a prediction whose input is\ninvisible cannot be trusted or debugged" — and it was introduced in the very change that wrote\nthat comment.\n\nMatters now because the deployed unit\'s direct fraction moved 21% -> 57% overnight after the\n`hop 1` cap, and that is exactly the quantity this field measures. It had to be recomputed from\nthe recorder CSV by hand instead of being read from the API.'}
