2026-07-28 08:14:20,741 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'B49 SEVERITY RAISED — "two configs" was filed as small housekeeping; it silently invalidated a whole night\'s radio experiment', 'description': 'Raised 2026-07-28 08:10 under the ledger rule that a finding proven worse than first recorded must have its severity raised explicitly, never quietly.\n\nORIGINAL RATING, in wake-preempt-performance.md:745 —\n\n    | bug ledger (no task) | small housekeeping | B49 two configs, B50 orphan `requests.db`, Q9 |\n\nSame family as B19, also found early: "the code\'s DEFAULT config-schema path points at the\nABANDONED old tree, and the two copies differ… host/host.config.json overrides."\n\nWHAT IT ACTUALLY COST, measured 2026-07-28 07:5x:\n\npac-host loads `host/host.config.json` — its own log says so on every start:\n\n    INFO config: /usr/share/pac/dev/projects/mt-alarm/services/host/host.config.json\n\n`mesh/config.yaml` is the CLI\'s config and is NOT read by the host. On 2026-07-27 ~21:50 I\nchanged `gw.gatewayId` in `mesh/config.yaml` from the omni to the yagi, restarted, and reported\nthat we were transmitting on the yagi. We were not. Proven on the wire:\n\n    POST /%212687afb1/messages   ->  E9:B0:3F:17:27:91   = THE OMNI\n\nConsequences, all of which were reported to Peter as fact:\n  - "switched to the yagi" — never happened; the yagi has still never been tested\n  - a `status` delivery credited to the yagi was actually the omni\n  - the revert to the omni was equally a no-op\n  - the `az 91 -> 14` rotator movement was used to invalidate a trial that was never on that\n    antenna, so that analysis was irrelevant too\n  - two commit messages assert the switch happened\n\nWHY THE RATING WAS WRONG: "two configs" reads as tidiness. It is not. One file is authoritative\nand the other is INDISTINGUISHABLE FROM IT at a glance — same keys, same shapes, same values —\nso editing the wrong one produces no error, no warning, and a service that keeps running exactly\nas before while reporting success. That is the silent-failure class this project has been burned\nby repeatedly, not housekeeping.\n\nSTATUS: CONFIRMED, HIGH. Fix is tracked in its own task (config-single-source): establish what\nstill consumes mesh/config.yaml (the mtmesh CLI does — mesh/index.js:44 "defaults < config.yaml <\nenv < opts"), migrate anything the host needs, remove or neuter the duplicate, and make the docs\nname the loaded file. Do NOT simply delete it before establishing the CLI\'s dependency.'}
2026-07-28 08:14:37,522 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'config-single-source', 'title': 'B49 HIGH: two interchangeable-looking configs, one of them dead under pac-host — remove the duplicate and make the docs name the loaded file', 'steps': ['Investigate: establish exactly who reads mesh/config.yaml (settings.js loader, mtmesh CLI, tests) and whether anything still needs it. Diff it field-by-field against host.config.json modules.mesh so nothing is lost on removal. Do NOT delete before this is answered.', 'Document: spec listing every field that differs, where each one goes, and what happens to the CLI.', 'Implement: migrate anything the host needs, then remove or neuter the duplicate so editing it cannot silently do nothing.', 'Observe: prove on the wire which radio a send uses (mesh-gw log shows POST /{node_id}/messages), and that the CLI either still works or is explicitly retired.', 'Track: fix every doc that names config.yaml as the place to change settings, including CLAUDE.md and docs/api/http.md if they do.']}
