2026-07-28 08:20:56,800 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_switch args={'name': 'config-single-source'}
2026-07-28 08:21:06,585 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'One config, not two. mesh/config.yaml sat beside the live host/host.config.json with the same keys and plausible values, and pac-host never read it — so an edit to it produced no error, no warning, and a service that carried on exactly as before while reporting success.\n\nThat is B49, originally filed as "small housekeeping". It silently invalidated a whole night\'s radio experiment: gw.gatewayId was changed omni -> yagi in the dead file, the switch was reported as done, and the wire showed POST /%212687afb1/messages on the omni throughout.\n\nSuccess: the duplicate is gone, no doc points a human at it, the ECONFIG message names the file that is actually loaded, and the service still transmits — proven on the wire, not inferred from config.'}
2026-07-28 08:21:12,074 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': '1. Establish who reads it before deleting anything. Answer: only the superseded mtmesh CLI (docs/api/http.md:16 — "pac-host replaced the separate mtmesh and trial-logger"). Under the host, settings.js:244 takes the injected object and does not touch the disk, deliberately.\n\n2. Diff field-by-field so nothing is lost. Nine keys existed only in the yaml; all dead defaults except units.*.mode, which is DROPPED not migrated — host.config.json has units:{} so it never applied, and unitMode() derives from the device\'s own slp. Migrating it would pin a physical fact from a config file (B30/wake-gate-removal).\n\n3. Delete the file; fix mesh/index.js\'s ECONFIG message, which pointed at it.\n\n4. Prove on the wire which radio a send uses, rather than reading config back to myself.\n\nDONE 2026-07-28 08:2x. 22 suites pass, commit be83790, pushed. Live send observed as\nPOST /%212687afb1/messages on E9:B0:3F — still the omni, unchanged and intended.'}
