2026-07-28 08:25:07,309 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'DELIBERATELY LEFT OPEN 2026-07-28 08:26, despite all five steps being complete.\n\nAcceptance 3 is "zero one-beat errors across >=30 consecutive wakes, with the median unchanged". That needs a night of GARG wakes at 900 s and has NOT been measured. The code is committed (6e47034), the unit test proves the fix is reached (reverting it fails with the exact defect), and 22 suites pass — but none of that is the acceptance.\n\nClosing now would record a pass I have not measured, which is the specific thing this workflow exists to stop.\n\nBASELINE to compare against, measured 2026-07-28 07:07 over 33 wakes on GARG:\n  median |err| 68 ms, 26 of 33 within 1 s, and ONE error of 901129 ms.\n\nTO CLOSE: re-run the same query after a night —\n  curl "http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1/debug/wakes?unit=!987ab80f&limit=40"\nand confirm no |err| near one beat (900000 +- a few seconds), with the median still ~tens of ms.\n\nNOTE the confound: pac-host has restarted several times since, and the gateway moved to the yagi at 08:23, so the wake sample restarts from there. Count only wakes after the last restart.'}
