2026-07-28 09:38:27,677 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'STEP 5 (docs/api/http.md + node-dash announce) LEFT OPEN DELIBERATELY, 2026-07-28 09:38.\n\nSteps 1-4 are done and committed:\n  device 60ab3ce  gen_schema emits device-api.yaml (30 verbs + 21 fields), generated每 build\n  services ede0656  api-parity test + api-coverage + EVERB guard at the boundary\n  services 1edc764  11 fields wired, 6 -> 17 of 21\n\nStep 5 is NOT done and must not be marked so. Two reasons, both requiring someone else:\n\n1. Publishing the verb surface in docs/api/http.md is a CONTRACT change. The repo rule is explicit:\n   "A change to anything in docs/api/ is not binding until the other party has acked it there."\n   node-dash is the consumer and has not been asked.\n\n2. Routing config writes through the butler (B67) would change POST /v1/mesh/config/:target from\n   synchronous to queued — also a contract change, also node-dash\'s to ack. Without it the 11\n   newly-wired fields are reachable in principle and unreliable in practice on a sleeping unit.\n\nWHAT REMAINS BLOCKED ON THE DEVICE SESSION, not on us:\n  B66 — det.n, mute, push.auto are advertised writable by the firmware\'s own generated schema and\n  have no verb at all. mute is the worst: a LIVE setting (main.cpp:2286 gates the PIR startup\n  lockout on it) that nothing can change. Three dispositions offered in the ledger; option 2\n  (mark them writable:false, as txp already is) costs nothing and makes the schema honest.\n\nWHAT IS NOW SELF-ENFORCING, which was the point: a verb added to the firmware turns\nmesh/test/api-parity.js red until someone decides about it. Verified by injecting a synthetic verb\nand watching it fail. That no longer depends on anyone remembering.'}
