2026-07-28 09:45:24,562 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'LEDGER SWEEP 2026-07-28 09:45 — closing B46, B49, B65 with evidence; B60 is DUPLICATED at steps 39 and 40', 'description': 'Peter, 2026-07-28: "if already fixed, make sure you update the steps / task". Three entries are fixed and were still sitting open. Each is closed here with the evidence, not on recollection.\n\nB46 (step 38) — the sleepmode reply reports `on`, we only read `slp`.\n  FIXED, verified by reading mesh/index.js:344-360 this turn:\n      if (reply.slp != null) { this.model.sleep(id, reply.slp); learned = true; }\n      else if (reply.type === \'sleep\' && reply.on != null) {\n        this.model.sleep(id, reply.on ? 1 : 0); learned = true;\n      }\n  `slp` keeps priority (a status reply carries it and is authoritative) and the fallback is\n  TYPE-GUARDED, so a stray `on` on some other reply cannot move sleep state. The same trap was\n  independently re-hit today in config-field-wiring, where the confirm predicate for `slp` also\n  has to read `on` — and the test fails if it is pointed at `slp`.\n\nB49 (step 47) — two configs, one of them dead under pac-host.\n  FIXED by config-single-source, commit be83790. mesh/config.yaml deleted; the ECONFIG message\n  now names host/host.config.json, the file pac-host actually loads. Verified on the wire after\n  the change: a live send appeared as POST /%212687afb1/messages, i.e. the loaded config is the\n  one in force.\n\nB65 (step 48) — our own radios relay each other, contaminating per-radio statistics.\n  FIXED by self-relay-exclusion, commit 5ac2dec. selfRelay is derived at the gateway boundary from\n  DISCOVERED radio identities (mesh-gw /devices plus the node_id on every event), never declared.\n  Self-relayed frames are kept out of the phase estimate while lastHeardMs and the butler cue still\n  fire. Verified the fix is REACHED: reverting the exclusion fails the suite with "a self-relayed\n  frame does not become a phase sample".\n\nSTILL OPEN and NOT closed here:\n  B60 (steps 39 AND 40 — a DUPLICATE I created; step 40 is the fuller entry, 39 should be treated\n       as superseded rather than deleted, per append-only)\n  B64 (step 46) — wakesDirect published nowhere. Being fixed now.\n  B63 (step 45, corrected at step 51) — downgraded to UNVERIFIED, evidence contradicts the claim.\n  B66, B67 — device-side and contract-change respectively; neither is ours to close.'}
