2026-07-28 09:57:02,004 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Our own gateway radios relay each other, and nothing marked it — so frames that travelled across the room entered statistics about a 2.5 km link.\n\nPeter, 2026-07-28: "we accept relays from OMNI -> YAGI and YAGI -> OMNI and that corrupts signal and hop counts."\n\nMeasured over 234 GARG frames since deployment: 8% were relayed by one of our own radios, at -29 to -39 dBm — roughly 80 dB stronger than the garage path — dragging every blended median upward. Figures built on them reached docs/history/radio-selection.md, host/host.config.json and commit d870054 as the justification for choosing a transmit antenna.\n\nSuccess: a frame relayed by any radio mesh-gw is connected to is tagged at the gateway boundary and kept out of the phase estimate, while liveness (lastHeardMs, the butler cue) is preserved — because the unit demonstrably transmitted.'}
2026-07-28 09:57:07,107 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Tag it in gw.js, where a mesh-gw envelope becomes our shape — a rule each read site must remember is one that will be forgotten at one of them.\n\n"Ours" is ANY radio mesh-gw is connected to, not a named pair, and DISCOVERED never declared: a node id in a config file is a hardware fact asserted by a file and goes stale on a swap. Two live sources — the node_id on every event (each frame identifies the radio that reported it) and the /devices roster at startup.\n\nMatch on the low byte, all relay_node carries; the collision risk is real and recorded rather than hidden.\n\nExclude self-relayed frames from the PHASE ESTIMATE only. Keep lastHeardMs and the butler cue: a self-relayed frame is good evidence the unit transmitted and worthless evidence about the link or the timing.\n\nDONE 2026-07-28, commit 5ac2dec. 23 suites, 20 new assertions. Fix verified REACHED: reverting the exclusion fails with "a self-relayed frame does not become a phase sample". Live discovery confirmed against the running gateway — both radios found, nothing in the code limited to two.'}
