2026-07-28 09:58:10,570 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'config-map-completeness', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'CLOSED 2026-07-28 as SUPERSEDED and DELIVERED.\n\nSuperseded by fw-surface-parity, which covers the whole firmware surface (30 verbs + 21 fields) rather than fields alone — Peter: "makes no diff if they are configs or not, they should be in the service, everything that is in the fw should be in the service."\n\nThe work this task named is DONE, commit 1edc764: COMMAND_MAP went from 6 to 17 of 21 fields. Each of the 11 new entries was derived by reading the firmware handler, with a confirm predicate asserted true for the real reply shape and false for a near-miss.\n\nThe four still unmapped are not oversights and each carries its reason in the code:\n  txp                    firmware marks it writable:false — read-only by design\n  det.n, mute, push.auto NO firmware verb exists at all (B66) — a device-session request,\n                         not ours. mute is the worst of them: a LIVE setting gating the PIR\n                         startup lockout at main.cpp:2286 that nothing can currently change.\n\nWhat replaces this task\'s watchfulness: mesh/test/api-parity.js now goes red if firmware gains a verb or field that services has neither handled nor exempted. The gap is enforced rather than remembered.\n\nAlso raised while doing it, NOT fixed here: B67 — POST /v1/mesh/config/:target sends direct with a 30 s timeout and no cross-window retry, so a config write to a sleeping unit fails by design. That makes these newly-wired fields reachable in principle but unreliable on the deployed unit. Routing config through the butler is an http.md contract change and needs node-dash\'s ack.'}
