2026-07-28 10:26:01,198 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'CLOSING SWEEP 2026-07-28 10:25 — B44, B45, B18 were fixed by the estimator rewrite and left open; B16 by D6', 'description': 'Verified in code this turn, not recalled. These were open only because nobody went back to close them after the work that fixed them.\n\nB44 (steps 34, 35) — "the wake predictor uses the single previous gap as the beat".\n  FIXED by wake-phase-precision. `beat = gap` is gone; model.js:311 uses medianOf(rejects) over a\n  run of RESEED_AFTER=3 agreeing gaps, and the comment at :317 names the old code exactly:\n  "THE BEAT DOES NOT WANDER. This was `beat = gap` — every agreeing wake overwrote the schedule."\n  Measured consequence: the bench went from +-1-2.5 s to 0 ms/cycle.\n\nB45 (steps 36, 37) — "agrees() accepts a reboot\'s partial gap as a new beat".\n  FIXED by beat-authority + wake-detector-resolution. model.js:101 isFactorAlias() rejects\n  small-integer multiples and divisors as ALIASING rather than a schedule change, and :266 gates\n  on `gap >= minBeatMs` so a partial gap is never credited at all.\n\nB18 (step 22) — "the live model is IN-MEMORY ONLY, so every restart discards the schedule".\n  FIXED by wake-state-persistence. index.js:109 _restoreWakeState() on connect, :243 and :393\n  _persistWakeState() on heard and on learn, backed by store.loadNodeState/saveNodeState.\n  Observed live today: pac-host restarted repeatedly and units kept beat/beatSource across it.\n\nB16 (step 17) — "timing.chunkAnswerMs is declared and consumed by nobody".\n  RESOLVED by D6 (commit 8df4f54): the knob was deleted rather than given an invented purpose.\n  Recorded in decisions-for-peter as a judgement call he may want reversed — a removal from a\n  declared surface — so it is closed here as ACTIONED, with that reversal noted, not as "fine".\n\nNOTE ON DUPLICATES: B44, B45, B60 and B63 each appear twice in this ledger. That is my doing —\nre-raising an entry instead of amending it. Both copies of each are closed together. The ledger is\nappend-only by design, so they stay visible; the duplication itself is a P4 tidiness cost.\n\nSTILL GENUINELY OPEN AND OURS after this sweep: B5, B6, B15, B22, B23, B24, B25, B26, B27, B54.\nMost are the S1 ack-consumption family — the ledger cannot show what was transmitted, only what was\nacked — which is the next substantial piece of work and is NOT started.'}
