lse / socket down)\nis covered by the code path returning false, NOT by an assertion; worth adding.\n\nNOT MEASURED, deliberately: whether this improves command success. GARG\'s direct path has\nbeen gone since 07:17 (B68) and 0 of 28 sends landed today (B69), so any rate now describes\nthe link. One change per measurement.'}
2026-07-28 11:34:39,225 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'task': 'radio-selection', 'kind': 'goal', 'content': "Transmit to each unit through whichever antenna measurably reaches it best, and make sure that antenna is actually POINTED at the unit when its wake window opens.\n\nSupersedes static gateway routing and absorbs B59. Two halves:\n\n1. ROTATOR LOCK (step 10) — DONE d8ee8a0. A few seconds before a unit's predicted wake, aim the yagi at it and tell the rotator to refuse every competing move for the window. node-dash's scanner and ACTV tracker drive the same antenna; the arbitration lives in the ROTATOR, by Peter's design 2026-07-27, not in either client. Proven live 11:32 with the antenna parked 60 deg off-target: it slewed back and held 30 s across the wake unprompted.\n\n2. PER-TARGET SELECTION — not started. Choose omni vs yagi per unit from measured link quality rather than one gatewayId in config. Blocked in practice while the garage direct path is down (B68/B69), because selection needs a working link to compare against."}
