s 3 consecutive windows, one is measured — the rest\naccrue on their own. Criterion 4 (enabled=false / socket down) is covered by the code path\nreturning false but NOT by an assertion; worth adding.\n\nNOT MEASURED, deliberately: whether this improves command success. GARG\'s direct path has been\ngone since 07:17 (B68) and 0 of 28 sends landed today (B69), so any rate measured now describes\nthe link, not this change. One change per measurement.'}
2026-07-28 11:35:10,342 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'task': 'radio-selection', 'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'PART 1 — ROTATOR LOCK. DONE (step 10, commit d8ee8a0).\n  Aim the yagi at a unit at nextWake - rotatorLeadMs, then hold for rotatorHoldMs so node-dash\'s\n  scanner/ACTV tracker cannot swing it mid-window. Move FIRST then hold — a hold refuses a move.\n  Bearings computed from positions; rotator.site declared because the rotator-mounted Heltec\n  reports none. minDistanceM stops a unit at the same site (BNCH) swinging the antenna.\n\nPART 2 — PER-TARGET SELECTION. NOT STARTED, and correctly blocked.\n  1. Restrict the metric to DIRECT receptions (hop_limit == hop_start, relay unset or ours).\n     A relayed copy describes a different physical link — see the 66 dB same-packet evidence in\n     the note above, and B65 for our own radios relaying each other.\n  2. Treat "no recent direct evidence" as UNKNOWN, never as a stale winner (B30/B32 rule).\n  3. Publish best-direct-reception with a `via` on /devices, and say so when only relayed data\n     exists (absorbs B59).\n  4. Only then choose omni vs yagi per unit instead of one gatewayId in config.\n\n  BLOCKED IN PRACTICE, not by a decision: the garage direct path has been gone since 07:17 today\n  (B68) and 0 of 28 sends were delivered (B69). Selection needs a working link to compare\n  against, and every figure taken now would describe the outage.\n\nOPEN QUESTION that bounds part 2, from the 2026-07-27 note and still unanswered: which antenna\nis the DEPLOYED RAK actually connected to — the garage yagi at 310 deg, or a local whip? Our\nmeasurements are all of the receive path into the house. Ask before assuming symmetry.'}
