s one. Same rule as "never infer a\n  physical fact from a config file", which this project bought expensively.\n\n## Two adjacent defects found in the same minute, both mine, both fixed in 5f8c69d\n\nB73a  The rotator\'s visible-skip line fired every 60 s for BNCH, forever — the exact flood I had\n      just spent the afternoon removing from the recorder (B72). The reason is STATIC (BNCH stands\n      at the antenna and always will), so it is a once-per-unit fact, not a per-wake event. Now\n      said once, and the message says so.\nB73b  `_roster` is an ARRAY, not a Map. My first _shortName wrote it as a Map lookup, which would\n      have returned null every time and fallen straight back to the wrong labels — a fix that\n      silently does nothing. Caught by checking the field\'s shape rather than assuming it.\n\n## Worth watching, NOT yet a defect\n\nThe first err values after a restart read -1204, -158, +792, -781 ms, against the +-8 ms measured\nover 26 settled intervals earlier today. These are the first wakes after a restart with restored\nstate, so a large error is expected there — but it is now VISIBLE PER WAKE instead of recoverable\nonly by hand from the CSV, which is exactly what the line is for. If it does not settle toward\nsingle-digit ms over the next hour, that is a real finding. Not claimed either way yet.'}
2026-07-28 13:28:36,273 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'fw-macaddr-nodeinfo', 'title': 'FIRMWARE: we broadcast macaddr as six zero bytes — send the real one, like every other node on the mesh', 'steps': ["Investigate: DONE. sendNodeInfo (src/main.cpp:1781) starts from meshtastic_User_init_zero and never assigns u.macaddr; the field is STATIC/SINGULAR FIXED_LENGTH_BYTES so it is always encoded - as zeros. Live proof: both our units report macaddr 'AAAAAAAA' = 00:00:00:00:00:00, while 134 of 216 mesh nodes report a real one.", 'Document: spec with the derivation and the invariant macaddr[2..5] == nodeNum, which is what 132 of 134 nodes do.', 'Implement: fill u.macaddr from the nRF52 FICR device address, low 4 bytes taken from g_nodeNum so the invariant holds even if MESH_NODE_NUM overrides it.', 'Observe: build, then verify on the wire that GET /v1/mesh/nodes shows a non-zero macaddr whose last 4 bytes equal the node id. FLASH IS GATED - the garage unit cannot be reflashed while deployed.', 'Track: hash the spec, commit.']}
