2026-07-28 14:02:51,203 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'B74 (OURS, extends B59) — /v1/mesh/devices publishes ONE rssi/snr per unit, so no consumer can see a per-radio difference, and the value shown flips 21 dB depending on which radio reported last', 'notes': 'Raised 2026-07-28 by Peter: "there\'s nothing in the existing dashboard which uses our services to\nshow differences between the radios / antenna ... this page needs a re-hash ... we now have a lot\nmore stats available than when this page was written". Page: node-dash /node/!987ab80f.\n\n## It is not node-dash\'s gap. It is ours.\n\nGET /v1/mesh/devices returns a SINGLE rssi/snr per unit:\n\n  keys: id num name shortName label source present mode awake slp lastHeard lastHeardMs\n        beat beatSource phase phaseSamples wakesDirect nextWake windowMs windowSource\n        fw position hops rssi snr\n\nThe only per-radio data anywhere in the API is align (align.js:245 byRadio, yagi_q/omni_q), and\nthat is an ON-DEMAND ping burst, not continuous. So a dashboard CANNOT show a radio comparison,\nhowever it is written.\n\n## And the single value is actively misleading\n\nMeasured, same GARG packet, same second:\n  OMNI  -96 dBm  SNR +5.00\n  YAGI  -117 dBm SNR -7.00\n21 dB apart, describing two different physical paths — the omni\'s copy came via relay node 4, so\n-96 is THAT NODE\'s signal, not the garage\'s. Whichever copy arrives last wins the published field.\nA page reading "GARG: -96 dBm" is showing the strength of a relay we do not own.\n\nSame root as the 66 dB same-packet example already recorded in radio-selection (2026-07-27) and as\nB59.\n\n## What it needs, and the order\n\n1. best DIRECT reception per radio (hop_limit == hop_start), each with a `via`\n2. direct vs relayed counts per radio, so "we only have relayed evidence" is VISIBLE\n3. an explicit UNKNOWN state when there is no recent direct sample — never a stale winner, and\n   never a relayed number dressed as a link measurement (B30/B32 rule)\n\nThis is the prerequisite for radio-selection part 2 as well: selection needs the same per-radio\ndirect metric, so building it once serves both.\n\n## Stats that DO now exist and no consumer reads\n\nRecorded because Peter\'s point was that the page predates them: beat/beatSource, phase,\nphaseSamples, wakesDirect, nextWake, windowMs/windowSource, the full ledger ack story\n(acks[]/ackState/sentIds[]/sentTo[]/tries/state), /v1/mesh/queue as a filterable outbox, and the\nconfig surface at 17 of 21 fields (was 6).\n\nNOT FIXED — comment only, at Peter\'s explicit request ("the UI is not your job ... just comment\nthat\'s all"). The API half is ours whenever it is picked up.'}
