2026-07-28 14:04:23,055 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': "B74 (OURS, extends B59) — we publish ONE rssi/snr per unit so no dashboard can show a per-radio difference, and the value flips 21 dB depending on which radio reported last. Plus: node-dash's node page shows a TWO-WEEK-OLD hop count as if live.", 'notes': 'Raised 2026-07-28 by Peter, on node-dash /node/!987ab80f: "there\'s nothing in the existing dashboard\nwhich uses our services to show differences between the radios / antenna ... we now have a lot more\nstats available than when this page was written", and "the page needs to be informative and partly\ndiagnostic, and not show info / data for the sake of it. golden UI/UIX rule".\n\nScreenshot taken via playwright and read. COMMENT ONLY at his request — the UI is not ours.\n\n## THE API HALF IS OURS, and it is the blocker\n\nGET /v1/mesh/devices returns a SINGLE rssi/snr per unit:\n  id num name shortName label source present mode awake slp lastHeard lastHeardMs beat beatSource\n  phase phaseSamples wakesDirect nextWake windowMs windowSource fw position hops rssi snr\n\nThe only per-radio data in the whole API is align (align.js:245 byRadio, yagi_q/omni_q), and that\nis an ON-DEMAND ping burst, not continuous. So no dashboard can show a radio comparison however it\nis written. This is not node-dash\'s gap.\n\nAND THE SINGLE VALUE IS MISLEADING. Same GARG packet, same second:\n  OMNI  -96 dBm  SNR +5.00     (via relay node 4 — that is THAT NODE\'s signal)\n  YAGI  -117 dBm SNR -7.00\n21 dB apart, two different physical paths, and whichever copy arrives last wins the field. Same\nroot as the 66 dB same-packet example in radio-selection (2026-07-27) and as B59.\n\n## WHAT THE PAGE GETS WRONG (node-dash\'s, reported not fixed)\n\nACTIVELY WRONG: tile "HOPS 0 — verified 14 Jul 17:51". A two-week-old value rendered with the same\nweight as live data. GARG has arrived at hop 1, RELAYED, for essentially all of today. The page\nasserts "direct" when it has not been direct in hours.\n\nRIGHT, AND THE PATTERN TO COPY: "SIGNAL -116 dBm · Fair · -6.5 dB · direct 45m ago". That qualifier\nis exactly correct — it states the KIND of reception and its AGE. HOPS should carry the same and\ndoes not.\n\nDATA FOR ITS OWN SAKE: LATITUDE and LONGITUDE as two large tiles (raw coordinates diagnose\nnothing — one tile "2.501 km @ 121 deg" is the derived fact you would actually use); BATTERY 79%\nAND VOLTAGE 4.02 V (one fact, two tiles); CHAN UTIL / AIR UTIL TX are mesh health, not this node\'s.\n\n## MISSING, on a page about a unit that stopped answering\n\n1. IS IT ANSWERING — command outcomes. 0 of 28 delivered today. The single most diagnostic fact\n   available and it is absent. We publish it: acks[]/ackState/sentIds[]/sentTo[]/tries/state.\n2. NEXT WAKE COUNTDOWN. The unit is deaf ~99% of the time, so "next window in 13m 20s" matters far\n   more than "last heard 41s ago". We publish nextWake/beat/beatSource/windowMs/windowSource.\n3. WAKE RELIABILITY — 45 of 47 expected today, 93.8%. The number that says whether the alarm works.\n4. DIRECT vs RELAYED split and VIA WHICH RELAY, with "relayed only, no recent direct evidence"\n   stated explicitly rather than implied by a stale number.\n\nThe through-line: the page shows what the node IS, and almost nothing about whether we can REACH\nit — which is the only reason anyone opens it.\n\n## Order of work when picked up\n\n1. (OURS) per-radio best DIRECT reception with a `via`, plus direct/relayed counts per radio, and\n   an explicit UNKNOWN when there is no recent direct sample — never a stale winner (B30/B32).\n2. (OURS) surface the ack summary and the wake countdown on the devices route.\n3. (node-dash) re-hash the page against those.\n\nStep 1 is also the prerequisite for radio-selection part 2 — the selector needs the same per-radio\ndirect metric, so building it once serves both.'}
2026-07-28 14:05:15,933 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'devices-answer-the-questions', 'title': 'Publish the answers to the questions Peter has to keep asking — tx radio, per-radio reception, rotator hold state, delivery rate, prediction error', 'steps': ['Investigate: DONE. Nine recurring questions from 2026-07-28 mapped to fields; seven are unpublished and had to be measured by hand each time. /v1/mesh/devices carries a single rssi/snr, no tx radio, no rotator state, no ack summary, no delivery rate.', 'Document: spec naming each field, which question it answers, and its null/unknown behaviour. A field that cannot be measured says null and why - never a guess.', 'Implement: rotator arming state per unit, tx radio identity, ack summary, wakes seen/expected, prediction error. Per-radio reception is B74 and is SEPARATE - it needs a model change, not a route change.', 'Observe: curl the route and answer all seven questions from the payload alone, without running a single ad-hoc query.', 'Track: hash the spec, run all suites, commit, and tell node-dash the contract changed.']}
