2026-07-28 15:25:45,362 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'B79 ROOT CAUSE OF 0-of-28, CONFIRMED FROM THE GATEWAY LOG — DMs to GARG fail with PKI_SEND_FAIL_PUBLIC_KEY. Broadcasts on the same radio go out fine.', 'notes': 'Found 2026-07-28 15:23 by sending a DM and a BROADCAST to GARG back-to-back on the same radio and\nreading mesh-gw\'s own log. This is the answer to B69/B78 and to the whole day\'s 0-of-28.\n\n## The evidence, one line each\n\n  DM        POST /%212687afb1/messages {"text":"@b80f ping","channel":2,"to":2558179343}\n            -> {"id":4154079194,"to":2558179343}\n            mesh-gw: routing_ack request_id=4154079194 failed error=PKI_SEND_FAIL_PUBLIC_KEY\n\n  BROADCAST POST /%212687afb1/messages {"text":"@b80f ping","channel":2}\n            -> {"id":1097330768,"to":4294967295}\n            mesh-gw: send_text_message to=!ffffffff id=1097330768 channel=2 sent\n\nSame radio, same channel, seconds apart. The DM is refused by the PKI layer; the broadcast is sent.\n\n## This explains every feature of B78\n\n  DESTINATION-SPECIFIC   only GARG\'s key is unusable; the bench\'s works, hence 0 refusals in 94\n                         sends to it.\n  BOTH RADIOS            each gateway radio holds its own copy of the same unusable key.\n  RUNS/INTERMITTENT      what looked like a filling queue is the PKI failure recurring per attempt.\n  NOT congestion, NOT duty cycle, NOT the antenna, NOT routing.\n\nIt also means B78\'s fix (one transmission per attempt instead of three) reduced load but could\nnever have fixed this — and the ledger says so: after the fix, tries=2 sends=4 refused=4.\n\n## MY EARLIER "RULED OUT" WAS WRONG, and the reason matters\n\nI checked the node roster, saw `public_key PRESENT len=44` for both units, and wrote that a missing\nkey was "ruled out by measurement, not by argument". PRESENT IS NOT USABLE. The roster shows what\nNodeInfo advertised; the sending radio still has to encrypt with it, and that is what fails. I\ntested the wrong proposition and reported the answer with more confidence than the test supported.\n\nMost likely cause: GARG\'s keypair CHANGED. It was reflashed 2026-07-26/27, the firmware derives\ng_pkiPublic at boot, and a gateway holding the pre-flash key would fail exactly like this. Not yet\nconfirmed — the stored key has not been compared against what GARG advertises now.\n\n## The workaround exists TODAY and is proven\n\nThe broadcast path is already built and declared: dm.default / dm.fallbackChannel (2) /\ndm.omitAddress, and the firmware still accepts the `@token ` prefix. The broadcast above WENT OUT.\nSetting GARG to the broadcast path makes it commandable again without waiting for a key fix.\n\nCost, stated honestly: a broadcast is unencrypted-to-a-node and every mesh member on channel 2 sees\nthe text; and broadcasts cannot be ACKed at all (`no_ack_needed: unackable`), so we lose the\nmesh-level ack — which today is worth little anyway, since a relay ack never proved arrival.\n\n## Real fix, in order\n\n1. CONFIRM the key mismatch: compare the key the gateway holds for !987ab80f against the one GARG\n   advertises in its current NodeInfo.\n2. Make the gateway RE-LEARN it. A fresh NodeInfo from GARG should do it; forcing that is the\n   question (mesh-gw may need the node record dropped).\n3. Only then return GARG to DMs.\n\n## Wider lesson for the ledger\n\nEvery layer reported success. mesh-gw returned 200 OK on the POST; our ledger recorded a `send`;\nthe failure existed only in a DEBUG line in mesh-gw\'s journal. That is exactly what Peter meant by\n"DO NOT ASSUME that packets sent by the butler were actually transmitted" — and it is why\nsent-is-not-transmitted (4b4d5fb) matters more than it looked when I wrote it an hour ago.'}
2026-07-28 15:26:44,972 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'per-unit-dm-fallback', 'title': "B79: let a unit be addressed by BROADCAST instead of DM, per unit — GARG's PKI DMs are refused and the broadcast path already works", 'steps': ['Investigate: DONE. mesh-gw log: DM to GARG -> routing_ack failed error=PKI_SEND_FAIL_PUBLIC_KEY; broadcast on the same radio, same channel, seconds later -> sent. Both units advertise the SAME public key because secrets.h holds ONE MESH_PKI_PRIVATE_KEY for the whole image.', 'Document: spec. dm.default is GLOBAL; this needs to be per-unit so the bench keeps working DMs while the garage uses the broadcast path. State the cost: broadcasts are visible to channel 2 and cannot be acked.', 'Implement: units.<id>.dm override honoured by _addressed(), defaulting to dm.default so nothing changes for anyone else.', 'Observe: a command to GARG goes out as to=!ffffffff and is NOT refused; the bench still sends DMs. From the gateway journal, not from our own logs.', 'Track: hash, run all suites, commit. The real fix is per-unit PKI keys in firmware - separate task, flash-gated.']}
2026-07-28 15:59:05,197 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_done args={'task': 'per-unit-dm-fallback', 'number': 4, 'notes': 'ACCEPTANCE MET 2026-07-28 15:57, all four criteria, read from the mesh-gw journal rather than our\nown ledger — because our ledger is precisely what could not see this failure.\n\n## The proof is inside ONE request, so nothing else varies\n\nThe `interval` request spans the change:\n\n  acks = [queue_failed, queue_failed, queue_failed, queue_failed, no_ack_needed, no_ack_needed]\n          |______________ as DM: refused by PKI ______________|  |__ as broadcast: SENT __|\n\nFour DMs refused and never on air; the fix lands; the next two go out. `no_ack_needed` is the\nbroadcast ack state ("acks impossible by protocol"), which is what a SENT broadcast looks like.\n\n  15:47:19  send_text_message to=!ffffffff id=470607080  channel=2 sent\n  15:52:20  send_text_message to=!ffffffff id=2523283385 channel=2 sent\n\n## Criterion by criterion\n\n1. GARG leaves the gateway as to=!ffffffff and is NOT refused.            MET, above.\n2. The bench still sends DMs, unaffected:\n     15:57:33 send_text_message to=!8cee336b id=550260954 channel=0 sent\n     ledger: ping done sends=3 acks=[\'delivered\',\'no_ack\',\'delivered\']    MET.\n3. Zero PKI_SEND_FAIL for GARG since the change (count since 15:30: 0).   MET.\n4. 32 suites pass.                                                        MET.\n\nNOTE on the bench\'s sends=3: that was a direct /v1/mesh/command call, which still carries\nretry.idempotent = 2 by design — B78 made only the BUTLER\'s own path send once. Correct behaviour,\nnot a regression.\n\n## What is NOT yet shown, and must not be claimed\n\nThat GARG RECEIVES the broadcast. Being sent is not being heard, and that is the same distinction\nthis whole thread has been about. A broadcast cannot be acked, so the only proof will be a REPLY —\nand the queued `ping` has not been delivered yet because GARG\'s 14:32Z wake was missed entirely\n(wakesSeen 0/1 that window; last heard 14:17:20Z).\n\nSo: the SEND path to the garage is fixed and proven. Whether the unit answers is the next question\nand it is open.'}
2026-07-28 15:59:19,105 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'task': 'per-unit-dm-fallback', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': "Make the deployed garage unit commandable again TODAY, without a flash.\n\nRoot cause (B79), from mesh-gw's own log: every DM to !987ab80f is refused with\n`routing_ack failed error=PKI_SEND_FAIL_PUBLIC_KEY`, while a BROADCAST on the same radio, same\nchannel, seconds later is sent. Both units advertise the SAME public key, because include/secrets.h\nholds ONE MESH_PKI_PRIVATE_KEY for the whole image and main.cpp:3616 calls setPkiIdentity with it.\n\nThat is the answer to the day's 0-of-28: those commands were never weak, never mistimed and never\ntransmitted. It also explains every feature of B78 that a queue-pressure theory had to strain at —\ndestination-specific, on BOTH radios, absent for the bench, and unaffected by cutting three\ntransmissions per attempt to one.\n\nThis task is the WORKAROUND: a per-unit `units.<id>.dm` override so the garage uses the existing\nbroadcast path while the bench keeps working DMs. The REAL fix is per-unit PKI keys in firmware,\nwhich is flash-gated and cannot reach a deployed unit."}
2026-07-28 15:59:31,980 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'task': 'per-unit-dm-fallback', 'kind': 'plan', 'text': '1. units.<id>.dm honoured by _addressed(), defaulting to dm.default so nothing changes for anyone\n   else. !987ab80f set to false in host.config.json. DONE, commit 65af938.\n2. Verify from the MESH-GW JOURNAL, not our ledger — our ledger reported "sends" for packets that\n   were refused, which is how this hid all day. DONE.\n3. Leave the bench on DMs: they work, they are encrypted, and they can be acked.\n4. NEXT, and separate: per-unit PKI keys in firmware. Flash-gated, so GARG gets it at the next\n   physical swap. Until then this stands.\n5. STILL OPEN after this: whether GARG ANSWERS a broadcast. Being sent is not being heard, and a\n   broadcast cannot be acked — so the only proof is a reply. Do not conflate the two.'}
