or that window; last heard 14:17:20Z).\n\nSo: the SEND path to the garage is fixed and proven. Whether the unit answers is the next question\nand it is open.'}
2026-07-28 16:50:40,818 337709 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'fw-per-unit-pki-key', 'title': 'FIRMWARE, URGENT before the unit swap: derive a DEVICE-UNIQUE PKI key — every unit currently shares one key from secrets.h, which is why all DMs to the garage are refused (B79)', 'steps': ['Investigate: DONE. secrets.h holds ONE MESH_PKI_PRIVATE_KEY; main.cpp:3616 setPkiIdentity(MESH_PKI_PRIVATE_KEY). Both units advertise the same public key, and mesh-gw refuses every DM to GARG with PKI_SEND_FAIL_PUBLIC_KEY.', 'Document: spec. Derive from HARDWARE (FICR DEVICEADDR), not from the role table - the role is chosen by VBUS at boot, so a role-keyed identity would change with the power source while the node num stayed put.', 'Implement: mt::pkiDeriveIdentity() in the transport lib (SHA256 of salt folded with the hardware id, then X25519 clamp), called from setup. secrets.h untouched - the existing shared key becomes the SALT.', 'Observe: the two units must advertise DIFFERENT public keys, and a DM to each must be accepted by mesh-gw. Read from the gateway, not from our ledger.', 'Track: hash the spec, build, flash the bench, commit. GARG gets it in the swap.']}
