2026-07-28 20:25:01,651 8170 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'B82 CONFIRMED (device/, NOT OURS to fix): every PKC DM from the omni fails X25519 auth at the RAK — pkiRxAuthFail only, never pkiRxNoKey, never pkiRxOk', 'description': '**Where:** `device/src/main.cpp:4286` reports it; the defect is in the key material, not the log.\n`device/transport/src/mt_pki.cpp` (FICR derivation) and the unit\'s own node-DB copy of the\ngateway\'s public key are the two suspects.\n\n**Evidence, measured on the bench\'s serial console 2026-07-28 ~19:20Z, unit awake and listening\ncontinuously (HB every 5 s), NOT asleep:**\n\n```\nHB up=869s ... rx=535s pki=0/0/6 pkifrom=2687afb1\nPOST /v1/mesh/command {unit:336b,verb:ping}   -> sent, sentIds [509062977]\nHB up=914s ... rx=580s pki=0/0/7 pkifrom=2687afb1      <-- authFail 6 -> 7 on that packet\n```\n\n`pki=` is `pkiRxOk/pkiRxNoKey/pkiRxAuthFail`. **0 decrypted, 0 missing-key, 7 auth failures**, all\nfrom `2687afb1` (our omni). The DM reaches the radio and fails authentication.\n\n**Control, same unit, same capture, minutes later:**\n\n```\nPOST /v1/mesh/text {text:"@336b ping"}    -> broadcast, channel 2\nRX: from=0x2687afb1 id=0x29b45c7d port=1 len=10 rssi=-51 snr=6.2\nTXT enq 88 1                                           <-- replied\n```\n\nBroadcast decodes and is answered; DM arrives and cannot be decrypted. Same radio, same peer,\nsame minute.\n\n**Not explained by a stale key at the gateway.** Both gateways\' node tables hold the bench\'s\nCURRENT key `/bgDYeVo3jTTbNBVXiRfbhfatSjv7CGSZz03SlCzZgY=` — read live from\n`/!2687afb1/nodes/2364420971` and `/!fa39f7b4/nodes/2364420971`, agreeing, `is_unmessagable:false`.\nAnd `pkiRxNoKey=0` says the bench holds *some* key for the omni. So the shared secret is being\ncomputed from a key that one side no longer holds — suspect the bench\'s stored copy of the\ngateway\'s public key, or the FICR derivation producing a private key that disagrees with the\npublic key it advertises.\n\n**NOT OURS.** Raised for the device session. Services works around it: `units.!8cee336b.dm=false`\nnow routes the bench by broadcast, as GARG already was.\n\n**Corrects an earlier claim of mine.** I reported the bench\'s receiver as dead from `rx=never/0s`.\n`g_lastRxMs` is stamped only after a packet has been decoded (`main.cpp:3955`, `4500`), so a\nPKI-failed frame never touches it. `rx=never` means "nothing decodable arrived", not "nothing\narrived". Peter said this was PKI all day and was right.'}
