2026-07-29 07:00:23,557 18559 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'wake-drain-queue', 'title': 'PARKED until after the swap: send SEVERAL queued commands per wake instead of one — the device drains its RX window, we serialise', 'steps': ["PARKED 2026-07-29 by agreement. Do NOT start without saying so. Service-side only, no flash, safe with a unit in the field — this is roadmap S2 wake-timed-send. Reason for parking: it inverts the pacer's core invariant in the exact file whose reply correlation was fixed and measured at 0/22 the same night, hours before the unit was deployed.", 'Investigate: mesh/lib/timing.js `inFlight` is a SINGLE slot referenced in 14 places — dedupe-by-key (:56), onReply (:85), abandonInFlight (:138), the pump gate (:150), the send path (:169/177/205/213) and `pending` (:221). mesh/lib/butler.js:111 `if (this.inflight.has(unit)) continue; // one command per window` is the per-unit half. Establish which of those genuinely need single-outstanding and which merely assume it.', 'Document: spec. Multiple outstanding sends per unit, replies matched by packet id (already correct since reply-correlation-off-by-one, dd9278a). State how retries, dedupe and abandonInFlight behave with N outstanding BEFORE writing code.', 'Implement: only what the spec names.', "Observe: the regression gate already exists — the 22-verb sweep at scratchpad/sweep.sh. It must still show ZERO verbs answered by another command's reply. Plus the actual number: queue 4 echos, count replies in ONE wake (today: 1).", 'Track: hash, run all 32 suites, commit.']}
