2026-07-29 07:38:41,833 18559 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'log-colour-central', 'title': "PARKED: colour every log line centrally from a key/colour table, replacing the call-site helper — Peter's design", 'steps': ["PARKED 2026-07-29, not urgent. Do NOT start without saying so.\n\nPETER'S DESIGN, in his words: 'pass every log through a function, and that function accepts the full log line, plus an array of keys / colours so that it works for everything and not hard coded to any specific log line as you have now.'\n\nWHY MINE IS WRONG: dfea5e9 colours at the CALL SITE via unitLabel(unit) — 14 edits in butler.js plus one in index.js. Consequence, which Peter spotted immediately: only the lines I remembered to touch are coloured, and every future log line must opt in. Central formatting inverts that: colour is applied once, to every line, and a new line gets it for free.", "Investigate: mesh/lib/log.js makeLogger()'s emit() already formats the whole line (util.format) before writing to the sink or stream. That is the single chokepoint every module's log goes through — root and children alike — so the colouriser belongs there and nowhere else.", 'Document: spec. A colourise(line, table) applied in emit(). The table is key -> colour, declared in ONE place (settings or log.js), covering at least: node ids (!xxxxxxxx, coloured stably by hash so a unit keeps its colour), short names, and request ids. State what happens to a line that already contains an escape (do not double-wrap) and confirm NO_COLOR still yields zero escapes.', 'Implement: colourise in log.js emit(); DELETE the call-site unitLabel() edits in butler.js and index.js so there is exactly one mechanism, not two.', 'Observe: every unit-bearing line is coloured, not just the ones previously touched — count coloured lines before/after over the same log window. NO_COLOR=1 still emits zero escapes. grep for a node id still matches the same number of lines.', 'Track: hash, run all 32 suites, commit.']}
