2026-07-29 07:47:22,205 18559 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "CONTROL MENU: 4 of 6 submenus are 'Coming soon' placeholders, and there is NO Images page — measured with playwright 2026-07-29", 'description': 'Peter, 2026-07-29: "look at the dash using playwright, the Control menu and it\'s submenus, most\nsub menus are placeholders" and "one submenu missing is a \'Images\' menu / page."\n\nMEASURED, by clicking each submenu and reading the rendered main content:\n\n| submenu     | state                                                        |\n|-------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Summary     | "Coming soon." (436 chars, all of it chrome)                  |\n| Command     | REAL — unit/verb UI, 14290 chars                             |\n| Config      | "Coming soon."                                                |\n| Stats       | "Coming soon."                                                |\n| Yagi Align  | partial — "Star a node to align", 678 chars                   |\n| Chat        | "Coming soon."                                                |\n| **Images**  | **DOES NOT EXIST**                                            |\n\nSo the only working control surface is Command.\n\n## The Images gap is the sharpest, because OUR side is already built\n\nThe pipeline works end to end — proven 2026-07-29 06:11Z: camera -> RAK -> mesh -> reassembly,\n32/32 chunks, 1 repair, 29 dupes, 7156-byte 320x240 JPEG, 274.3 s. Already served by:\n\n- `GET /v1/mesh/images/:target`        -> {pid, state, chunks, crc, proto, fw, ready}\n- `GET /v1/mesh/images/:target/:pid`   -> the JPEG itself (image/jpeg)\n- per-transfer stats persisted per pid (chunks, received, missing, repairs, repairIds, dupes,\n  staleRounds, firstChunkAt, streamMs, totalMs) via images.store.loadStats\n- progress now logged live during a pull (image-transfer-progress-log)\n\nNone of it is visible in the UI. The only way to see a picture from the garage today is a curl.\n\nWHAT AN IMAGES PAGE NEEDS, and it is mostly OURS to supply where it does not exist yet:\n1. The latest image per unit, with its capture time — the actual point of the alarm.\n2. A GRAB button, with the honest caveat that a grab captures a NEW image and REPLACES the one in\n   flash (Peter, 2026-07-29: "the camera needs a grab to get a new image to replace the one in\n   flash"), and that pulling without a grab returns the STORED one.\n3. Transfer telemetry per pull — chunks/repairs/dupes/elapsed. We persist all of it.\n4. Progress WHILE a pull runs. A pull is ~274 s on the bench and will be far longer from the\n   garage; without progress the page would look frozen.\n5. The camera\'s own state, honestly: `cam` is unreliable after a failed `camu ping` (B58\n   overwrites cam:1 with cam:0), so the page must not present it as fact.\n\nCAVEAT TO CARRY: from GARG a single picture is a ~20 minute operation — one command per wake\nwindow (300 s beat) for the grab, then a 32-chunk pull at -128 dBm. A UI that does not show that\nas an in-progress operation will look broken.\n\nDIVISION UNCHANGED: node-dash owns the page and is NEVER edited from here. Ours is the API plus\nhttp.md. Raise on the cross-session channel.'}
