2026-07-29 07:53:05,797 18559 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "B89 CONFIRMED: GARG's replies name packet ids that are in NO ledger row, so every one is dropped and its commands fail while the unit is answering — old firmware only, exposed (not caused) by the correlation fix", 'description': 'Measured 2026-07-29 06:37-06:47Z, after reply-correlation-off-by-one (dd9278a) shipped.\n\n```\npush stat  sentIds = [798839701, 261089903, 3664224927, 2288893124, 772027905]  -> failed 5/5\nlog:  butler: reply_id 3972863052 from !987ab80f matches no request — dropped\n      butler: reply_id 3204855756 from !987ab80f matches no request — dropped\n      butler: push for !987ab80f (id ms5pn4hr.3) was already failed when its answer arrived\n```\n\nGARG replied. The reply_ids it threaded to appear in NO row\'s sentIds for that unit, so\nsettleByReplyId dropped them and the request timed out through all five tries.\n\nNOT CAUSED BY THE FIX, BUT EXPOSED BY IT — stated plainly because it would be easy to misread as\na regression. Before dd9278a, `onReply`\'s positional fallback would accept a reply whose id did\nnot match, so GARG\'s answers were being credited BY LUCK rather than by identity. That is the\nsame defect class the fix removed (10 of 22 verbs answered by the previous command\'s reply). The\nfix is correct; what it revealed is that GARG\'s ids never matched in the first place.\n\nTHE ASYMMETRY THAT POINTS AT THE CAUSE, and it is not yet proven:\n- BNCH (fw 2-260729-x, new): correlates perfectly. 22-verb sweep, 0 mismatches, ids match every\n  time, both by the timing fast path and by settleByReplyId.\n- GARG (fw 2-260727-120, OLD): no reply id has matched since the fix.\nBoth are addressed by BROADCAST (units.<id>.dm=false), so the transport is not the difference.\nThe remaining difference is the firmware. SUSPECT: what the old build threads reply_id to.\nNOT ESTABLISHED — do not act on it without reading the 2-260727-120 reply path.\n\nIMPACT TODAY: limited, because GARG is being swapped out 2026-07-29 and the unit going to the\ngarage is the one that correlates correctly. It would bite the moment an unflashed unit came\nback into service — which is exactly what the returning GARG hardware will be.\n\nDO NOT "FIX" THIS BY RESTORING POSITIONAL MATCHING. That would re-introduce B86/off-by-one on\nevery unit to paper over one unit\'s id mismatch. A timeout beats a wrong receipt.'}
2026-07-29 08:08:58,981 18559 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'http-md-data-ownership', 'title': 'http.md must state WHICH DATA IS OURS: generic mesh streams vs the additive data we compute — so there is never doubt where a displayed field came from', 'steps': ['Investigate: DONE. Measured 2026-07-29. (a) /v1/mesh/devices publishes flat `hops`/`rssi`/`snr` with no age and no radio attribution, duplicating what mesh-gw already streams — that duplication is the source of the doubt. (b) /v1/mesh/nodes returns an IDENTICAL shape for ours and foreign ({id,num,name,hops,lastHeard,ours,raw}), so base+additive is already the architecture. (c) our /nodes returned 3 nodes while the dash header showed 17, so node-dash is NOT sourcing its node list from us despite http.md §1 forbidding direct mesh-gw reads for anything this API covers.', 'Document: add an OWNERSHIP section to docs/api/http.md — the one-line rule (we publish only what we measured or computed; anything the mesh already streams we do not restate), the additive catalogue with per-field provenance, the two boundary cases (per-radio reception is additive not a restatement; 260/261 are ours by frame, but beat/acks/radios are ours by COMPUTATION on standard ports), and the open questions for node-dash.', 'Implement: the doc change. Then, separately and under its own task, REMOVE the duplicated flat hops/rssi/snr from /devices — not part of this doc task.', "Observe: the doc states, for every field we publish, whether it is ours and how it was obtained. A reader can answer 'where did this number come from' without reading code.", 'Track: raise on the xsession channel with node-dash — questions and ambiguities only, after the doc exists. A contract change is NOT binding until they ack it.']}
