2026-07-29 08:10:35,683 18559 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'http-md-data-ownership', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter, 2026-07-29: "the reason for us owning the mesh and the data and node-dash ONLY owning the\nUI was to ensure that the data you see and the data that node-dash shows are IDENTICAL... right\nnow, the data we are providing to node dash is incomplete and inaccurate / stale... I cannot\ntrust the hops nor the signal strength values on the page, I suspect many others are also stale."\n\nAnd, decisively: "it should use the same stats for our custom device as it does for any other\ndevice. it already has those streams setup and working for months now. it\'s the ADDITIVE data\nthat we have and own which it needs to know about, such that if I ask it to display specific\ninfo, there is no doubt where that comes from."\n\nTHE RULE THAT FALLS OUT: we publish only what we MEASURED or COMPUTED ourselves. Anything the\nmesh already streams, we do not restate.\n\nMEASURED 2026-07-29, the three facts that set the shape:\n1. /v1/mesh/devices carries flat `hops`/`rssi`/`snr` with no age, no radio, no source, ALONGSIDE\n   radios.<addr>.direct.{rssi,snr,at} + directAgeMs. Two versions of one fact; the undated one is\n   what the page renders. That IS the doubt.\n2. Base+additive is already the architecture: /v1/mesh/nodes returns an identical shape for ours\n   and foreign ({id,num,name,hops,lastHeard,ours,raw}); /nodes/:target merges enrichment.\n3. The single-source rule is ALREADY broken: our /nodes returned 3 nodes, the dash header showed\n   17 — so node-dash is not sourcing its node list from us, although http.md §1 already says\n   "do not talk to mesh-gw (:8001) directly for anything this API covers".\n\nTHE CORRECTION THE DISCUSSION PRODUCED, recorded because it reverses my first proposal: the fix\nfor hops/rssi/snr is NOT to timestamp our copies. It is to STOP PUBLISHING THEM. A timestamped\nduplicate still leaves two answers to one question.\n\nPHASING (Peter\'s two phases, plus a blocking question, with his phase 1 corrected):\n  P0 BLOCKING, theirs to answer: which fields does the page take from us vs mesh-gw? Without it\n     "fix the stale data" has no measurable acceptance.\n  P1 DOCUMENT ownership in http.md. No code, no UI. THIS TASK.\n  P2 DELETE the duplicated flat hops/rssi/snr from /devices. Needs node-dash\'s ack — it is a\n     removal from a contract they consume. Own task.\n  P3 PROVIDE EVERYTHING ADDITIVE, unfiltered (Peter\'s phase 2), on the condition the discussion\n     established: every value carries its own provenance (at / *AgeMs / *Source). Without that\n     condition P3 undoes P2.\n  P4 node-dash renders it. Theirs, never edited from here.\n  ORDERING CONSTRAINT: P3 must not precede P2, or the page gains more ways to show a number of\n  doubtful origin.\n\nBOUNDARY CASES that must survive review:\n- Per-radio reception is ADDITIVE, not a restatement: the generic stream gives one value from\n  whichever radio reported last, undated; ours is per-radio, direct-only, timestamped. The same\n  GARG packet reads -96 dBm on the omni and -117 on the yagi.\n- Ports 260/261 are ours by FRAME. Peter\'s port-number instinct is right for frames, but beat,\n  acks and radios are derived from STANDARD-port telemetry plus our own send ledger — so the\n  boundary is ownership of the COMPUTATION, not the port.\n- No base key ever changes meaning based on `ours`. A key with two meanings is worse than a stale\n  one.\n\nPROCESS, per Peter: the doc comes FIRST, then the xsession channel carries questions and\nambiguities only. Nothing in docs/api/ is binding until node-dash acks it.'}
2026-07-29 08:10:59,468 18559 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'node-page-rehash', 'title': 'SUPERSEDED IN PART by http-md-data-ownership — the data-provenance half of this task moved there, with a phasing agreed with Peter 2026-07-29', 'description': 'This task\'s step 2/3 (per-radio reception, and the fields from devices-answer-the-questions\nneeding http.md) are now the subject of a dedicated task: `http-md-data-ownership`.\n\nWHY IT MOVED. Peter reframed the problem on 2026-07-29 from "the page shows the wrong things" to\n"we cannot tell where a displayed number came from":\n\n  "it should use the same stats for our custom device as it does for any other device. it already\n   has those streams setup and working for months now. it\'s the ADDITIVE data that we have and\n   own which it needs to know about, such that if I ask it to display specific info, there is no\n   doubt where that comes from."\n\nThat makes the HOPS and SIGNAL complaints in this task symptoms of one cause, measured 2026-07-29:\n/v1/mesh/devices publishes flat `hops`/`rssi`/`snr` with NO age, NO radio and NO source, alongside\nthe qualified `radios.<addr>.direct.{rssi,snr,at}` + `directAgeMs`. Two versions of one fact, and\nthe undated one is what the page renders.\n\nALSO MEASURED, and it changes this task\'s assumptions: our `/v1/mesh/nodes` returned 3 nodes while\nthe dash header showed 17. node-dash is NOT sourcing its node list from us, despite http.md §1\nforbidding direct mesh-gw reads for anything this API covers. So "fix our data and the page\nimproves" cannot be assumed — which fields the page takes from us is the BLOCKING question (P0).\n\nSTILL LIVE IN THIS TASK, and not moved: everything about the page itself — the HOPS tile rendering\na 13 Jul value with live weight, lat/lon as raw tiles, battery+voltage duplication, the missing\nreach/next-wake/reliability panels, and the CONTROL menu finding (4 of 6 submenus are "Coming\nsoon", no Images page).\n\nDO NOT start the UI work before P0 is answered and P2 has shipped; otherwise the page is being\nbuilt against fields that are about to be removed.'}
