2026-07-29 08:46:37,297 24922 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'node-page-reachability', 'title': "WO1 — node page reachability: render pac-host's delivery/wake/radio facts", 'steps': ["Phase 1 — Investigate: map the node page's current field sources and every render site", 'Phase 1 — Investigate: confirm the pac-host contract once services ships its four fixes', 'Phase 2 — Document: write docs/modules/pac-host.md changes + browser spec for the reachability tiles', 'Phase 3 — Implement (Domain 1): widen src/pac-host.js to carry the reachability fields into pac_host_status', 'Phase 3 — Implement (Domain 2): render reachability tiles on the node page with kind+age qualifiers', 'Phase 4 — Observe: Playwright validation in both themes at 1600x1000, against real pac-host data', 'Phase 5 — Track: check_specs.py exits 0, hashes updated, commit, report evidence to services']}
2026-07-29 08:46:43,803 24922 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter can answer "can we reach this unit, and when is its next chance" from the node page alone, without asking anyone.\n\nThat is services\' acceptance criterion, verbatim, on xsession work order [wo1-reachability]. It is not ours to soften.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS NOW: Peter is about to be ~8000 km away for six months. Today the node page answers what a unit IS and almost nothing about whether we can REACH it — which is the only reason anyone opens it.\n\nROLE: node-dash is the FOLLOWER under /xlead. Leader = services (Peter: "you will drive this, it will follow"). STATE is HOLD. Nothing is implemented until services replies GO on the xsession item.'}
2026-07-29 08:47:11,077 24922 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': '## Known / Unconfirmed split — read this before touching anything\n\n### KNOWN (measured from our own source, 2026-07-29)\n\nThe browser reads exactly FOUR fields out of pac-host\'s `units[]`: `id`, `num`, `shortName||name`, `present`. Proof: `public/app-control.js:33-36` is a four-key `.map()` and nothing else touches `units[]`.\n\nEverything else pac-host publishes — `acks{}`, `nextWake`, `beat`, `wakesSeen/wakesExpected`, `txRadio`, `radios{}`, `awake`, `slp`, `mode`, `fw` — arrives in the 30 s `_poll()` and is DISCARDED.\n\nSo this is NEW UI over data already being delivered and thrown away. It is not a rendering fix.\n\nData path today: `src/pac-host.js:_poll()` → `GET /health` + `GET /mesh/devices` → `_units` → `connectMessage()` → WS `pac_host_status` → `app-ws.js:67` → `this.pacHostStatus` → `app-control.js:controlDevices()`.\n\nEvery node field on every other page is mesh-gw\'s, not pac-host\'s. Confirmed and accepted by services.\n\n### DOMAIN SPLIT (CLAUDE.md — no fix may span domains in one task)\n\n- Domain 1 (`src/pac-host.js`): stop discarding the fields; carry them into `pac_host_status`. Server computes every display string and relative time — BROWSER_CONTRACT.\n- Domain 2 (`public/`): render tiles on the node page. Zero decisions, zero derivation.\n\nThese are steps 4 and 5. If they cannot be done as one task under the domain rule, step 5 splits into its own task before implementation — decide at Phase 2, not now.\n\n### UNCONFIRMED — services owes us answers; do not design around a guess\n\nTheir three self-reported defects, all blocking their GO:\n1. `nextWake` null has two meanings; `wakeSource` disambiguates but lives only in `GET /v1/mesh/mode/:target`, not `/devices`. They are moving it. (NOTE: we are not "discarding" wakeSource — it has never been offered to us.)\n2. `wakesSeen 11` vs `wakesExpected 10` = 110%. Cause unestablished.\n3. `acks` currently reports `verb:"push"` — their own housekeeping poll, not a command anyone issued. Rendering that as "can we reach it" would be false.\n\nOur six open questions to them (xsession #20):\n4. **AGE — the biggest one, and not covered by their three.** Only `acks.settledAt` carries a timestamp. `awake`, `slp`, `txRadio`, `mode`, `fw`, `beat`, `windowMs` are bare values. That is exactly the HOPS-tile defect services filed against US. Asked for PER-FACT time, not a per-block `lastHeard` — a single block timestamp is what caused the HOPS bug.\n5. When `present:false`, which fields stay meaningful and which are frozen last-known? If all freeze together, one card-level "as at HH:MM" suffices; if independently, per-fact timing is required.\n6. "Never tried" must render as unknown, not as failed. Empty `acks{}` on an uncommanded unit is not unreachable. Wanted explicit in the contract.\n7. Is `acks` a map keyed by verb, or one object with a `verb` field? "Can we reach it" is answered by the most recent attempt of ANY kind, not a per-verb table.\n8. Epoch **milliseconds** everywhere — say which fields are seconds. We have already been bitten: their ledger is ms, `fmtAgo` takes seconds, and the divide is silent and plausible.\n9. No pre-formatted relative strings from them. Send instants; node-dash owns the wording.\n\nAnswered by us, awaiting their action:\n- `windowSource: "assumed"` → PUBLISH IT, do not omit. A blank is indistinguishable from "we never asked". Render assumed de-emphasised + labelled, same as the SIGNAL tile. Apply value+source pairing to everything, incl. `awake` (measured vs inferred from `slp`).\n- `acks` must keep SENT and DELIVERED visibly separate. Never collapse to one success boolean — that boolean would have shown a green tick through the whole of 2026-07-28, when mesh-gw reported "sent" while every send was refused.\n\n### PRECEDENT TO COPY, NOT REINVENT\n\nOur own SIGNAL tile already states kind + age: `-116 dBm · Fair · -6.5 dB · direct 45m ago`. Services cited it as the correct pattern. Every reachability tile follows it. The HOPS tile currently does NOT and is a confirmed bug — but it is OUT OF SCOPE here (separate task; raise, do not fix).\n\n### OUT OF SCOPE — raise, do not fix\n\n- HOPS tile qualifier (own task)\n- Images / Camera page = WO2, blocked on services building a progress source. Predecessor at `reference/alarm-integration/public/push.html` (547 lines).\n- The four "Coming soon" Control submenus\n- Traceroute universal timeout; possible move of traceroute to services (Peter\'s call)\n- Uncommitted `traceroute-header-button` work in `public/`\n\n### EXIT\n\n`python scripts/check_specs.py` prints "All specs current." Then completion reported to services on the xsession item WITH EVIDENCE — what changed by file/route, and the acceptance criterion MEASURED after the change, not predicted (/xlead). Services verifies before any next GO.'}
2026-07-29 08:47:38,454 18559 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'devices-honest-fields', 'title': 'WO1 blocker: /devices hands out facts that cannot be dated or trusted — per-fact age, wakeSource, awake source, acks excluding our own housekeeping, and a >100% wake rate', 'steps': ["Investigate: DONE, measured 2026-07-29 and confirmed against source. (1) wakeSource is in /mode/:target but NOT /devices, so nextWake:null cannot be told from 'we do not know' — index.js:998 vs the /mode route. (2) wakesSeen 11 vs wakesExpected 10 = 110%. (3) _ackSummary (index.js:280) takes requests({unit,limit:1}) — the latest row of ANY kind — so our internal `push stat` housekeeping is what 'can we reach it' currently reports. (4) FIELDS FREEZE INDEPENDENTLY: hops/rssi/snr come from the gateway roster and go null when it drops the node (index.js:973-975), while beat/wakesSeen/mode come from our persisted model and hold last-known — so one block timestamp would repeat the HOPS bug. (5) `awake` is a bare boolean with no indication whether it was measured or inferred from slp. (6) lastHeard is epoch SECONDS while lastHeardMs/nextWake/settledAt/radios.*.at are epoch MS — two units, near-identical names, in one object.", "Document: spec at docs/history/devices-honest-fields.md. Sibling <field>At keys in epoch ms (additive, cannot break node-dash's existing four-field read), wakeSource in /devices, awakeSource measured|inferred, acks excluding internal housekeeping, the null/never-commanded contract, and a decision on the seconds-valued lastHeard.", 'Implement: only what the spec names.', 'Observe: re-measure every field on both units. Acceptance: no field that can go stale lacks an At; nextWake:null is explainable from /devices alone; wake rate <= 100%; acks reflects a REAL command or is null; a deliberately never-commanded unit renders null not failed.', 'Track: hash, all 32 suites, commit, THEN issue GO on [wo1-reachability] stating what was measured — not that it is finished.']}
2026-07-29 08:48:17,112 24922 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': '## CONTRACT ANSWERS FROM SERVICES — xsession #22/#23, 2026-07-29. Confirmed from their source, not memory.\n\nThese move items out of the UNCONFIRMED list in the plan note. Read both together.\n\n### CONFIRMED: fields freeze INDEPENDENTLY — per-fact age is mandatory\nTheir `index.js` builds a device from two sources with different lifetimes:\n- from the gateway roster `r`: `hops`, `rssi`, `snr` → go **NULL** when the node leaves the roster\n- from their own persisted model: `beat`, `beatSource`, `phase`, `wakesSeen/Expected`, `wakeErrMs`, `mode`, `present` → **HOLD last known**, never null out\n\nSo a single card-level "as at HH:MM" is ruled out — it would be the HOPS bug again, one age painted over facts of different ages. Per-fact it is.\n\n### CONFIRMED: sibling `<field>At`, not a `{value,at,source}` wrapper\nAgreed by both sides. We required **mechanical naming**: strictly `<field>` + `"At"` / `"Source"`, no abbreviations, no special cases — so age can be resolved *by construction* instead of a hand-written lookup table that rots when they add a field. If a field cannot carry an `At`, they omit the sibling entirely (an absent sibling is detectable; a creatively-named one is not).\n\n### CONFIRMED: `acks` is a SINGLE OBJECT — the LATEST OVERALL, not a map keyed by verb\nTheir `_ackSummary` does `requests({unit, limit:1})` and summarises that one row whatever the verb. It already answers "can we reach it" by the most recent attempt of any kind. They refused to make it a per-verb map, correctly: the question is binary, a verb table invites the wrong page.\n\n### CONFIRMED: `acks` NULL means NEVER COMMANDED, and must render UNKNOWN\n`_ackSummary` returns null when the unit has no request rows at all. Being written into their http.md rather than left for us to infer.\n\n**Expect an apparent regression:** once they strip their internal `push` housekeeping (their defect 3), units that today show acks will legitimately go to null. That is honest — nobody has actually commanded them. We committed in writing to render it as *"no command has been sent to this unit"* — NOT a blank, NOT a failure. Peter must be able to tell "not yet asked" from "asked and got nothing" at a glance.\n\n### CONFIRMED: time units — exactly ONE seconds field, and it is being deleted\nIn `GET /v1/mesh/devices`: `lastHeard` is **epoch seconds** (their `index.js:998`, straight from mesh-gw `last_heard`). `lastHeardMs`, `nextWake`, `acks.settledAt`, `radios.*.direct.at`, `radios.*.lastAt` are all **epoch ms**. Every new `<field>At` is epoch ms without exception.\n\nWe confirmed we do not consume their `lastHeard` (four-field read, `app-control.js:33-36`) and told them to **delete it**. One time unit in the object.\n\n### CONFIRMED: sent vs delivered stay four numbers, never one boolean\nTheir own evidence for why: `sends` counts POSTs mesh-gw **accepted**, not transmissions — **15 of GARG\'s 131 sends one day never left the radio, and every one was counted as a send.** Hence `transmitted` / `notSent` / `unknownSent` / `delivered` as four numbers. `unknownSent` exists because a send with no status yet is neither transmitted nor refused; folding it into `transmitted` would be the same assumption wearing a new name. They committed not to simplify it later "for our benefit".\n\n### CONFIRMED: `windowSource: "assumed"` is published, not omitted\nAnd value+source pairing extends to `awake`, which becomes measured (heard inside a window) vs inferred (from `slp`). It is currently a bare boolean — exactly the kind of thing that gets believed.\n\n---\n\n## SERVICES\' OWN BLOCKING WORK — five items, was three\n1. `wakeSource` into `/devices` beside `nextWake`\n2. `wakesSeen`/`wakesExpected` > 100% — establish, then bound or explain\n3. `acks` to exclude their internal housekeeping traffic\n4. per-fact `<field>At` on everything that can go stale, epoch ms\n5. `awake` gains a source: measured vs inferred\n\nPlus contract text for the null/never-tried case, and the `lastHeard` deletion.\n\nThey will GO when these are **shipped AND measured**, and stated they will tell us what they measured, not that they finished.\n\n---\n\n## RAISED, NOT IN SCOPE (do not fix here)\nTheir `sends`-counting defect is the same class as our own message-feed defect: pac-host-originated sends bypass `src/mesh-send.js` entirely and mesh-gw suppresses its own TX echo, so our feed showed 95 replies against 1 recorded send over 12 hours. If they ever publish a per-unit "what did we transmit" count, that is what would let us reconcile the feed — and it may be nearly free once their four ack numbers exist. Flagged to them as free information, explicitly not a request.'}
