2026-07-29 08:49:08,359 18559 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'B90 OBSERVED, UNDIAGNOSED: a GARG image pull died at 4 of 32 chunks with EDEADLINE — spotted by Peter in the pm2 log, not by us', 'description': 'Peter, 2026-07-29, from the pm2 log:\n\n```\n2|pac-host  | MeshError: image 1: deadline at 4/32\n2|pac-host  |     at Images._drive (mesh/lib/images.js:210:13) {\n2|pac-host  |   code: \'EDEADLINE\'\n2|pac-host  | }\n```\n\nWHAT IS KNOWN:\n- pid 1, 4 of 32 chunks received, then the pushDeadlineMs (900000 = 15 min) expired.\n- Thrown at images.js:210, the `throw new MeshError(...deadline at N/M...)` at the bottom of the\n  poll loop — i.e. the transfer ran the FULL 15 minutes and gave up, it did not fail fast.\n- This is almost certainly the GARG pull attempted ~06:06-06:11Z, the same one whose replies were\n  being dropped (B89). NOT CONFIRMED — the log line Peter pasted carries no unit and no timestamp,\n  which is itself a finding: an image error should name the unit.\n\nWHAT IS NOT KNOWN, and must not be assumed:\n- Whether the device stopped sending after 4 chunks, or sent more and we did not receive them.\n- Whether the give-up guards fired at all. maxStale/maxUnanswered exist precisely so a stuck\n  transfer reports WHICH SIDE stopped rather than waiting out the full deadline\n  (push-giveup-guards-dead). A generic "deadline at 4/32" is the symptom that task was created to\n  remove, so either the guards are still not firing or this failed a different way.\n- Whether B89 (GARG\'s replies dropped because their reply_ids match no ledger row) is the cause.\n  If our repair/query control frames were answered and the answers discarded, the receiver would\n  see silence and stall exactly like this. PLAUSIBLE, NOT ESTABLISHED.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: 15 minutes of a deployed unit\'s airtime and battery to produce one unattributed\nerror line. On the unit that goes to the garage today, that is the difference between diagnosing\nremotely and driving out.\n\nRELATED: image-transfer-progress-log shipped this morning adds per-progress logging, which would\nhave shown WHERE it stalled and whether repairs were being sent. This failure predates a chance to\nobserve it with that in place.\n\nNOT FIXED, NOT DIAGNOSED. Recorded so it is not lost.'}
