2026-07-29 09:36:55,471 27975 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'CONFIRMED: public/app.js (422 lines) and public/app-rotator.js (272 lines) have NO module spec — check_specs cannot report what is absent', 'description': '**Status: CONFIRMED** (verified 2026-07-29)\n\n```\n$ ls docs/modules/ | grep -E "app-rotator|^app\\.md"\n(no output)\n$ wc -l public/app.js public/app-rotator.js\n  422 public/app.js\n  272 public/app-rotator.js\n```\n\nNeither file has a spec in `docs/modules/`. `scripts/check_specs.py` reads `docs/modules/*.md` and validates each against its declared `source:` — so **a module with no spec passes silently.** The validator cannot report an absence it was never told about.\n\nMeasured this turn: `check_specs.py` prints 70 `ok` lines, and `ls docs/modules/*.md | grep -v _TEMPLATE | wc -l` is 70. The counts match, so nothing is being skipped — but 70 is the number of specs that *exist*, not the number of modules that *should* have one.\n\n**Partial cover only, and it is incidental:** `public/app.js` appears in `docs/modules/browser-playwright-audit.md`\'s 27-file `source:` list, so an edit to it does invalidate *that* spec\'s hash. `public/app-rotator.js` appears in no spec\'s source list at all — it can be changed with zero effect on `check_specs`.\n\n**How it surfaced:** task `traceroute-header-button` modified both files. `app.js` forced a hash bump via the audit spec; `app-rotator.js` gained a whole new exported handler (`toggleTraceroute`) and the validator was indifferent.\n\n**Not yet known:** whether other `public/` or `src/` modules are equally uncovered. A full audit of every source file against every spec\'s `source:` list has NOT been run.\n\n**Disposition:** own task — writing two module specs from scratch is not a side-effect of a UI change. Prerequisite for it to mean anything: a check that every `src/*.js` and `public/*.js` appears in at least one spec\'s `source:`, otherwise the same gap reopens silently.\n\nSame root cause as the memory note "check_specs can\'t see missing specs" — this is that note with two named files and a measurement attached.'}
