2026-07-29 09:37:48,844 27975 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Four files in `public/`, all shipped at `9648d08`. Full detail in `docs/TRACEROUTE_MASTER_SWITCH_SPEC.md` §3.\n\n| file | change |\n|---|---|\n| `public/index.html:187-196` | TRACE button, after the rotator group and **outside its `x-show`** |\n| `public/app.js:145` | `tracerouteEnabled: true` — display cache only |\n| `public/app-ws.js:108` | read from the `settings` WS event |\n| `public/app-rotator.js:87-101` | `toggleTraceroute()` — optimistic, **reverts on failure** |\n\nOutside the rotator\'s `x-show` is the one non-obvious choice: hiding the control when the rotator is disconnected would remove it at exactly the moment you still want to stop traceroutes.\n\n## Verified live 2026-07-29, 1600×1000, both themes, screenshots read\n\n- OFF matches backend: `GET /config` → `false`; `btn-ghost opacity-40`, title "…OFF — click to enable"\n- click enables: `GET /config` → `true`; `btn-outline btn-success`, title "…ON — click to disable"\n- **state survives a full page reload** → still ON\n- click disables: `GET /config` → `false`\n- 0 console errors (1 pre-existing Tailwind CDN warning)\n- **Left OFF**, which is how Peter set it\n\nBackend gate proved *reached* separately at `d691303`: `enabled=false` → `traceroute disabled`, `enabled=true` → `timeout !987ab80f`.\n\n## Why this task blocked the whole repo\n\nIts four files sat modified and uncommitted since 2026-07-27 with specs unhashed. `public/app-ws.js` is `app-ws.md`\'s source; `public/app.js` and `public/index.html` are two of `browser-playwright-audit.md`\'s 27. **No task in this repo could show a clean `check_specs` until this one closed.** Both rehashed here.\n\nExit: `All specs current.` — 70 `ok` against 70 specs on disk, so the validator checked everything rather than silently skipping.\n\n## Raised, not fixed\n\n`public/app.js` (422 lines) and `public/app-rotator.js` (272 lines) have **no module spec**. `check_specs` validates only specs that exist, so `app-rotator.js` — which gained a whole new exported handler here — can be changed with zero effect on it. `app.js` is covered only incidentally, via the audit spec\'s source list. Own task; the ledger append failed on a tool error and must be retried.\n\n## Commits\n\n- `9648d08` — this task\n- `5ea2df7` — follow-up: `docs/REACHABILITY_SPEC.md` had been left untracked while `9f6e7fa` cited it'}
