2026-07-29 09:38:21,185 28111 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'camera-rtc-recovery', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'RE-RAISED BY PETER 2026-07-29, SWAP DAY, with a NEW suspicion that is not yet recorded anywhere:\n\n  "the esp32-cam issue with the fact that it is powered via it\'s internal battery connector (from\n   the rak) and needs me to manually press and hold the button to power it on and we suspect that\n   it is actually awake all of the time?"\n\nTHE FIRST HALF IS ALREADY SPECCED ABOVE and unchanged: power comes from the RAK\'s VBAT with no\nUSB, the firmware latches G33 in setup() and relies on ext0 deep sleep, and a fully powered-off\nTimer Camera X has exactly two documented ways back on - the PWR button held 2 s, or a BM8563 RTC\nalarm. We use neither.\n\nTHE SECOND HALF IS NEW. "Awake all of the time" is NOT what B80 says. B80 records only that the\ncamera LATCHES its own power and cannot be switched off remotely. Whether it then SLEEPS is a\nseparate question and has never been measured. If it does not sleep, it is drawing continuously\nfrom the same cell the alarm depends on, and that - not the latch - would be the real cause of\nthe drain.\n\nTHE DECISIVE TEST IS NOW CHEAP, and Peter has the instrument. An LTC4150 coulomb counter is inline\non the RAK\'s battery connector (http://192.168.10.181/), and because the camera is powered FROM\nthat connector the meter measures BOTH DEVICES TOGETHER. So:\n\n  1. measure with the camera connected      (2026-07-29 08:31Z: 23.3 mA avg, 25.5 mA now,\n                                             560 mAh/day, est life 15.0 h, 90% of run time in\n                                             the 14.7-31.6 mA bands, 9.8% at ~0.01 mA)\n  2. disconnect the camera, measure again\n  3. THE DIFFERENCE IS THE CAMERA\'S DRAW. No inference required.\n\nMY READING OF STEP 1, OFFERED AS INFERENCE AND NOT AS FACT: 23 mA looks like an always-listening\nRAK (~20 mA) plus a camera drawing very little. An ESP32 with the camera powered and awake would\nbe 100-200 mA and would be unmissable in that histogram. So the camera is PROBABLY sleeping. That\nis exactly the kind of "probably" this measurement replaces with a number.\n\nCONFOUND THAT MUST BE CONTROLLED: the RAK under that meter currently has slp=0 (sleep DISABLED,\nalways-listening, confirmed from /v1/mesh/devices the same minute), so most of the 23 mA is very\nlikely the RAK, not the camera. Measure the camera delta BEFORE changing the RAK\'s sleep state, or\nthe two changes land in one number and neither is attributable.\n\nALSO NOTE, and it is the reason this matters today: USB MASKS THE WHOLE PROBLEM. M5\'s own docs say\n"when using external power, the device will remain powered on". Any test of the power-loss failure\nmust be on BATTERY with NO USB, or it will pass and mean nothing.'}
