2026-07-29 10:00:26,549 27975 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': '## ROOT CAUSE FOUND AND PROVEN, 2026-07-29 — Peter: "is HOPS and Signal correct? I am sceptical… the header stats don\'t match the reachability stats"\n\nHe was right. The new Reachability section (`1f8842b`) put honest per-radio numbers beside the header tiles and the header lost.\n\n### The proof: the header displayed a reading that does not exist\n\nScreenshot of GARG\'s node page showed header SIGNAL = **`-98 dBm · Good · 6.8 dB · direct 4m ago`**.\n\nMeasured against `signal_history` for num 2558179343, last 24 h:\n\n| rx_device | rows | best rssi | worst rssi | best snr |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `E9:B0:3F:17:27:91` (OMNI) | 211 | −125.0 | −128.0 | −15.25 |\n| `F4:12:FA:39:F7:B6` (YAGI) | 300 | −112.0 | −128.0 | −3.25 |\n\n**Zero rows with positive SNR in 24 h. No row anywhere near −98 dBm.** The displayed value matched neither radio and corresponded to no stored measurement. (The only +6 dB GARG readings on record are 27 Jul at −17 to −33 dBm — the bench period before it went to the garage.)\n\n### Two independent defects, both in `buildSignal`\'s inputs\n\n`src/node-status.js:426`:\n```js\nsignal: buildSignal(node?.rssi ?? null, node?.snr ?? null, stmts.latestSignalTs.get(num)?.ts ?? null)\n```\n\n**1. The VALUE comes from `nodes.rssi/snr`, which is ungated.**\n`handleNodeInfo` (`src/persist.js:459-475`) writes mesh-gw\'s NodeInfo aggregate `node.snr` / `node.rssi` straight into the `nodes` table — **no direct-gate, no `relay_node` check, no radio attribution**. That is the gateway\'s nodedb figure, which can be a relayed last-hop reading or a cached value from either radio.\n\n`signal_history` by contrast IS correctly gated and attributed (`635370d` added `rx_device`, `4340f56` added the `relay_node` gate). So the two stores legitimately diverge — one is disciplined, the other is not.\n\n**2. `upsertNode` never clears a stale value.** `src/db.js:423-424`:\n```sql\nsnr  = COALESCE(excluded.snr,  snr),\nrssi = COALESCE(excluded.rssi, rssi),\n```\nA null does not overwrite. A wrong value written once persists **indefinitely** until some other non-null write replaces it.\n\n**3. Value and age come from DIFFERENT SOURCES.** The `desc` string `"direct 4m ago"` is built from `latestSignalTs` — the newest `signal_history` row — while the number beside it came from `nodes`. So the tile asserts freshness and directness about a value that may be neither. That is the "mixed source" in this task\'s title, now with a measurement attached.\n\n### Also confirmed: the two views disagree in the same payload\n\nOne `node_status` response, same instant:\n\n```\nHEADER SIGNAL      -116 dBm / -8.8 dB    desc "direct 1m ago"\nREACHABILITY YAGI  -112 dBm / -5.8 dB    direct 6m ago · 12 direct, 0 relayed\nREACHABILITY OMNI  -127 dBm / -16.0 dB   direct 6m ago ·  3 direct, 0 relayed\n```\n\nHere the header happened to match our own latest YAGI row (09:57:11, −116, −8.75) — so it is not *always* wrong. But it collapses two radios 15 dB apart into one unlabelled scalar, and pac-host\'s `radios.*.direct` was 5 minutes staler than ours at that moment. Three numbers, three provenances, one tile that names none of them.\n\n### HOPS — separate, and worse in one respect\n\n`hopsField` prefers a verified traceroute. GARG\'s is **`verified 14 Jul 17:51` — 15 days stale**, rendered at full live-data weight. It does at least state its age, which is why it is a lesser defect than SIGNAL.\n\nBut it **cannot self-heal**: every traceroute dispatch currently returns `status: timeout` (unexplained, still open), so the verified value will never refresh. A tile whose only refresh path is broken is effectively frozen, and nothing on the page says so.\n\n### Disposition\n\nOut of scope for `node-page-reachability`, which is closed and committed. Recorded here rather than fixed, per the report-don\'t-fix rule. This task now has its root cause and its evidence; the remaining work is the fix, not more investigation.\n\nThe Reachability section is deliberately left alone — it renders pac-host\'s per-radio numbers faithfully and is the *correct* view. The header is what needs to change.'}
