2026-07-29 11:31:53,230 27975 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': '**node-dash runs identically with the alarm absent.** The alarm is a PLUGIN: additive, self-contained, and it changes nothing about node communications, stats or messages.\n\nPeter, 2026-07-29: *"node-dash exists with or without the alarm. alarm is addative, it changes nothing about node communications, stats, messages. do NOT get that wrong. the alarm is a plugin. it is ADDATIVE and node dash must be able to exist with or without it. alarm related code is supposed to be self contained and not mixed in with core."*\n\n**I broke this rule in `1f8842b` and this task undoes it.** `src/node-status.js` — a core module that builds `node_status` for ANY node in the mesh — now imports `pac-host.js` and carries 164 lines of alarm-specific logic (`buildReachabilitySection`, `deliveryField`, `nextWindowField`, `wakeReliabilityField`, `WAKE_SOURCE_TEXT`, `AWAKE_SOURCE_TEXT`).\n\nAlso violates `reference/alarm-integration/INVENTORY.md`: *"New integration work must use an explicit module boundary; code must not be copied back into shared dashboard modules."*\n\n## Acceptance — a test, not an assertion\n\n1. **`pac-host` STOPPED → every page renders identically.** That is the property, and it is the one to measure.\n2. **`node_status` payload byte-identical before/after** for a non-alarm node; and for an alarm unit, identical while pac-host is up.\n3. `grep "pac-host" src/node-status.js` returns nothing.\n\n## Not in scope — do not touch\n\n- The header Signal / Least hops / Verified hops work (`cc2e55f`) is **pure core** — `signal_history`, `messages`, `traceroute_history`. No alarm dependency. It stays exactly as it is.\n- `9f6e7fa` (`value_grid` desc) and `2dd2540` (desc wrapping) are generic presentation. Untouched.\n- `src/pac-align-api.js`, `src/pac-command-api.js`, `src/pac-host.js` — the plugin\'s own files. Correct as they are.\n- The mesh-ownership question. Peter has clarified it is **alarm-scoped only**: core mesh access via mesh-gw is unchanged. services must be corrected separately — they stated it as blanket.'}
