2026-07-29 12:15:53,726 27975 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'CONFIRMED: src/ws-relay.js has 7 pac-host couplings in a core module — plugin state reaches the browser through core', 'description': '**Status: CONFIRMED** (grep, 2026-07-29)\n\n```\nsrc/ws-relay.js:3     import * as pacHost from \'./pac-host.js\'\n:339  pacHost.events.on(\'change\', …)\n:340  broadcast(pacHost.connectMessage())\n:341  for (const num of pacHost.unitNums()) _hintNodeStatus(…)   ← added by 1f8842b\n:346  pacHost.events.on(\'queuesChanged\', …)\n:349  pacHost.events.on(\'alignChanged\', …)\n:773  ws.send(JSON.stringify(pacHost.connectMessage()))\n:776  ws.send(JSON.stringify(pacHost.queuesMessage()))\n:778  ws.send(JSON.stringify(pacHost.alignMessage()))\n```\n\n`ws-relay.js` is core — it serves the WS for every page. **Six of these pre-date 2026-07-29**; only `:341` was added by `1f8842b`, inside an already-coupled block, so it created no new crossing.\n\n**Why this is a real breach and not pedantry.** Peter, 2026-07-29: *"the alarm is a plugin. it is ADDATIVE … alarm related code is supposed to be self contained and not mixed in with core."* Task `alarm-plugin-boundary-restore` removed the equivalent breach from `node-status.js` and gave core a `registerNodeSection` extension point. `ws-relay.js` has no such point: plugin state (`pac_host_status`, `pac_host_queues`, `pac_host_align`) is broadcast by name from core.\n\n**Consequence today:** deleting the alarm requires editing `ws-relay.js`, so node-dash does NOT yet run unmodified without the plugin — the property is satisfied for `node_status` and not for the WS broadcast path.\n\n**Not yet known:** whether a generic hook (e.g. `registerWsBroadcaster(fn)` + `registerConnectReplay(fn)`) is sufficient, or whether the replay-on-connect ordering constraints make it harder. Not designed, not attempted.\n\n**Why not fixed with `alarm-plugin-boundary-restore`:** that task\'s acceptance was behaviour preservation proven by payload diff, and it deliberately did not touch `ws-relay.js` (stated in `docs/PLUGIN_BOUNDARY_SPEC.md` §5). Fixing this means redesigning how plugin state reaches the browser, which is its own task with its own spec.\n\nRelated: `docs/PLUGIN_BOUNDARY_SPEC.md`, `reference/alarm-integration/INVENTORY.md` ("browser contribution: explicit navigation/page descriptors").'}
