2026-07-29 12:16:16,350 27975 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Shipped at **`b16304b`**. Three files; spec `docs/PLUGIN_BOUNDARY_SPEC.md`.\n\n| file | change |\n|---|---|\n| **NEW** `src/alarm-sections.js` | the 164 lines, moved **verbatim**, + `pac-host` import; self-registers |\n| `src/node-status.js` | lost the import, the block and the call site; gained `registerNodeSection` |\n| `src/index.js` | one line — `import(\'./alarm-sections.js\')` beside `pacHost.start()` |\n\n```js\nexport function registerNodeSection(fn) { _sectionProviders.push(fn); }\n```\n\nProviders run before core sections, receive `(num, { perRadio, now, since })`. Returning `null` contributes nothing — so *"no plugin installed"* and *"plugin has nothing to say"* are one code path, and core needs no `if (pluginPresent)`.\n\n`ctx.perRadio` is passed in, never re-queried: same `stmts.latestDirectPerRadio` array the header\'s Signal tile uses, so the header↔section agreement from `cc2e55f` stays true by construction.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Verbatim move, proven:** 163 lines removed, 163 moved, diffed → **zero differences**.\n\n**Plugin-absent test** — the property itself. With `index.js`\'s single import commented out:\n\n| node | plugin wired | plugin absent |\n|---|---|---|\n| GARG | `reachability, device_vitals, signal, environment, air_quality, detections` | `device_vitals, signal, environment, air_quality, detections` |\n| coreA | `device_vitals, environment` | unchanged |\n| coreB | `device_vitals` | unchanged |\n\nNo load errors either way. Wiring restored, section returned. **Stricter than stopping pac-host, and it never touched the live gateway.**\n\n**One shape difference chased, not waved past:** GARG gained `Wake reliability` between captures because services\' fencepost fix landed mid-task (`wakesExpected` null → 2). The rule `if (exp == null) return null` is byte-identical in the moved code.\n\n`fmtUntil` deliberately dropped from core\'s imports — `nextWake` belongs to the plugin, and an unused import would imply core does countdowns.\n\n`check_specs`: **All specs current**, 71 ok / 71 on disk.\n\n## Raised, not fixed\n\n`src/ws-relay.js` has **seven** pac-host couplings (`:3`, `:339/340/341/346/349`, `:773/776/778`), six pre-dating this work; only `:341` was mine and it sat inside an already-coupled block. So the plugin-absent property holds for `node_status` but **not** for the WS broadcast path — deleting the alarm would still require editing `ws-relay.js`. Fixing it means redesigning how plugin state reaches the browser: own task, own spec. Stated in `docs/PLUGIN_BOUNDARY_SPEC.md` §5. *(Ledger append failed on a tool error — retry.)*'}
