2026-07-29 12:18:19,203 28111 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'B98 CONFIRMED AND QUANTIFIED (was UNVERIFIED, reported by node-dash) — and it is NOT a deadlock.\n  MEASURED BY ME 2026-07-29 against the live service:\n      GET /v1/mesh/images/!8cee336b/99999      HTTP 502 in 75.02 SECONDS\n      GET /v1/mesh/images/!8cee336b/progress   HTTP 200 in 0.0015 s   (the new local endpoint)\n  CAUSE: images.js list() calls this.command(node,\'push\',[\'stat\']) — a RADIO round-trip through\n  the butler, aimed at the unit\'s next RX window and retried across windows. The unit is deaf ~99%\n  of the time on a 300 s beat, so a "read" endpoint legitimately takes MINUTES. node-dash\'s client\n  gave up at 25 s and reported http 000. Nothing was broken; a read was built on a round-trip.\n  FIXED by ADDING GET /images/:target/progress (local, synchronous, transmits nothing) rather than\n  changing /images/:target, whose live semantics grab() depends on.\n\nB100 CONFIRMED — the image pid is NOT range-checked before the mesh round-trip, so a bad pid costs\n  75 seconds and then fails on encoding anyway.\n      GET /v1/mesh/images/!8cee336b/99999\n      -> {"error":"The value of \\"value\\" is out of range. It must be >= 0 and <= 65535.\n          Received 99999"}  HTTP 502, after 75 s\n  A pid is a uint16. 99999 is unanswerable BY INSPECTION, before any radio is touched, and could\n  be a 400 in microseconds. Instead the service queued it, spent a wake window on it, and returned\n  a 502 whose text is an internal encoder message.\n  THREE THINGS WRONG: airtime spent on a request that could never succeed; a caller punished with a\n  75 s wait for a typo; and a 502 (upstream failed) for what is a 400 (you asked wrongly).\n  NOT FIXED — outside the attached spec\'s described change. Own task, small.\n\nB101 CONFIRMED, POTENTIALLY FATAL TO THE SERVICE — an AUTO-ADOPTED push creates a promise whose\n  rejection NOBODY handles.\n      images.js onFrame():   const entry = this._startTransfer(node, f.pid);   // promise ignored\n      images.js _startTransfer():  entry.promise = this._drive(entry, opts).finally(...)\n  _drive() THROWS on deadline/abort (`MeshError: image 7: deadline at 1/5`, code EDEADLINE,\n  images.js:221). For a REQUESTED image this is fine — get() awaits entry.promise and catches it.\n  But the auto-adopt path in onFrame() awaits nothing, so a spontaneously-pushed image that hits\n  its deadline produces an UNHANDLED PROMISE REJECTION. Node 15+ terminates the process on those\n  by default, so this is a candidate for an unexplained pac-host restart.\n  FOUND while writing the progress test: the identical shape crashed the test runner AFTER the\n  suite had printed "images OK: 49 assertions passed" and exited 1 — a green suite with a dead\n  process, which is exactly how this would look in production.\n  NOT REPRODUCED IN PRODUCTION and I am not claiming it has happened — pm2 restart counts should be\n  checked against the image-pull log before treating it as the cause of anything.\n  NOT FIXED — the attached spec does not describe it. Own task, and it should be soon.'}
