2026-07-29 15:08:55,452 27975 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'Phase 6 — make the boundary property a REPEATABLE test in tests/test_playwright.py, and run it', 'description': "`docs/WS_PLUGIN_HOOKS_SPEC.md` §7 and `docs/PLUGIN_BOUNDARY_SPEC.md` §7 describe the verification I ran by hand. A property that is only ever checked by hand is a property that regresses.\n\nAdds to the existing audit:\n\n1. **`/control` route** — it is a real page with six sub-tabs and was **absent from `ROUTES` entirely**. A gap, not a new feature.\n2. **`audit_plugin_boundary`** — the additivity property, testable from the browser without unwiring anything:\n   - an **alarm** node's page has the `Reachability` section\n   - a **core** node's page does **not**\n   - **every core section behaves identically on both** — the plugin adds, it never alters\n3. **stat-desc clipping guard** — regression cover for `2dd2540`. `scrollWidth > clientWidth` on any `.stat-desc` means a provenance qualifier is being silently truncated, which is the defect that hid `886 failed since`.\n\nNode ids come from env (`PLAYWRIGHT_ALARM_NODE_ID`, `PLAYWRIGHT_CORE_NODE_ID`) so the test is not wired to this installation."}
