2026-07-29 15:20:13,444 27975 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': '**Core must not name the alarm.** `src/ws-relay.js` serves the WebSocket for every page and referenced `pac-host` **seven** times — an import, three event handlers, three replay sends. Deleting the alarm therefore meant editing core.\n\nPeter, 2026-07-29, on being told six of the seven pre-dated that day\'s work: *"makes no difference if they were added today or not they break the rules and need fixing."*\n\nCompletes what `b16304b` began — that removed the alarm from `node-status.js`; this removes it from the last core module that named it.\n\n## Acceptance — measured, not asserted\n\n1. `grep "pacHost" src/ws-relay.js` → nothing\n2. WS message set **and order** identical before/after\n3. Plugin unwired → **zero** `pac_host_*`, core set otherwise intact\n4. Live broadcasts still fire — the wiring proven *reached*, not merely present\n\nSpec: `docs/WS_PLUGIN_HOOKS_SPEC.md`'}
2026-07-29 15:20:33,262 27975 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Shipped: **`cde43bc`** (boundary) + **`e237b12`** (test).\n\n## Hooks\n\n```js\nexport function registerWsWiring(fn)      { _wsWirings.push(fn); }\nexport function registerConnectReplay(fn) { _connectReplays.push(fn); }\n```\n\nPlugin needs three things, all generic: `broadcast`, a replay contribution, `hintNodeStatus(num)` (bound wrapper — `_hintNodeStatus` stays private). Wiring moved verbatim to `src/alarm-ws.js`.\n\n## The regression caught before commit\n\n`_wsWirings` is read **once** by `attachWsRelay` (`index.js:263`); `_connectReplays` is read **per connection**. With `import(\'./alarm-ws.js\')` inside `server.listen()` at line 313, the wiring registered too late:\n\n| plugin import | connect replay | live broadcasts / 110 s |\n|---|---|---|\n| dynamic, inside `listen()` | worked | **0** |\n| static, top-level | worked | **21** |\n\n**Invisible from the UI** — the Control page paints correctly on load and then never updates. Fixed by static top-level imports; that ordering is now a documented invariant.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Connect order unchanged: `bridge_connected, pac_host_status, pac_host_queues, pac_host_align, settings, …`\n- Live cadence matches pac-host\'s polls: `pac_host_queues` ~5 s, `pac_host_status` ~30 s\n- Plugin unwired: **0** `pac_host_*`, no load errors, core set intact (`packet`, `node_list`, `device_list`, `rotator`, `tilt_cal`, `message_history`, `env_history`, `range_test_log`, `node_status_update`)\n- Two constraints preserved deliberately: **replay position** (between bridge-state and `settings`) and **no enrichment** on the replay path\n\n## Phase 6 — the property is now a test\n\n`audit_plugin_boundary` in `tests/test_playwright.py`: alarm node has `reachability`, core node does not, core sections on both, no plugin label in either header, no truncated `.stat-desc`. **12/12.** Full audit **303 passed**.\n\n`/control` added to `ROUTES` — it had never been audited at all. 24 checks, both viewports, all passing.\n\nTwo mistakes of mine in the first test version, both fixed: the "core node" was `646426545` = `0x2687afb1` = **OMNI**, a gateway radio, passed as a decimal when the route takes `!hexid`; and the header check demanded `Least hops`, which comes from `messages` so a node sending no text legitimately lacks it — the assertion failed on correct behaviour.\n\n## Left open, deliberately\n\n`invalid activeTab is replaced` still fails. Premise is stale: treats `control` as a *removed* tab, but Control was rebuilt (`control-section-ia`, 2026-07-25). Confirmed unrelated — `audit_invalid_persisted_tab` is untouched by this diff and fails in isolation. **The test is wrong, not the app.** Own task, not a silent edit inside this one.\n\n`check_specs`: All specs current.'}
