2026-07-29 20:42:44,527 53368 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'From the 2026-07-29 history /investigate: (a) sub-quantum runs (shorter than one 0.17067 mAh pulse interval — common on sparse DUTs) record used/avg 0.0 and render as "0,0,0,0" rows, reading as data corruption; (b) records saved pre-NTP stamp t=time()≈0-60, colliding in the client histMap (keyed by t — ledger L1) and in rewriteRuns t-matching, so note-edit/delete can hit the wrong record and rows collapse/vanish. Fix: firmware stamps a unique-in-boot sentinel band (900000000+millis/1000, always <1e9) when the clock is invalid so records never collide and the UI can label them "no clock"; dashboard renders zero measurements as "—", dates <1e9 as "no clock", and the stop toast says when a run captured nothing measurable.'}
