2026-07-30 11:46:29,121 80352 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'sleep-floor-unexplained', 'title': '0.506 mA in System-OFF, ~1000x the datasheet — the number that decides whether the 1-year target is reachable on this hardware at all', 'steps': ['MEASURED 2026-07-30: unit 1FC4, System-OFF, radio held in reset, NFC off, unused GPIO disconnected -> 0.506 mA (one quantum over 1214 s, so charge is exact). Datasheet says ~0.4 uA. Fixes took it from 1.99 mA, so F1/F3 worked and this is what remains.', "DECISIVE TEST, Peter's: base board alone, no RAK fitted. Splits 'the RAK19007 does this' from 'the module does this'. Nothing else can separate them.", "Calibrate the instrument: run the LTC with NOTHING connected. Whatever it reads is the floor every measurement today sits on. I have NOT verified the rig's power topology and must not guess at it again.", 'CANDIDATE, unverified: the RAK4631 carries external QSPI flash (PIN_QSPI_CS 26, IO0-3, SCK 3) and nothing puts it into deep power-down before sleep. A serial flash idling in standby rather than DPD is a plausible continuous draw of roughly the right order. One command, not a pin audit.', 'Confirm System-OFF is actually entered — statically verified reachable with __DSB(), NOT empirically confirmed on hardware.', 'Decide: if the floor really is ~0.5 mA, the 0.251 mA one-year target is unreachable without a hardware change, and that conclusion must be stated plainly rather than chased in firmware.']}
