2026-07-30 11:54:05,981 80352 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'v3-wire-seam-not-fork', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'CORRECTION 2026-07-30, Peter: "mcpp-chat no longer exists."\n\nStep 5 of this task names mcpp-chat as the cross-session channel. That mechanism is GONE. The\ncurrent mechanism is the `xsession` skill (folder-per-channel, cursor-tracked shared board), with\n`xlead` when one session must lead.\n\nThe rule itself is UNCHANGED and still binding: a change to anything in docs/api/ is not binding\nuntil the other party has acked it. Only the transport for that ack has changed. Read step 5 as\n"announce and get the ack over xsession".\n\nSTALE DOCUMENTATION THIS EXPOSES — reported, not fixed, because both are CLAUDE.md changes and\nneed their own task and spec:\n\n  - services/CLAUDE.md, section "The other sessions": "Cross-session chat (`mcpp-chat`) is how you\n    reach them. A change to anything in `docs/api/` is not binding until the other party has acked\n    it there."\n  - mt-alarm/CLAUDE.md, section "Changing a contract": "...is not binding until the other party has\n    acked it on the cross-session chat channel."\n\nBoth point a future session at a channel that does not exist, on the one rule the coordination repo\nexists to enforce. That makes it worth fixing properly rather than leaving as a footnote here.'}
