STARTING ANY SLICE: verify against the code that the thing being extracted is actually\nin main.cpp and not already living somewhere correct. That check costs minutes and would have\ncaught this.'}
2026-07-30 11:59:23,069 80352 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'refactor-modular-libs', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'MASTER TASK for the firmware decomposition. Every lib-* slice task belongs to this one.\n\nmcpp tasks are FLAT — there is no parent/child link — so this task is the master by CONVENTION:\nit owns the spec, and every slice references that spec instead of restating it. If you are\npicking up a lib-* task, read this one and its spec FIRST.\n\nSPEC (the single source of truth):  device/docs/history/refactor-modular-libs.md   (commit 55fbdc3)\n\nGOAL: main.cpp becomes a BOOTSTRAP — construct the modules, wire them, run the loop. Everything\nelse moves into independently developable libraries under device/lib/, each with its own\nlibrary.json so the floor rig, TimerCAM and v3 can consume any subset via lib_extra_dirs.\n\nWHY (Peter, 2026-07-30): "we can tweak individual modules and have a clean share between\nversions", and "the finer the grain / role split the better". Split by ROLE, never by\nconvenience. Sleep/power currently exists in THREE copies (v2 main.cpp, rak-sleep-floor,\ntimercam-chunk) and F11 landed in only one of them — that duplication is the concrete cost this\ntask exists to remove.\n\nTHIS IS A SEPARATE CONCERN FROM POWER OPTIMISATION. Peter, 2026-07-30: "2 different issue,\n1) refactor for better development / tuning / sharing across versions, and power optimisation."\nThe refactor is justified on its own even if the power numbers were perfect. The two streams do\nNOT block each other: the binary-identity gate is what makes them independent, because a pure\nmove cannot change a measurement. Power work lives in power-levers-dcdc-gpio-nfc and\nsleep-floor-unexplained, NOT here.\n\nTWO KINDS OF ACCEPTANCE — conflating them is the likeliest way this fails:\n  - pure moves (every slice except mt-wake) -> THE v2 BINARY IS UNCHANGED. Symbols, section\n    sizes, disassembly. Evidence, not a promise; checkable on every build forever.\n  - mt-wake, the v2/v3 seam -> introduces an interface, so it can NEVER be binary-identical.\n    Acceptance is behavioural equivalence measured on hardware: same beat, same window width,\n    same wake timing as v2 today.\n\nHARD RULE: there is no mt-globals. If one appears, the refactor has failed — it is main.cpp\'s\ncoupling under a new name and nothing could then be developed independently. State is owned by\nexactly ONE module. If a piece of state has no natural owner, the BOUNDARY is wrong.\n\nDO NOT ABSORB ANYTHING INTO transport/ — it is vendored, with its own library.json, tests and\nCHANGELOG.\n\nSTATUS 2026-07-30: definition committed (55fbdc3). NO slice tasks created yet. Slice 1 as\noriginally ordered was investigated and ABANDONED before any code was written — see the note on\nthis task. Start at mt-sleep or mt-rails instead, and verify against the code that what you are\nextracting is actually in main.cpp before beginning.'}
