2026-07-30 12:14:25,941 82417 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'sleep-floor-unexplained', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'SOAK STATUS — unit 1FC4, System-OFF floor test. All figures below RE-QUERIED at 11:13:40 UTC\n2026-07-30, not carried from earlier in the session.\n\nLTC4150 project "RAK4631 floor 1FC4" (id rak4631-floor):\n\n    state      running        armed      false\n    pulses     4              run_secs   4207\n    used_mah   0.68           avg_ma     0.53\n    vbat       3.97           soc        100.0\n    tgt_secs   7200  -> the 2 h backstop lands at roughly 12:03 UTC\n\nINTERVAL-DERIVED CURRENT: 0.4382 mA  =>  209 days on 2200 mAh.\nComputed pulse-to-pulse: 3 quanta (pulses 1->4) x 0.17067759 mAh over 4207 s. This is the number\nto quote, NOT avg_ma and NOT used_mah, because charge between pulses is exact while the FIRST\npulse can carry pre-run charge (the integrator holds up to one quantum; /CLR is unsoldered on\nthis build).\n\nREFINES, DOES NOT CONTRADICT, this morning\'s figure. The first estimate was 0.5061 mA from a\nSINGLE interval (pulse 1 -> pulse 2, 1214 s). Three intervals now give 0.4382 mA. Expect it to\nkeep tightening; treat anything from one interval as provisional.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT ESTABLISH:\n  - DOES: the F1/F3 fixes worked. The pre-fix firmware measured 1.99 mA and would have produced\n    ~23 pulses by now; we have 4.\n  - DOES: something is connected and drawing - vbat reads 3.97, so this is not an open circuit.\n  - DOES NOT: establish that the chip is in System-OFF. That was verified STATICALLY (the\n    SYSTEMOFF write is reachable and barriered, no svc in setup) and has NEVER been confirmed\n    empirically on hardware.\n  - DOES NOT: attribute the 0.44 mA to anything. ~0.44 mA against a ~0.4 uA datasheet figure is\n    ~1000x, and the cause is UNKNOWN. Candidates are in this task\'s steps: RAK19007 quiescent,\n    the QSPI flash never being put into deep power-down, and System-OFF not actually taking.\n    I do not know the LTC rig\'s own power topology and must not guess at it again.\n\nACCEPTANCE FROM THE SPEC, FOR THE RECORD: the pass condition was 0-1 pulses in 2 h (<=0.085 mA).\n4 pulses at 4207 s FAILS that. The firmware defects are fixed; the FLOOR is not explained.\n\nBLOCKING NOTHING. Peter, 2026-07-30: the refactor and power optimisation are "2 different issue".\nThis measurement does not gate refactor-modular-libs and must not be treated as if it does.'}
