2026-07-30 14:04:00,314 88795 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "Target is /usr/share/pac/dev/pio/projects/rak-sleep-floor -- outside mt-alarm entirely, a standalone rig built solely to answer sleep-floor-unexplained's (866) question: what the bare RAK4631+RAK19007 draws in System-OFF, isolating hardware floor from application-level defects. 11 firmware defects found; F1 (svc 51 landing in FreeRTOS's own vPortSVCHandler made the SYSTEMOFF write unreachable) and F3 (SX1262 never slept) each independently voided the measurement. Both fixed. Unit flashed first time, MAC F2:43:18:A0:1F:C4 reported. LTC4150 soak stood up and run: result 0.4382 mA interval-derived (209 days on 2200mAh) -- FAILS the spec's own acceptance (0-1 pulses/2h). Rig placed under version control 2026-07-30 (e4abf73 fixes, c89a3f4 records the result), hashed with spec-hash.py, closing the Track-phase blocker that had left the rig producing quoted numbers with no history."}
