2026-07-30 14:11:04,385 88795 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'B1 [UNVERIFIED, simplification] src/main.cpp:3553,3574,3585 -- three independent reads of NRF_POWER->USBREGSTATUS & POWER_USBREGSTATUS_VBUSDETECT_Msk within ~30 lines of each other, all in setup(), all before anything could change the register. :3553 latches it into g_usbHost; :3574 and :3585 each re-read the raw register instead of reusing g_usbHost, which is already correct by that point. Not a bug (VBUS cannot change mid-boot), just redundant. Found while investigating lib-rails (task 879) -- explicitly NOT touched there, since a pure-move refactor must preserve exact read structure, not opportunistically simplify it. Worth a follow-up task if anyone wants the cleanup.'}
