2026-07-30 14:11:24,285 88795 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Move these exact lines from src/main.cpp into lib/mt-rails/MtRails.{h,cpp}:\n- static bool g_usbHost (line 64) -> class member, exposed via isUsbHost()\n- NRF_POWER->DCDCEN = 1 (line 3542, with its full comment block 3517-3541) -> MtRails::begin()\n- pinMode(PIN_PWR_EN,OUTPUT)/digitalWrite HIGH (3545-3546) -> MtRails::begin()\n- pinMode(PIN_3V3S_EN,OUTPUT)/digitalWrite HIGH (3547-3548) -> MtRails::begin()\n- VBUS read + g_usbHost latch (3553) -> MtRails::begin() returns/sets via readVbusPresent()\n- the two redundant raw VBUS reads (3574, 3585) -> call MtRails::readVbusPresent() in place, unchanged structure (see bug B1 -- not simplified here)\n- digitalWrite(PIN_3V3S_EN,HIGH) reassert (3602) -> MtRails::sensorRailOn()\n- digitalWrite(PIN_3V3S_EN,LOW) in doSleep (3911) -> MtRails::sensorRailOff()\n- g_usbHost reads at 3892, 3949 -> MtRails::isUsbHost()\nNOT moved: LED_GREEN pinMode (3544, textually adjacent, different owner), Wire/Serial.end/begin (3891-3892 partial, 3946-3949 partial -- those calls stay in main.cpp/future mt-sleep, only the g_usbHost READ inside the Serial guard moves), SERIAL_CAM lines (uart-float-before-sleep\'s territory), the sleep delay loop.\nDesign decision: PIN_3V3S_EN on/off during sleep/wake is control-flow-called FROM main.cpp\'s doSleep (mt-sleep doesn\'t exist as a module yet), but the PIN OWNERSHIP is mt-rails per the spec\'s table ("what is energised"). So main.cpp calls mtRails.sensorRailOff()/On() rather than touching the pin directly -- keeps single ownership even before mt-sleep is extracted.'}
