2026-07-30 14:17:34,535 88716 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'decisions-for-peter', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'D7 — AUDIT OF THE 14 DEVICE/CAMERA TASKS SITTING IN THE SERVICES PROJECT, 2026-07-30.\nPeter asked for housekeeping BEFORE moving them. Audited against device/ and timercam-chunk git\nhistory, which is the only trustworthy evidence — see the finding about spec status fields below.\n\nCLOSED (2) — acceptance actually evidenced:\n  806 fw-macaddr-nodeinfo   fbfd548 "acceptance MET on the wire — BNCH publishes 2f:86:8c:ee:33:6b,\n                            last4 == node id". Implemented in 8b9e13f.\n  778 rx-window-configurable  spec status reads "IMPLEMENTED + VERIFIED 2026-07-27 on 2-260727-116".\n\nDELIBERATELY NOT CLOSED (4) — CODE SHIPPED, NO RECORDED ACCEPTANCE. This is the judgement call:\n  794 hop-zero-direct            aa416e1\n  811 fw-reply-ack-configurable  3b5f9c7\n  816 fw-per-unit-pki-key        c7a8345\n  819 fw-key-repair-on-authfail  a859876\nEach has a commit. NONE has a recorded acceptance measurement I could find — I grepped their specs\'\nAcceptance/Observe sections and found no MET / measured / verified result. 819\'s mcpp note contains\nstrong measured evidence ("routing_ack delivered from=!8cee336b at 21:19:59, first PKC DM success\nsince 15:52") but that proves the DIAGNOSIS, not that the fix was verified after landing.\nI could have closed all four and made the list tidy. Closing a task whose acceptance was never\nmeasured is exactly the "downgrade a finding to close cleanly" failure /idiot forbids, so I left\nthem open. IF YOU\'D RATHER THEY WERE CLOSED, SAY SO — but somebody should confirm the four actually\nwork before they are.\n\nNOT IMPLEMENTED — investigate-only, correctly open (4):\n  820 fw-forget-evicts-transport-key   no spec file, no commit\n  779 fw-version-only-on-change        investigate done; the defect (a bump per INVOCATION) is live\n                                       and just bit the refactor\'s binary-identity gate\n  776 wake-lifecycle-logging           spec exists, no implementing commit found\n  808 fw-state-the-schedule            no spec file; sits at step 9, unclear\n  777 agc-reset-necessity              PARKED BY YOU 2026-07-27 — untouched, stays parked\n\nCAMERA (3) — belong to pio/projects/timercam-chunk, a THIRD project, same class of problem as 863:\n  839 cam-sensor-standby   SHIPPED AND MEASURED: a8a96b8 (the OV3660 is 56 mA, the ESP32\'s sleep\n                           mode was never the problem) + 92a0183 (3.20 mA over a full hour, ~9.4x).\n                           Should be closed; I did not, to avoid another full-list dump.\n  835 cam-fw-never-sleeps  partially shipped, 5f68c15 makes the sleep decision observable\n  782 camera-rtc-recovery  investigate done, not implemented\n\nFINDING WORTH MORE THAN THE HOUSEKEEPING: THE SPECS\' status: FIELDS ARE ALL STALE.\nEvery one I checked reads "status: in-progress", INCLUDING fw-macaddr-nodeinfo, whose own commit\nsays acceptance was met on the wire. So the spec status field is not maintained and cannot be used\nto answer "what shipped". Only git can. That silently breaks the /idiot Track phase\'s purpose, and\nit is why this audit had to be done from commit messages.\n\nSECOND FINDING: four tasks have shipped code with no acceptance recorded anywhere. That is Phase 4\neither skipped or never written back. Worth a rule: a spec whose code has landed must carry its\nmeasured result, or the task stays open.\n\nNEXT STEP (Peter\'s instruction): move these to device in BATCHES, coordinating over xsession — NOT\nin one go. The 3 camera ones need a home decision first; timercam-chunk is neither device nor\nservices.'}
