2026-07-30 14:21:13,994 88795 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'B2 UPDATE, confirmed by services independently against committed HEAD (a1d92b1): 4 occurrences in the committed file, not 2 (my "2" was counted against my already-mid-edit working tree, which had folded the boot-time HIGH writes into mtRails.begin() by that point -- not wrong, just a different reference point, noted for clarity). All setup()-time writes (:3547-3548, :3602 in committed HEAD) never re-run after first sleep; only :3911\'s LOW survives -- finding stands unchanged.\nHARDWARE IMPACT, from services: 336B (bench) was flashed ~10:00 UTC today from a tree already containing 926d2c7, sleeping on a 900s beat since -- its 3V3S rail has been LOW since first sleep, so SHTC3/PIR have been unpowered for hours. GARG (deployed unit) was NOT reflashed today -- NOT affected by this specific defect, on older firmware.\nRoot cause: 926d2c7\'s own commit message claimed "Restored before any sensor read — see the wake path" -- no such restore exists; services (author) confirmed this was a false claim in the commit, caught only by lib-rails\' extraction walking the code.\nOwnership confirmed: services will not touch main.cpp (mid-extraction, and generally "yours from now"); fix lands as a NEW step on task 852, NOT folded into any lib-rails pure-move commit (would break the binary-identity claim). BNCH needs reflashing once fixed before trusting any of its PIR/env numbers.'}
