2026-07-30 14:33:15,359 88795 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'Rail-restore fix (B2) implemented: mtRails.sensorRailOn() added to doSleep()\'s wake section, builds clean, code re-read confirmed correct. Attempted to flash 336B to verify on hardware -- FAILED on first attempt (1200bps touch dropped the board off USB, "Couldn\'t find a board on the selected port"), and it has NOT re-enumerated after ~30s passive checking. Per the documented hazard (a looped upload wedged a board 7h on 2026-07-27), NOT retrying -- stopped, no further touches. Committing the fix now regardless (code-correct, builds clean), but the AMENDMENT\'s stated acceptance (336B reflashed + 2 sleep/wake cycles showing real sensor data + PIR detection) is NOT met -- DEFERRED pending the board coming back (may need a physical reset-button press). This does not change 852\'s remaining steps 5/6 (Observe/Track for the original Wire/Serial/3V3S current measurements) -- still open, now also blocked on the same unreachable board.'}
