2026-07-30 14:34:33,362 88795 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': "B3 [UNVERIFIED, from services, plausible] 336B's post-flash-attempt USB silence -- NOT the DFU wedge (services confirmed via lsusb: no 239a device at ALL, not even bootloader 0029/002a/802a, and the Adafruit bootloader DOES enumerate -- so the board is not sitting in DFU). Hypothesis: g_usbHost (now mtrails::MtRails::usbHost_, src/main.cpp mtRails.begin()) is latched ONCE at boot from NRF_POWER->USBREGSTATUS.VBUSDETECT (commit 1ca63db, services'). If VBUS was momentarily absent/marginal during the 1200bps-touch reset pulse, the board could boot with usbHost_=false and NEVER call SERIAL_USB.begin() -- running perfectly, beating on schedule, permanently invisible over USB until POWER-CYCLED (not reset) with VBUS already present. Test: BNCH's next scheduled mesh beat, due ~13:44 UTC (900s beat, last mesh contact ~13:29:34 UTC, before the flash attempt) -- services has a watcher running. If it beats on schedule, hypothesis confirmed as leading explanation and this becomes a real defect (any USB-disturbing restart can strand a unit invisible over USB) worth its own task. If no beat by ~13:58 UTC, board is genuinely gone, different problem. NOT testing/touching the board further until this resolves. If confirmed, recovery is a power cycle WITH USB connected first, not a reset."}
