2026-07-30 15:12:59,662 88795 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'F7 (from power-levers.md/task 864): "no GPIO returned to input-disconnected before sleep". This is NEW code, not an existing block to move -- unlike lib-rails/lib-sleep this is not a pure-move slice. Real risk, per services: many pins are owned by libraries (LoRa SPI, I2C, USB, SERIAL1, QSPI) without an explicit pinMode call in main.cpp, several alias (28/29/30/2/3 appear as both PIN_A*/PIN_SPI1_* and PIN_QSPI_*), and disconnecting on a guess breaks the radio or filesystem silently. Doing the pin inventory (safe, read-only) now; NOT implementing until the inventory is trustworthy and reviewed, and NOT flashing/measuring until hardware is available again (336B currently blocked on a Proxmox USB-passthrough bug, per services -- device/CLAUDE.md \'ONE flash, one attempt\' discipline applies once ready).'}
