2026-07-30 15:34:55,172 1251 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'B4 [CONFIRMED, design hazard not a live bug] PIN_PIR (io.h, =10) aliases PIN_NFC2 (variant.h, =10) -- the SAME physical GPIO. Also PIN_NFC1 (variant.h, =9) aliases PIN_BUTTON1 (variant.h, =9), unused currently but same trap. Found during lib-gpio (881) Investigate, doing the pin inventory for F7 (GPIO-disconnect-before-sleep, task 864). Not a current defect -- PIR works fine today since nothing else claims pin 10 -- but a held-pin list for F7 that reasons from "NFC pins are now GPIO (F4, 37982ce) and unused, disconnect them" would disconnect the PIR by accident, since PIN_NFC2 and PIN_PIR are literally the same pin under two names. Any future F7 implementation must build its held-list from pins, not from symbolic names, or de-duplicate by GPIO number first.'}
