2026-07-30 16:48:29,325 1251 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Leaf slice (tier 7) of refactor-modular-libs. serviceSerialConsole() (src/main.cpp:4174-4209) conflates two concerns: byte-accumulation-into-a-line (generic, reusable -- floor rig/TimerCAM/v3 all want this) and command-dispatch (RxPacket construction, g_cmdFromSerial, handleCommand -- deeply main.cpp/mt-cmd specific, the "biggest single lump", not this slice). Boundary: mt-console owns ONLY the byte-reading -- a poll(Stream&, char*, size_t) that returns true with a trimmed line when \\r/\\n arrives, false otherwise (mirrors the exact while(available()) loop structure so multiple complete lines in one call still each get processed). g_cmdFromSerial, RxPacket, handleCommand() call stay in main.cpp\'s serviceSerialConsole(), now calling mtConsole.poll() in its while loop instead of reading SERIAL_DBG directly.'}
2026-07-30 16:48:37,382 1251 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'MtConsole API: bool poll(Stream &in, char *lineOut, size_t cap) -- internal buffer+length become class members (persist across calls exactly like the original function-static line[80]/n did). Reads in.available()/in.read() in a loop; on \\r or \\n with n>0, null-terminates into lineOut (capped at cap-1) and returns true, resetting internal state; on \\r/\\n with n==0 (blank line) continues without returning; otherwise buffers the char (capped at internal buffer size 80, matching original) and continues the loop. Returns false when in.available() is exhausted with no complete line yet.'}
