ib-pir/lib-env.\nbuildStatus alone is a legitimate pure move (17 read-only external reads, passed as refs/pointers —\nsame DI pattern as mt-sleep/mt-rails). buildConfig/broadcastConfig is arguably mt-config\'s, not\nmt-status\'s. broadcastDebug pulls in mesh/radio + B5\'s PIR-window globals — extracting it now means\neither (a) mt-status reaching into radio/PIR-window internals prematurely, or (b) deferring\nbroadcastDebug to when mt-wake/a PIR-window module exist. Recommending narrow scope: buildStatus\nonly for this slice, defer buildConfig (→ mt-config), broadcastDebug (→ needs mt-wake first),\nbroadcastCalc (small, could go either way — low risk to include or defer).\n\nBug ledger: no new findings this phase (g_pirTsCount array reinforces existing B5, not a new entry).\n\nSTOPPING for user approval before Phase 2 (Document/spec) per /idiot — scope decision above is\nPeter\'s call, not mine to assume.'}
