2026-07-30 17:50:00,979 1251 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'text': "B6 (UNVERIFIED, out of scope for lib-reply): after the routine `pio run -e rak4631_camuart -t upload`\nfor lib-reply (2026-07-30, ~17:00), the console showed `boots=1 (por=0 pin=0 DOG=0 soft=1\nlockup=0)` and `settings: defaults (hb=60s det=3/10s)` on the very next boot. mtBoot's\nflash-persisted boot log was at boots=230 as of lib-pir's hardware-confirmed flash earlier the\nsame session, and persisted settings were previously non-default (bench role config had been\nexercised repeatedly all day). Both InternalFS-persisted structures (boot log AND settings)\nreset to defaults SIMULTANEOUSLY, which points at the whole LittleFS partition being wiped, not\nan isolated bug in either module. rst reason was soft=1 (SREQ, 0x4) — the normal DFU-triggered\nreset, same as every other flash today. NOT caused by lib-reply's changes (diff touches only\njsonBuild/JField/jn/jf/js/jb in main.cpp + a new lib, no flash/settings/boot code). Root cause\nunknown: could be a full-chip-erase side effect of a normal `pio -t upload` under some condition,\nor residual from an earlier upload today. Evidence: this exact same flash procedure was used for\nall 7 prior slices today with boots incrementing correctly each time (verified: boots=230 after\nlib-pir) — so this is NOT how upload always behaves, something changed. Worth a dedicated\ninvestigation if it recurs; for now recorded as observed-once."}
