2026-07-30 19:49:40,351 1251 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'text': 'B6 CORRECTION, 2026-07-30: my earlier "did not recur" update was premature -- it recurred, partially.\nlib-config\'s hardware verification flash shows HB\'s boot= field (mtBoot.bootCount(), :3685) reading\n2, down from 231 confirmed after lib-status. BUT this time settings persisted correctly: cfg="saved",\nand an interval 301->300 round-trip read back exactly right both times -- config store (mt-config,\nInternalFS "/settings.bin") was NOT reset. Only the boot log (mt-boot\'s own persisted state,\nseparate mechanism -- GPREGRET2 + a flash-persisted BootLog struct per lib-boot.md) reset. This\nnarrows the anomaly: it is not "the whole LittleFS partition wiped" (my first hypothesis) since\nconfig settings and boot log clearly use independent storage that can diverge. Two data points now:\nlib-reply\'s flash reset BOTH (boots=1, settings=defaults); lib-status\'s flash reset NEITHER\n(boots=231 continued correctly); lib-config\'s flash reset ONLY boot count (boots=2, settings intact).\nInconsistent pattern, no root cause identified, occurs on SOME but not all `pio -t upload` cycles.\nNot caused by lib-config\'s changes (this slice touches settings persistence only, never mtBoot).\nWorth a dedicated investigation using mt-boot\'s own tooling if it keeps recurring -- three\noccurrences in one session\'s worth of ~10 flashes is not obviously rare.'}
