2026-07-30 22:00:17,566 1041 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Repair both halves of the 14287f1 (B104) regression in the send injected into the images module, keeping B104's wake-window aiming and supersedeKey — those were correct and are not in doubt.\n\n1. mesh/index.js:119 — restore _sendRaw's resolve-and-address: _resolveOrThrow -> _addressed, then hand the ADDRESSED text plus toNum/channel to butler.enqueue, keyed by the resolved node id. send becomes async again, which is the honest shape since resolution needs I/O.\n2. mesh/lib/images.js:145 — Promise.resolve().then(() => this.send(...)).catch(...), which covers a synchronous EQUEUEFULL throw AND an asynchronous ETARGET rejection. A bare .catch() covered neither.\n3. images.js:32 — the declaration comment described the pre-B104 contract, whose absence is what let this through.\n\nSpec: docs/history/image-send-catch-regression.md. Acceptance is HTTP 200 and a non-zero byte count starting ff d8 — a rising chunk count is only the intermediate signal."}
