2026-07-30 22:17:09,661 1041 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'images-local-store-read', 'title': "B107: images.get() never reads the payload store, so a JPEG already on disk is re-fetched over the radio — the reason node-dash's Image card is empty", 'steps': ["Investigate: DONE 2026-07-30. images.get() (mesh/lib/images.js) validates the pid, checks this.active for an in-flight transfer, then goes STRAIGHT to _startTransfer — a radio round-trip. There is no store lookup on any path. Measured: a cached, complete, CRC-verified pid took 183-239 s to serve. PayloadStore has save() (store.js:126, writes <dir>/<node>/<when>_pid<pid>.jpg) but NO load or list for saved images — savePartial/loadPartial/saveStats/loadStats exist, the finished JPEG has neither. 12 JPEGs are on disk and unreachable through the API. node-dash's Camera panel says so in its own markup: 'A local read of what is already stored is being built; this panel is wired for it and shows nothing until it exists.'", "Document: spec it. Two additions to PayloadStore (listImages, loadImage) and a store-first path in images.get() with an explicit refresh override. MUST handle the directory split: payloads/336b/ and payloads/!8cee336b/ both exist because save() uses the caller's raw string, so a local read has to match across BOTH forms — use the resolveKey injected for B106 rather than moving files. RECORD THE PID-RECYCLING CAVEAT: a pid is a uint16 and recycles, so a cached pid is not guaranteed to be what the device holds under that pid now. State the trade explicitly rather than leaving it implied.", 'Implement: mesh/lib/store.js, mesh/lib/images.js, mesh/host-module.js, mesh/index.js.', 'Observe: measure the SAME pid twice — once served from disk, once forced over the radio — and report both durations. A cached fetch must return HTTP 200 with identical bytes to the radio-fetched copy (compare sha256, do not eyeball the size), and the new list endpoint must report every JPEG actually on disk (count it with find, do not trust the endpoint against itself).', 'Track: hash, commit, and tell node-dash on xsession — this is the last thing between them and a working Image card, and they should not have to ask twice.']}
