2026-07-30 22:22:12,888 1041 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'B106 + B107 CONFIRMED, FIXED (e7e8492, 160a4a1): the two remaining reasons the Camera page was blank — a transfer findable only under one key, and a picture on disk with no way to read it', 'description': 'BOTH REPORTED BY node-dash, both ours, both with their measurement not ours.\n\nB106 — images.js progress() compared the target by RAW STRING, and the stored e.node differs BY ORIGIN: a requested pull keeps the caller\'s path segment (\'336b\'), an adopted push keeps the gateway sender id (\'!8cee336b\'). node-dash polled /images/!8cee336b/progress every 2s across a WORKING pid 43238 pull and got {"transfers":[]} throughout — their page read "no transfer in flight" during a successful download. There was NO key a consumer could pass that always worked. Fixed by canonicalising both sides via a SYNC resolver (progress() must answer while a pull blocks, B98). Measured: before, ?336b found it and ?!8cee336b / ?8cee336b returned []; after, all three find it, "unit":"!8cee336b", rising 2/12 17%.\n\nB107 — images.get() never read the payload store on ANY path: validate pid, check in-flight, go to the radio. So a complete CRC-verified JPEG on our own disk was re-pulled over the air every time, 183-239 s. PayloadStore.save() had no counterpart: savePartial/loadPartial and saveStats/loadStats are paired, the finished image was written and never read. Fixed with listImages()/loadImage(), a store-first get(), ?refresh=1 to force the radio, and GET /images/:target/stored. Measured: cached 0.0033 s vs 183-239 s; sha256 17150dcc..6203de79 IDENTICAL to the radio-fetched copy (cmp confirms); endpoint 5 images = find 5.\n\nACCEPTED AND RECORDED, not glossed: a pid is uint16 and RECYCLES, so a cached pid is not guaranteed to be what the device holds under that pid now. Serving from disk by default is the deliberate trade against a 4-minute pull to render a thumbnail; ?refresh=1 is the escape hatch. The stats sidecar already holds a per-pid CRC if this ever needs tightening.\n\nSTILL OPEN, reported not fixed: payloads/336b/ and payloads/!8cee336b/ are the same split in the filesystem (save() keys the subdir on the raw string) — the read now spans both, but the directories were NOT merged; that moves files and needs its own before/after. And store.prune() still throws "retention policy not implemented", which matters more now that stored images are reachable and therefore worth keeping.'}
