2026-07-31 05:46:04,003 1041 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'floor-rig-really-sleeps', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'SOAK 1 RESULT, 2026-07-30 20:18Z -> 2026-07-31 04:44Z, 4 pulses. THE CURRENT RISES MONOTONICALLY AND THE BRACKETS DO NOT OVERLAP.\n\nQuantum 0.17067799 mAh/pulse; each transition bracketed by the 300 s poll, so every figure is a range, not a point.\n\n  arm -> p1   15148-15448 s   39.8 - 40.6 uA   (mid 40.2)\n  p1  -> p2    9606-10206 s   60.2 - 64.0 uA   (mid 62.0)\n  p2  -> p3    8789-9389  s   65.4 - 69.9 uA   (mid 67.6)\n  p3  -> p4    7504-8104  s   75.8 - 81.9 uA   (mid 78.7)\n\nConsecutive ranges are DISJOINT (64.0 < 65.4, 69.9 < 75.8), so this is not poll-quantisation noise. Mean of the three inter-pulse intervals 69.5 uA -> 3.6 years on 2200 mAh. The pass/fail from the spec still holds (we are far under the old 0.44 mA and the rig genuinely sleeps), but "<=40 uA achieved" would be FALSE: only the very first interval was at 40 uA.\n\nCAUSE UNKNOWN. Recorded as unexplained, not as a hunch:\n- vbat flat at 3.96-3.97 throughout, so not supply sag. It is also a BENCH SUPPLY, not a cell.\n- Overnight run (20:18 -> 04:44), so ambient was FALLING. nRF52 leakage rises with temperature, so temperature points the WRONG WAY to explain a rise.\n- Nothing was touched between intervals: same rig, same firmware, no intervention.\n- It rhymes with the previous rig\'s unexplained mid-run rise (0.438-0.506 -> 2.46 mA on 2026-07-30), which is still open.\n\nWHY I CANNOT ANSWER IT, AND WHAT WOULD: in System-OFF no code runs, so a rise cannot come from evolving firmware behaviour — UNLESS the board is resetting and re-entering System-OFF repeatedly, which would raise the average. I CANNOT DETECT THAT on this build: GPREGRET does not survive the bench->LTC power cycle (that was F6\'s fatal flaw) and R6\'s flash-backed log was STRIPPED from this firmware after the RadioLib+LittleFS build hung. So the one instrument that would distinguish "steady leak that is growing" from "a reset loop" is exactly the one not present.\n\nNEXT: R6 (flash-backed boot counter + RESETREAS + begin/sleep status, LittleFS ALONE this time, proven separately rather than bundled with a radio change). Watcher extended to 7 pulses to see whether the rise continues or plateaus.'}
