2026-07-31 06:01:13,443 50469 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'ALARM PLUGIN. Extends src/alarm-images.js; no new plugin file unless Phase 1 shows one is needed.\n\nThe list is page data -> WS push, never a browser GET (BROWSER_CONTRACT). The BYTES are not page data — they are a binary asset, like a font or an icon — so they need a route the browser can put in <img src>. Phase 1 must establish how that route is exposed without breaching the WS-only rule or letting a page load trigger a radio round-trip.\n\nHonesty rules that are already known and non-negotiable:\n- pid is a uint16 and RECYCLES. A cached pid is not guaranteed to be what the device holds now.\n- Label the time "saved" from savedAt (epoch MS — /progress uses ms too and fmtAgo takes SECONDS; that divide is silent when missed).\n- ?refresh=1 forces the radio path: minutes, and it costs a wake window. It must not be reachable from a page load.\n- pid 1 on !8cee336b is a 7156-byte TEST pattern, not a capture. Label it, do not silently drop rows.\n- Bind to the canonical \'unit\', not the raw \'node\'.\n\nVerify against a REAL stored image rendered in a real browser, not a fixture. Keep the plugin-absent test passing.'}
