2026-07-31 06:04:40,281 50469 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'B47 CONFIRMED (NOT OURS, but binds our design): unstored valid pid on /images/&lt;t&gt;/&lt;pid&gt; hangs &gt;45s and never takes the store path', 'description': 'Measured 2026-07-31 05:02Z during `camera-image-card` Phase 1.\n\n`GET /v1/mesh/images/!8cee336b/12345` — 12345 is a valid uint16 and is NOT in that unit\'s `/stored` list — **did not return within 45 s** and was killed by the client timeout.\n\nEvidence it did not take the store path: every stored fetch logs a line of the form\n`[images] image 50108 served from store (2685 bytes, saved ...) — no radio`.\nThe 12345 request produced **no `[images]` log line at all**.\n\nContrast, same session:\n- pid 50108 / 45886 / 60780 / 1 → 200, 1.4–14 ms, "served from store — no radio"\n- pid 99999 (out of uint16 range) → 400 in 1.3 ms\n- pid abc → 400 in 3.5 ms\n- pid 0 → 502 after **3.46 s**, log shows `image ENOIMG: pid 0 ... total 3.5s` — i.e. it did reach the device\n\nNOT verified: exactly what 12345 did on air. A butler `push` for !8cee336b was queued 45 s later, but a routine stat poll also runs on that cadence, so causation is **not** established and is not claimed. To be asked of services rather than guessed.\n\n**Design consequence for node-dash, which is the reason this is logged:** node-dash must never blind-proxy a browser-supplied pid. A stale page holding an evicted pid would hang a connection for minutes and may cost a wake window — precisely the hazard the Camera page exists to avoid. The proxy must validate the pid against the last-polled `/stored` list and 404 otherwise, plus carry its own abort timeout for the eviction race.'}
2026-07-31 06:04:47,968 50469 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'B48 CONFIRMED (OURS): docs/modules/index.md invariant is factually wrong — it claims the 3 alarm imports are the ONLY alarm reference in core', 'description': 'Written by me in commit 44e9ca5 (2026-07-30) and wrong as written.\n\n`docs/modules/index.md` Invariants says of `./alarm-sections.js`, `./alarm-ws.js`, `./alarm-images.js`: *"These three lines are the **only** permitted reference to the alarm plugin anywhere in core."*\n\nContradicted by `src/index.js` itself:\n- line 24 `import pacCommandRouter from \'./pac-command-api.js\';`\n- line 25 `import pacAlignRouter from \'./pac-align-api.js\';`\n- line 215 `app.use(pacCommandRouter);`\n- line 216 `app.use(pacAlignRouter);`\n\nBoth routers are alarm-specific (`/nodes/:num/pac-command` proxies to pac-host\'s queue; the align router likewise). So there are **seven** alarm references in `src/index.js`, not three.\n\nThe underlying architectural point is defensible — `index.js` is the composition root, and wiring plugins is what a composition root is for — but the invariant as phrased is false, and a false invariant is worse than none: the next reader either trusts it or stops trusting the spec.\n\nNeeds rewording to say what is actually meant: core modules other than the composition root must not name the plugin, and every reference in `index.js` must be a bare wiring line that can be deleted without touching anything else. Not fixed in-flight — `camera-image-card` will likely add an eighth reference, so the rewording belongs with that change.'}
