2026-07-31 10:35:08,134 50469 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'camera-capture-verb', 'title': "Take photo sends 'cam', which is a no-op error listing sub-verbs — send the real capture verb, and prove it on air", 'steps': ["Phase 1 — Investigate: what each cam sub-verb does in firmware, and what bare 'cam' actually returns", 'Phase 2 — Document: the verb, the async-reply caveat, and the firmware-cited test-image rule', "Phase 3 — Implement: send 'cam grab'; restore the test-image label with a firmware citation", 'Phase 4 — Observe: send it to a REAL unit and watch the reply and the image arrive', 'Phase 5 — Track: hashes, check_specs, UI audit, commit']}
2026-07-31 10:35:17,374 50469 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Make Take photo actually take a photo, and prove it by sending one to a real unit and watching the image arrive.\n\nPeter, 2026-07-31: "it seems that \'cam\' is the wrong command to send to the device, that is a query and returns the verbs. so it is NOT working... AND FUCKING TEST IT".\n\nHe is right. main.cpp:2097 — bare `cam` falls through to {"type":"err","msg":"cam snap|grab|info|read|diag"}. Every Take photo press since the button shipped has queued a no-op. It was carried over from the archived push.html era and never once sent and observed.\n\nDone means: a capture command goes out, the device replies with a cam JSON carrying a pid, and that image appears in the Camera page\'s stored list. Not "the string changed".'}
2026-07-31 10:35:25,278 50469 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Verb: `cam grab`, not `cam snap`. From main.cpp — snap publishes by REFERENCE (camera stays awake, RAK reads a 224-byte window per chunk over I2C); grab does capture -> bulk read to RAM -> CRC-verify against the camera\'s own CRC -> camera SLEEPS -> upload from RAM. For a battery unit mid-multi-minute-upload the sleeping camera is the whole point, and grab fails before anything goes on air if the RAM copy is bad.\n\nSend it bare, no pid override: camGrabBegin takes an optional pid (sscanf on the tail, -1 when absent) and the content-derived pid is what we want — same image gives the same pid, which is what makes resume idempotent.\n\nALSO RESTORE the test-image label I wrongly removed, this time cited to firmware not to services\' say-so:\n  main.cpp:489            TEST_IMAGE_PID = 1\n  include/test_image.h:22 TEST_IMAGE_LEN = 7156\n  main.cpp:521            camPidFromCrc excludes pid 0 and TEST_IMAGE_PID\npid 1 is RESERVED — a real capture can never be assigned it. I removed the label because the image "looked like a real photo"; it is a real photo used as embedded test data, so appearance was never the test.\n\nOPEN QUESTION for services (#58): on the UART build camGrabBegin is ASYNC — it returns immediately with reply[0]=0 and the JSON is emitted later from loop(). If their ledger does not correlate that deferred reply to the request id, our Command tab will render a false failure.\n\nTEST ON BENCH !8cee336b, not GARG. Private channel only, never Primary.'}
