2026-07-31 11:31:34,355 1251 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'PAUSED 2026-07-31 after Investigate. sleepCycle() (main.cpp ~3306-3434) touches 27 distinct\nexternals (handleCommand, handlePrivateApp, handleNodeInfo, 5 telemetry senders, evaluateAlarms,\nmtdb, mesh, PIR/push/chunk state, wdtFeed, agcProbe...) -- comparable to or larger than lib-cmd\'s\nalready-declared-too-large surface, and directly calls handleCommand (not extracted). mt-wake is\nalso supposed to be THE v2/v3 seam (a real interface both versions implement), but no v3 spec\nexists beyond one module-map sentence (awake_ms/seq/last_rx_id, device-initiated poll) -- building\n"the seam" without knowing v3\'s shape means guessing at an abstraction, not extracting one.\n\nFound and corrected a real error while investigating: told services (xsession #89) that REQ3\n(wake-cycle-observability, phase-boundary logging) was "not implemented" -- it IS, as lcPhase()/\nthe LC log lines, landed 2026-07-27 same day as the request (commit aa416e1, spec\ndocs/history/wake-lifecycle-logging.md). Corrected via xsession #92/93.\n\nConclusion: mt-wake, mt-cmd, and full mt-config field-ownership are one interlocked piece of work,\nnot three independent slices -- mt-cmd needs config ownership to be tractable, mt-wake needs\nmt-cmd to exist (calls handleCommand directly) AND needs a v3 spec that doesn\'t exist yet. Reported\nto Peter, offered to stop or find a narrower cut. Not implementing further without direction.'}
