2026-07-31 12:56:03,886 1041 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'B110 CONFIRMED, FIXED: every /idiot spec attachment today was BROKEN — the gate passed five times on a file mcpp could not read', 'description': 'PROCESS DEFECT, found 2026-07-31 while running the gate properly at Peter\'s instruction ("it ni more mistakes").\n\nmcpp\'s workspace root for this project is services/, NOT mt-alarm/. I attached every spec today as `services/docs/history/<task>.md`. plan_file_attach RETURNS SUCCESS for a path that does not resolve — it echoes "Attached `<path>` to task (id:N)" either way. plan_file_list is where the truth is: it prints "⚠ broken" and shows no content.\n\nI read the attach call\'s success line five times and never once called plan_file_list to check the effect. That is verifying the confirmation instead of the effect — the same error as reading a serial banner that printed a variable the firmware ignored, and the same error as reporting a soak result from a board that had stopped.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: /idiot Phase 0 gate item 3 is "plan_file_list — must show at least one spec file attached. If none, STOP." A BROKEN attachment satisfies that check. So the gate passed all day while the attached spec was unreadable, on:\n  778 image-send-catch-regression\n  779 progress-key-normalise\n  780 images-local-store-read\n  783 device-registry-removable\n  784 soak-ladder-4-tests\n\nFIXED: all five detached and re-attached as `docs/history/<task>.md`; plan_file_list now reports broken:false and renders the content for each. The spec FILES were always correct on disk and correctly hashed — this was record-keeping, not data loss, and the commits are unaffected.\n\nReopening the three completed tasks needed workflow.allow_reopen_completed, which was false in /usr/share/pac/dev/py/mcpp-plan/config.yaml. Peter confirmed reopening is permitted; I set it true and backed the file up first (config.yaml.bak-*). Flagging that I changed a shared config outside this repo.\n\nSTANDING RULE FROM THIS: after plan_file_attach, ALWAYS call plan_file_list and confirm broken:false. An attach that reports success is not an attach that works.'}
